{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'rvb-f71272a8111ac846|pose-assess-leaves-sealed-checkouts-alone|structural' .pose/review-bundles .pose/review-runs .pose/review-conclusions --glob '*.json'\"","aggregated_output":".pose/review-runs/rrn-2312702d8e59883f.json:106:  \"output\": \"decision: approved\\n\\nNo blocking defect found. Two existing low-priority follow-ups remain accepted: report provenance and dedicated end-to-end coverage for carried records.\\n\\nFocused CLI tests, the delivery-parser test, scoped `go vet`, and selected race tests passed. Explicit-range artifact reconciliation exited 0 with warnings only. Surface-check passed with one target, 236 results, and zero findings. Full validation relies on the supplied sealed evidence; I did not rerun commands that could modify checkout artifacts.\\n\\nApplied the review workflow and Backend Go, security, documentation-style, and delivery-evidence rules. Reviewed bundle `rvb-3540657ae0a94c2f`, digest `sha256:3540657ae0a94c2f7019d7642aa90f2738f393f23311d03089e32ba565262504`. HEAD remained `481d36dfd2ea673b5f5dc58a76d3e4213dac35bf`, and the working tree remained clean. No attestation was recorded.\\n\\n```pose-draft\\n{\\n  \\\"schema\\\": \\\"pose.review.draft/v1\\\",\\n  \\\"decision\\\": \\\"approved\\\",\\n  \\\"findings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"N62\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"low\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"follow-up\\\",\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": 1623,\\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"Existing F2 remains: validationSummaryOf includes carried checks in executed Commands and renders their previous outcomes and durations without their original head or time. A newly dated --carry --report therefore presents reused observations as commands executed by this run.\\\",\\n      \\\"action\\\": \\\"Complete spec follow-up F2: exclude carried checks from executed Commands and label reused results with carried_from and carried_generated_at.\\\",\\n      \\\"owner\\\": \\\"@pose-maintainers\\\",\\n      \\\"review_by\\\": \\\"2026-12-15\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"N63\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"low\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"follow-up\\\",\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\".pose/specs/2026-11-22-pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks.md\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": 264,\\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"Existing F1 remains: direct delivery-reader coverage verifies carried head and time, but no dedicated end-to-end fixture seals a bundle, verifies it and checks closeout over a carried record.\\\",\\n      \\\"action\\\": \\\"Complete spec follow-up F1 with a fixture proving seal, verify and closeout-check judge the carried check's original head.\\\",\\n      \\\"owner\\\": \\\"@pose-maintainers\\\",\\n      \\\"review_by\\\": \\\"2026-12-15\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"prior_findings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R12-N39\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"not-fixed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go:1623-1636 still includes carried commands and omits their origin; owned as F2 at spec line 265.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R13-N42\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"not-fixed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go:1623-1636 still includes carried commands and omits their origin; owned as F2 at spec line 265.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R14-N44\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"not-fixed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go:1623-1636 still includes carried commands and omits their origin; owned as F2 at spec line 265.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R16-N51\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"not-fixed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go:1623-1636 still includes carried commands and omits their origin; owned as F2 at spec line 265.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R17-N53\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"not-fixed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go:1623-1636 still includes carried commands and omits their origin; owned as F2 at spec line 265.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R17-N54\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"not-fixed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"Spec line 264 retains F1. go -C pose-mcp test ./internal/pose -run TestDeliveryValidationRunReadsTheCarriedHead -count=1 passed, but this test exercises parsing rather than seal, verify and closeout.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R18-N55\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"not-fixed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go:1623-1636 still includes carried commands and omits their origin; owned as F2 at spec line 265.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R18-N56\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"not-fixed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"Spec line 264 retains F1. The direct carried-head parser test passed; no dedicated carried-record seal/verify/closeout fixture was found in the reviewed tests.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R19-N60\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"not-fixed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go:1623-1636 still includes carried commands and omits their origin; owned as F2 at spec line 265.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R19-N61\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"not-fixed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"Spec line 264 retains F1. The direct carried-head parser test passed; the dedicated end-to-end consumer journey remains absent.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"sweep\\\": \\\"Reviewed the requested dec2e64c1395fafbf8e2a78171e5437c1720bbbf..481d36dfd2ea673b5f5dc58a76d3e4213dac35bf source diff, requirements R1-R10, decisions D1-D3, ADR, CLI help, English and Portuguese manuals and scaffold copies. Swept eligibility, unavailable bindings, cleanliness and reflog witnesses, cancellation, hidden index entries, submodule and alias handling, pinned metadata, changed-scope ownership and dependency widening, base completeness, chained provenance, failure accounting, dispatch, serialization, report projection and delivery consumption. Examined negative tests, the adversarial corpus and owned follow-ups. Focused CLI tests, direct delivery-parser test, scoped vet and selected race tests passed. Explicit-range artifact-check exited 0 with warning-only findings; surface-check exited 0 with zero findings. Full matrix evidence was supplied by the sealed bundle, not rerun. Final git status was clean. No blocker beyond the two accepted existing low-priority follow-ups was established.\\\",\\n  \\\"criteria\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assumption-integrity\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Examined R2 and the start/end full cleanliness predicate, movement witnesses and cancellation invalidation. Removing the unavailable-binding refusal leaves material_clean as the independent witness that the base validated its head; unclean or cancelled runs invalidate bindings. Focused tests passed. Correct selfContained declarations remain an explicit instance-owned assumption; arbitrary undeclared check inputs are outside the design's guarantee.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-concurrency\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/validate-concurrent-steps-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Carried entries are silent and bypass dispatch; aggregation reads their unchanged results. Traced cancellation finalization and lifecycle behavior. Focused Validate tests and selected race tests for cancellation, cancelled bases and submodule movement passed.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-contracts\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delivery-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Reviewed additive result fields and legacy fallback behavior. The delivery reader preserves run-level provenance for ordinary records and uses per-check provenance for carried records. The direct carried-head and time parser test passed.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-input-errors\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Focused tests passed for incompatible flags, unusable bases, malformed or unreadable metadata, path aliases, hidden index entries and cancellation. Invalid eligibility widens to full execution with a reason; incompatible invocation flags return exit 2.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-integration-impact\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N63\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The producer-to-delivery-reader boundary is directly tested. Dedicated carried-record seal, verify and closeout coverage remains the accepted low-priority F1 gap.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-observability\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N62\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Structured provenance, carry counts and fallback explanations are present, but the human report summary still loses carried provenance.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"compatibility\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delivery-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Examined CLI parsing, schema additions and the delivery consumer. Carry is opt-in, old records retain their meaning, and records without engine_version cannot become carry bases. The selfContained extension is specified and documented.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"correctness\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Independently passed go -C pose-mcp test ./internal/cli -run 'Carry|ChangedScope|Validate|Material|Cancellation' -count=1 and the direct delivery-parser test. Examined selection, chained origins, preserved failures, missing prior results and cleanliness invalidation. Full build and matrix coverage relies on the supplied sealed evidence.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"design-causality\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-c1f08e237f8792fa\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"D1 addresses the inability of partial changed-scope records to replace canonical evidence: a complete result retains each reused observation's actual origin. D2 conservatively rejects matrix or engine changes; D3 makes narrower root-change behavior explicit. The cheapest stale-reuse shortcut is representing an old observation as newly executed; carried_from and the delivery reader preserve its origin, and dirty-base tests reject invalid reuse. The corpus has no dedicated carried-record seal/closeout case; N63 records that assurance gap.\\\",\\n      \\\"mappings\\\": [\\n        {\\n          \\\"delta\\\": \\\"SD-253b523c\\\",\\n          \\\"basis\\\": \\\"D1\\\",\\n          \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"mapped\\\",\\n          \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The ADR records canonical carry and original-observation provenance required by D1, whose declared basis is R3, R4 and R7. It also records the D2 comparability boundary and D3 selfContained trade-off.\\\"\\n        }\\n      ]\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"documentation\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Compared help, both language manuals and scaffold changes with runtime eligibility and selection. All four manuals correctly state that an uncomputable binding alone does not refuse a clean base. The full English scaffold difference is the instance-only Contributor Mode section.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"operability\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N62\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Fallback reasons and selection explanations provide actionable context. Report provenance remains the accepted low-priority F2 defect.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"requirements\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N63\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Mapped R1-R10 to code and focused tests. Direct R7 provenance parsing passed, while the additional end-to-end delivery-consumer assurance remains the owned F1 follow-up.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"scope\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-c1f08e237f8792fa\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The runtime paths, tests, help, manuals and ADR implement the approved carry scope. The unavailable-binding change matches current R2. The delivery declaration identifies the production validate entrypoint, and surface-check found one target with zero findings.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"security\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/adversarial-corpus\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Examined revision confinement before Git calls, dependency containment, physical aliases, symlinks, hidden index flags, submodules and administrative exclusions. Focused negative tests passed. Carry retains the existing local validation-record trust boundary and introduces no external execution authority.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"solution-proportionality\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-c1f08e237f8792fa\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Reusing changed-scope selection and comparing the whole matrix and engine is smaller than per-command caching or arbitrary input hashing. Refusing every unavailable binding would disable legitimate reuse without strengthening the independent material_clean witness. This choice becomes insufficient when checks depend on undeclared inputs outside the selection model.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"tools\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"artifact-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks --strict --from dec2e64c1395fafbf8e2a78171e5437c1720bbbf --to 481d36dfd2ea673b5f5dc58a76d3e4213dac35bf --json\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Ran the required default command and an additional reconciliation pinned to the sealed range because automatic attribution selected a wider range. The explicit-range command exited 0; all 985 findings were warnings. Reviewed the requested source diff independently.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-design\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-c1f08e237f8792fa\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Did not rerun the writing assessment in the sealed checkout. Examined the spec, ADR and structural change directly and used the supplied sealed design evidence.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-discover\\\",\\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Skipped assessment writes under the no-change boundary. Inspected the component and independently ran focused tests; these are not represented as a new discovery assessment.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-integrate\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delivery-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Skipped the writing assessment. Traced the validation producer and delivery consumer and passed the direct carried-head parser test. Dedicated end-to-end coverage remains N63.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-tech-debt\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Skipped the writing assessment. Manually scanned the changed implementation for TODO, FIXME, stub and panic markers and checked the spec's owned follow-ups; no additional marker debt was established.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"closeout-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Completion requires POSE to record and verify this review conclusion. No attestation or closeout was recorded by this reviewer.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"review-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Deferred until POSE records this conclusion; it cannot validate an attestation that does not yet exist.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"suggest-review\\\",\\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Executed successfully and applied the selected Backend Go, security and documentation rules.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"surface-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delivery-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Executed pose surface-check --spec pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks --strict successfully: one target, 236 results and zero findings. Also cites sealed reachability:pose-mcp/go/delivery-reachability. Traced the declared validate.go entrypoint through dispatch, canonical serialization and delivery parsing; dedicated carried-record end-to-end assurance remains N63.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"validate\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Relies on the supplied sealed canonical run, including passing build, unit, integration and e2e evidence. Did not rerun the full writing matrix in the read-only checkout. Independently passed focused CLI tests, scoped vet, the delivery-parser test and selected race tests.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"validate\\\",\\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Uses the supplied sealed pose-mcp validation evidence. Independently passed focused component tests, scoped vet and selected race tests. The full --strict --module pose-mcp command was not rerun because it can write checkout artifacts.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\\n```\",\n.pose/review-runs/rrn-d94a50c1b4d6e56f.json:97:  \"brief_notes\": \"Review of spec pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit, implemented by Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic). The ADR `.pose/adr/2026-11-12-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-and-benefit.md` is Accepted; judge the implementation against it and the spec, not the decision itself.\\n\\nMechanism. Review policy schema 5 adds `milestone_review_required` / `roadmap_review_required` (`never|when-justified|always`), validated in `parseReviewPolicy` via `validateCloseoutReviewPolicyKeys` (closeout_review_policy.go). One evaluator `evaluateCloseoutReview` (closeout-review@1): canonical members `xref:\\u003cproject\\u003e/spec:\\u003cslug\\u003e` (aliases, verified redirects, federated resolver, unknown = diagnostic, never zero) and ADR associations (closeout_adr_associations.go: roadmap `adrs:`, ADR `roadmaps:`, local Markdown links both ways; malformed/missing/unreadable = unknown). `closeoutReviewGate` is the single entry for readers: receipt first, roadmap done before adoption = legacy (nil decision), else evaluate + `protectCloseoutDecision` (baseline policy at the change set base when the scope changes the review contract); exemption only when not required AND no review recorded on the scope (`scopeReviewRecorded`, unreadable counts as recorded). Consumers: `reviewCheck` (review_closeout.go, Required=false + ApprovalOrigin), `proportionalReviewVerification` (review_bundle.go; under adoption the legacy singleton inheritance and `unreviewed_milestones` are skipped), `getCloseoutState` (CloseRequired, receipt, terminal only with receipt, new diagnostics), `ReachedMilestones`/`RoadmapsReachedBy`/`roadmapReachedApartFrom` (roadmaps.go), `milestoneReachedObligations`, `ReviewPlan.CloseoutReview` (out of the digest), doctor (`CloseoutReviewsOwed`), setup and `pose adopt` (capability_catalog.go `closeoutReviewPolicyCatalogEntry`, `SetCloseoutReviewPolicy`; refs/transfer adopt/retire no longer lower schema 5). CLI close (cli/review_closeout.go `closeoutReceiptPreflight`, `publishCloseoutReceipt`): milestone and roadmap close publish an immutable receipt (closeout_receipt.go, ExpectAbsent publish, strict parse); a done roadmap without receipt is completed by a new close. `milestoneMember` now maps `spec:\\u003cslug\\u003e` to its slug (was `spec:spec:\\u003cslug\\u003e` in closeout state). Existing tests changed on purpose: catalog lists, schema after adopt (fresh install is now schema 5), progressive_review fixtures that force schema 2, and the previous-release compatibility test (a fresh install is refused by v7.4.0 by its schema, by ADR design; an updated legacy instance stays readable).\\n\\nPlease do an exhaustive sweep in this round and report ALL findings together, classified blocker vs follow-up. Inventory every entry point that answers \\\"is this aggregate scope approved / closed / reached\\\" (CLI close, closeout-check, review-check, review verify, review-plan, attention/obligations, reached, nextCloses, roadmap check, MCP closeout state, federated acceptance, doctor) and check each one reads the same gate, cannot launder a recorded rejection under `never`, cannot let `always` be weakened by inheritance or `unreviewed_milestones`, and never treats an unknown member/association as an exemption. Also check: receipts are never overwritten nor fabricated for history; `pose update` never adopts; no schema-5 downgrade path; the recovery path for a roadmap done without receipt cannot close a scope whose review is required and unapproved.\\n\\nKnown pre-existing state: `pose check --strict` reports 19 delivery-contract errors of other specs (runtime worktree, common-domain handoff, governance performance, bounded graph caches), identical line by line on the base commit 956153f1; they are follow-up F4, not this spec.\\n\\nRequired tools: run `pose artifact-check --spec pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit --strict` and `pose surface-check --spec pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit --strict`; declare each `passed` only after running it (evidence `command:\\u003cthe command\\u003e`, rationale quoting its result). The surface-check disposition must cite both an `integration:` and a `reachability:` sealed evidence id. Cite sealed `unit:`/`integration:` ids for criteria, never `SD-…` structural facts or requirement ids. Send each shell command alone in its own call (no pipes, `;`, `\\u0026\\u0026`, redirects). `validate` of a component with registered checks is `passed` with the sealed run's evidence; `review-check` and `closeout-check` are `deferred`. New findings have bare ids (F1, F2 …); follow-ups carry `action`, `owner`, `review_by`; only low-severity risks may be accepted.\\n\\nRound 2. Your round-1 draft (run rrn-7c2315202e585212) requested changes; the run itself was refused because `pose assess integrate` and `pose assess tech-debt` wrote `.pose/assessments/*` and `.pose/state/*` inside the sealed worktree. Do NOT run any `pose assess` command (nor `pose state`, `pose index` or anything else that writes under `.pose/`): dispose the assess-* tools from the sealed evidence, the plan and reading the code (`not-used` with a rationale, or `passed` citing a sealed id), never by running them. Dispositions of round 1, all fixed in code with tests unless noted (see the spec's \\\"### Review\\\"): R1-F1 `mandatoryHumanReview` in `currentCloseoutDecision`; R1-F2 a close with a receipt requires `state.Terminal`; R1-F3 recovery via `CloseoutRecoveryDecision` (exempt only when known, unprotected exemption impossible, no review on file) and refusal when a recorded review is not approved; R1-F4 `closeoutReceiptStands` (same canonical members, else error) and parse refuses `always` with required=false; R1-F5 close intent (`PublishCloseoutIntent`/`ClearCloseoutIntent`, `closeoutScopeHistorical` requires no receipt and no intent); R1-F6 gate before enabled/cutoff in `reviewCheck`; R1-F7 receipt-bound proof in `federatedSourceProof`; R1-F8 preflight and publication share `CurrentCloseoutDecision`; R1-F9 exemption refuses any non-lifecycle blocker, publication re-verifies decision, members, ADRs and state in the protected region (before the status for a roadmap, because the index lags after it); R1-F10 transferred members go through the resolver to their final identity, unknown without one; R1-F11 associated ADRs are read and validated; R1-F12 `ReviewPlan` returns the gate error; R1-F13 `roadmapGate` normalizes `spec:\\u003cslug\\u003e`; R1-F14 the gate requires `Known` and `reviewCheck` blocks unknown; R1-F15 doctor requires a fresh approval via `ReviewCheck`. List them in `prior_findings` as `R1-F1` … `R1-F15` and state whether each stands; again report every new finding in one pass, classified blocker vs follow-up.\\n\",\n.pose/review-runs/rrn-d94a50c1b4d6e56f.json:117:  \"output\": \"decision: changes-requested\\n\\nSix blockers remain: mandatory-human overlay bypass, incomplete receipt verification, incorrect historical classification, two ADR handling gaps, and inconsistent terminal-state projections. Two low-severity CLI issues are follow-ups.\\n\\nValidation: root `pose validate --strict` passed 213/213 checks. The separate module run timed out on its unit step; the successful root run subsequently covered that module. Focused policy tests, CLI publication testing under `-race`, and `go vet` passed. The repository remains unchanged.\\n\\nApplied the `pose-review` skill and Go, security, documentation-style, delivery-evidence, and knowledge-governance rules. No assessment writers or attestation commands were run.\\n\\n```pose-draft\\n{\\n  \\\"schema\\\": \\\"pose.review.draft/v1\\\",\\n  \\\"decision\\\": \\\"changes-requested\\\",\\n  \\\"findings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"F1\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"high\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"blocker\\\",\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_review_policy.go\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": 305,\\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"Mandatory-human protection ignores selected overlays. mandatoryHumanReview examines only reviewer_independence and the base profile, whereas ReviewPlan composes overlay independence at review_plan.go:350. With never, a matching mandatory-human overlay and no recorded aggregate review, the gate grants an exemption before that effective obligation is enforced. Resolve the effective human requirement, including protected baseline obligations, before granting an exemption.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"F2\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"high\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"blocker\\\",\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_review_policy.go\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": 359,\\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"Receipt verification checks only canonical member identities and never verifies SubjectDigest or the closed semantic inputs. After an exempt close, changing a milestone exit gate while retaining its member names leaves the receipt standing; repeated close returns before rerunning roadmapGate. Conversely, this function evaluates the current policy, so changing never to when-justified can invalidate an unchanged historical receipt through newly inspected unresolved ADR inputs. Verify semantic integrity under the recorded closeout contract while preserving later policy independence.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"F3\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"high\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"blocker\\\",\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_review_policy.go\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": 415,\\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"Historical classification is inferred from parent roadmap status and absent receipt/intent rather than positive prior terminal evidence. Marking an adopted roadmap done without an intent re-enables legacy singleton inheritance despite always. In the opposite direction, a milestone with its own valid sealed approval before adoption is reopened when its parent roadmap remains active, because it now owes a receipt. Preserve positively established historical closures without treating status alone as proof of pre-adoption closure.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"F4\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"medium\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"blocker\\\",\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_review_policy.go\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": 195,\\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"A when-justified roadmap with at most one distinct member returns Known=true and Required=false before resolving any ADR associations. An explicit missing or malformed adrs declaration, or an unreadable ADR inventory, therefore grants an exemption. The spec permits skipping ADR inventory for never and always, but requires unknown association inputs to block when-justified exemptions.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"F5\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"medium\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"blocker\\\",\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_adr_associations.go\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": 140,\\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"The ADR inventory can silently omit unresolved inputs. README.md is skipped even when explicitly associated, so its contents, size and backward declaration are never validated. At line 143, regularADR failures are also ignored unless a forward association already identified that filename; an unreadable or dangling candidate that might contain a backlink consequently becomes absence. Unknown inventory entries must produce diagnostics rather than establish an exemption.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"F6\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"medium\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"blocker\\\",\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_review_policy.go\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": 478,\\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"Doctor and reached/attention projections bypass terminal verification. Doctor skips every done roadmap and every scope with any parseable receipt, including an interrupted done roadmap still owing review or a receipt whose recorded review no longer stands. ReachedMilestones, roadmapReachedApartFrom and milestoneReachedObligations likewise use receipt presence without checking its standing. A later rejection or composition change can make closeout-check nonterminal while doctor reports no review owed and attention hides the scope. These readers must project the same applicable gate.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"F7\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"low\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"follow-up\\\",\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/adopt.go\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": 101,\\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"The --request branch returns before validating closeoutPairGiven. A command combining --request with either new closeout flag silently ignores the flags, even for another capability or an incomplete pair, instead of rejecting the combination.\\\",\\n      \\\"action\\\": \\\"Reject closeout policy flags with --request and --list before entering their early-return branches; add CLI argument coverage.\\\",\\n      \\\"owner\\\": \\\"@pose-maintainers\\\",\\n      \\\"review_by\\\": \\\"2026-12-13\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"F8\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"low\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"follow-up\\\",\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/adopt.go\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": 310,\\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"Fresh installation advertises pose adopt closeout-review-policy --off --apply as the way to turn this capability off, although its RetireRefusal deliberately rejects that command. The installation output gives an unusable remediation instruction.\\\",\\n      \\\"action\\\": \\\"Render the closeout capability's supported pair-change command instead of the generic --off instruction.\\\",\\n      \\\"owner\\\": \\\"@pose-maintainers\\\",\\n      \\\"review_by\\\": \\\"2026-12-13\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"prior_findings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R1-F1\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"partial\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"closeout_review_policy.go:305 protects policy/base-profile human requirements, but selected overlay requirements remain bypassable; F1.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R1-F2\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout.go:2457 requires state.Terminal for receipt-backed repeated close; TestCloseoutReviewPolicyRepeatedCloseVerifiesTheTerminalContract passed in the focused run.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R1-F3\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout.go:2476 uses CloseoutRecoveryDecision and refuses required-unapproved or recorded-unapproved recovery.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R1-F4\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"partial\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"closeout_review_policy.go:367 now compares canonical members and closeout_receipt.go:114 rejects always/not-required, but semantic receipt integrity remains incomplete; F2.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R1-F5\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"partial\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout.go:2117 records an intent before status publication, fixing engine-interruption handling. Historical classification still lacks positive historical proof; F3.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R1-F6\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_closeout.go:1526 evaluates the adopted gate before enabled/cutoff shortcuts; focused protection tests passed.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R1-F7\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/federated_acceptance.go:701 supplies receipt-bound proof after terminal source verification; TestCloseoutReviewPolicyFederatedReceiptProof passed.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R1-F8\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout.go:2530 rechecks CurrentCloseoutDecision before publication, using the same protected producer as preflight.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R1-F9\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_closeout.go:2503 rejects non-lifecycle blockers; verifyCloseoutPublication rechecks decision, members, associations and state.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R1-F10\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_review_policy.go:265 follows transferred members through the resolver to final identity and refuses resolution without a bound resolver.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R1-F11\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"partial\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_adr_associations.go:149 validates ordinary associated ADRs, but README and unresolved inventory entries still escape complete validation; F5.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R1-F12\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_plan.go:407 propagates gate errors; TestCloseoutReviewPolicyReceiptIntegrity passed.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R1-F13\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/surface_check.go:406 normalizes typed local spec members; TestCloseoutReviewPolicyTypedLocalMemberCloses passed.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R1-F14\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"partial\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_review_policy.go:353 requires Known for exemption, but the small-roadmap branch incorrectly establishes Known without resolving associations; F4.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R1-F15\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"partial\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_review_policy.go:504 requires a fresh approval for scopes it examines, but earlier status/receipt shortcuts hide nonterminal scopes; F6.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"sweep\\\": \\\"Reviewed R1-R7, D1-D2, the accepted ADR, changed implementation/tests/schemas/docs/templates, adoption and schema transitions, canonical members, ADR inventory, receipts and intents, CLI close/recovery/repetition, closeout-check, review-check, review verification, review-plan, attention/obligations, reached/nextCloses, roadmap check, MCP state, federated acceptance and doctor. Checked the adversarial corpus inventory: its closeout-plan judgment case does not cover the overlay, history-classification or receipt semantic-drift bypasses reported here. Ran artifact-check, surface-check, suggest review, focused policy tests, CLI publication testing under race detection, go vet, root validation and module validation. Root validation passed 213/213; the separate module run had 209 passes and a 600-second unit timeout. Final git status was clean. No repository changes or attestation were made.\\\",\\n  \\\"criteria\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assumption-integrity\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Verified authority at the requested head and distinguished sealed evidence, independently executed checks and code-derived findings. Historical closure, complete ADR absence and effective human requirements are not assumed proven merely by status, receipt presence or base-profile inspection. The module timeout is disclosed separately from the successful root run. Only F7/F8 are accepted low-severity follow-ups.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-concurrency\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/writer-coordination-and-atomic-publication-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Inspected existing write guards, intent-before-status ordering, ExpectAbsent receipt publication and protected rechecks. The focused CLI publication test passed under -race; its pose-package invocation had no matching test. No new goroutine lifecycle was introduced.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-contracts\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"F3\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Schema migration is explicit, but historical aggregate-state compatibility is not preserved correctly.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-input-errors\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"F4\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Unresolved association inputs can be returned as a known exemption.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-integration-impact\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"F6\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Doctor, reached and attention do not consistently consume the terminal gate used by closeout state.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-observability\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"F6\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The diagnostic projection can report no review owed while authoritative closeout verification is nonterminal.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"compatibility\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"F3\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Existing sealed milestone closures under active roadmaps can reopen, while status-only history can weaken adopted always.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"correctness\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"F2\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"A receipt can survive semantic changes that its original close never judged.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"design-causality\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-a8489a97539b30e7\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"D1 separates aggregate review cost from mandatory explicit close; D2 supplies explicit adoption, canonical association inputs and a persistent receipt. A common domain evaluator directly addresses inconsistent thresholds across transports. The implementation defects are failures to complete those selected boundaries, rather than evidence against the accepted decision.\\\",\\n      \\\"mappings\\\": [\\n        {\\n          \\\"delta\\\": \\\"SD-607ff681\\\",\\n          \\\"basis\\\": \\\"D2\\\",\\n          \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"mapped\\\",\\n          \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The roadmap template adds the planned flat adrs association syntax needed by R3.\\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"delta\\\": \\\"SD-ec2d86f4\\\",\\n          \\\"basis\\\": \\\"D1\\\",\\n          \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"mapped\\\",\\n          \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The new accepted ADR records the policy semantics, deterministic thresholds, explicit close and historical compatibility required by R1.\\\"\\n        }\\n      ]\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"documentation\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"F8\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The manuals/templates describe the intended pair and receipt contract, but installation output recommends an unsupported rollback command.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"operability\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"F6\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Operators can lose the obligation and next-action signal for a scope whose receipt or review no longer stands.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"requirements\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"F1\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"R5's non-waivable authority protection is incomplete; F2-F6 additionally leave R3, R4, R6 and R7 unsatisfied despite passing registered checks.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"scope\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-a8489a97539b30e7\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The feature-owned changes implement the planned policy pair, evaluator, associations, receipt, adoption/setup, projections and distributed documentation. No unrelated feature expansion is needed to address the findings.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"security\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"F1\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"An aggregate exemption can bypass a selected mandatory-human authority requirement. Path containment and immutable publication alone do not repair that authority gap.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"solution-proportionality\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-a8489a97539b30e7\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The pair of enums, existing adopt/setup surface, one evaluator and separate receipt are proportionate to the three requested modes and explicit-close requirement. A boolean cannot express when-justified, and an ephemeral exemption cannot establish explicit closure. Avoiding global ADR identities and remote backlink discovery limits speculative scope. A future requirement for remote association discovery would invalidate the present local-inventory boundary and require another design decision.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"tools\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"artifact-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit --strict\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Executed; exit 0. Output included artifact.claims=39, artifact.observed=54 and artifact.findings=926, with warnings. Its attribution query reported cs-265abd4131d5 and head e94ae458 rather than the sealed brief's change set; this command result is not treated as proof that those ranges are identical.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-design\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-a8489a97539b30e7\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Used the sealed structural assessment and independently mapped both listed deltas to D1/D2. Did not rerun an assessment writer.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-discover\\\",\\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Discovery persists assessment/state artifacts. The review boundary forbids those writes; component scope was established from the sealed plan and source.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-integrate\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Did not run the assessment writer. Inspected CLI/MCP/federation consumers directly and used sealed integration evidence plus the successful root validation; F6 records a remaining integration divergence.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-tech-debt\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Did not run the assessment writer inside the sealed checkout. Reviewed the changed sources and recorded concrete defects here without staging repository feedback or follow-up artifacts.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"closeout-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Completion verification depends on the review attestation, which this independent run is explicitly forbidden to record.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"review-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The review's completion gate cannot establish this review's approval before POSE records its verified conclusion.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"suggest-review\\\",\\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Executed successfully; selected backend-go, security and documentation-style, with review workflow and implementation validation evidence.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"surface-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Executed pose surface-check --spec pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit --strict; exit 0, surface.targets=1, surface.results=213, surface.findings=0. Composition evidence: integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration. Reachability evidence: reachability:pose-mcp/go/spec-surface-reachability. Passing composition does not resolve the reported semantic defects.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"validate\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Executed pose validate --strict; exit 0, 213 step(s), 213 pass, Result: SUCCESS. The run included pose-mcp build, unit and registered integrations.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"validate\\\",\\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Executed pose validate --strict --module pose-mcp: 209 passes and one unit-step timeout after 600 seconds, exit 1. The subsequent successful root validation covered the same module, including its unit step and all required checks. This passed disposition rests on that successful module coverage and the sealed integration evidence, not on misclassifying the timed-out invocation.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\\n```\",\n.pose/review-runs/rrn-b07ee93779a65e40.json:106:  \"output\": \"decision: changes-requested\\n\\nThree prior findings are fixed; **R3-N9 and R3-N10 remain partial**. Four blockers remain:\\n\\n- **N11 — high:** [validate_scope.go:172](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-1501693732/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go:172). The helper returns the first matching dependency before discovered dependencies are filtered. With modules `a`, `a/nested`, and `b`, `b.dependsOn: [\\\"a\\\", \\\".\\\"]`, and a change inside `a/nested`, the discovered `a` match masks the eligible root dependency. `b` can be carried; reversing dependency order selects it. Evaluate every eligible match.\\n- **N12 — high:** [validate.go:1431](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-1501693732/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go:1431). A material-changing HEAD transition clears `material_clean` but leaves the original material bindings intact. Delivery parsing ignores `material_clean`; after restoring the earlier source, those bindings can make the incorrectly attributed pass current again. Invalidate unverifiable bindings before publication.\\n- **N13 — medium:** [validate_carry.go:110](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-1501693732/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry.go:110). `EvalSymlinks` does not identify case aliases on case-insensitive Unix filesystems. An override `A` can alias discovered module `a`, pass this guard, and retain results when `a` changes. Check physical directory identity or conservatively refuse alias reuse.\\n- **N14 — high:** [validate.go:1167](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-1501693732/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go:1167). HEAD is captured after carry selection. If selection finishes at H0 and HEAD advances to H1 before capture, old results can receive H1 provenance while the final head comparison passes. Capture and pin the subject before planning.\\n\\nThese are code-inspection findings. Additional reproduction fixtures, including a case-insensitive filesystem probe, were unavailable because scratch storage is read-only.\\n\\nFocused and broader tests, race tests, vet, and strict artifact-check passed. Both required matrix runs failed on sandbox write restrictions. The sealed canonical record has 236 passes; fresh required-tool validation remains unmet.\\n\\nApplied the review workflow, backend-go, security, documentation-style and delivery-evidence rules. No repository changes or attestation were made.\\n\\n```pose-draft\\n{\\n  \\\"schema\\\": \\\"pose.review.draft/v1\\\",\\n  \\\"decision\\\": \\\"changes-requested\\\",\\n  \\\"findings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"N11\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"high\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"blocker\\\",\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": 172,\\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"declaredDependencyHit returns the first matching dependency before the caller filters discovered modules, masking later eligible matches. With discovered a, a/nested and b, no root module, and b.dependsOn=['a','.'], a change inside a/nested selects the nested owner; the first hit a is discarded, the root dependency is never examined, and transitive widening cannot select b. Reversing dependency order changes selection. Evaluate all eligible dependency intersections and add an order-independence regression.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"N12\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"high\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"blocker\\\",\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": 1431,\\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"A material-changing HEAD transition clears material_clean but does not invalidate MaterialProvenance when the ending worktree is clean. ParseDeliveryValidationRun ignores material_clean, and deliveryEvidenceCurrent accepts matching material bindings. A pass observed after a concurrent committed fix can retain bindings for the earlier failing source and become current again after that source is restored. Invalidate bindings whose observed material is unverifiable and extend the regression through delivery parsing and freshness.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"N13\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"medium\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"blocker\\\",\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry.go\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": 110,\\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"The alias guard detects symlink spelling changes but not case aliases on case-insensitive Unix filesystems. EvalSymlinks preserves ordinary component spelling there, so moduleOverrides['A'] can alias discovered module a while passing the guard. Changes recorded under a select only a, leaving an alias-specific check carried. Detect shared physical directory identity or conservatively refuse reuse for aliases; add a conditional case-insensitive-filesystem regression.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"N14\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"high\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"blocker\\\",\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": 1167,\\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"run.GitHead is captured after planCarry has selected checks using symbolic HEAD. If selection finishes at H0 and a concurrent commit advances HEAD to H1 before this capture, carried H0 outcomes receive H1 provenance and material_clean can remain true because the ending head also equals H1. Capture the subject before planning, use its immutable OID consistently, and invalidate evidence on drift. Add a synchronized planning-to-capture regression.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"prior_findings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R2-N5\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"TestCarryDeletedDependencySelectsItsDependents and TestCarryDeletedNestedDependencySelectsItsDependents passed. validate_scope.go:168-176 applies dependency-path handling independently of owner matching for undiscovered dependencies.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R3-N7\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"validate_scope.go:168-174 independently selects descendant modules and consumers of undiscovered dependency paths. TestCarryDeletedNestedDependencySelectsItsDependents and TestChangedScopeGitlinkAboveADependencySelectsItsDependents passed.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R3-N8\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"validate_scope.go:221 explicitly matches dependency '.'. TestCarryRootDependencyIsChangedByRootFiles passed. N11 identifies a separate multiple-match ordering defect.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R3-N9\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"partial\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"TestCarryRefusesModulesReachedThroughASymlink passed and validate_carry.go:109-113 refuses symlink-reached modules. Case aliases remain undetected on case-insensitive Unix filesystems; see N13. Inspected the local Go filepath Unix implementation, which preserves non-symlink component spelling.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R3-N10\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"partial\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"TestValidateHeadMovingDuringTheRunIsNotClean passed and validate.go:1430 clears material_clean for a different ending head. The producer still retains old material bindings and captures the subject after planning; see N12 and N14.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"sweep\\\": \\\"Reviewed the rewritten selector and complete carry flow against R1-R10 and D1-D3, including all carried-forward findings, overlapping dependency order, nested and removed modules, root dependencies, gitlinks/submodule status handling, symlink and conditional case aliases, manifestless overrides, stack/check identity changes, criticality widening, chained origins, base eligibility, administrative exclusions, dispatch/cancellation, canonical publication guards, material provenance consumers, legacy parsing, manuals and scaffold copies. Focused and broader validation-related tests, focused race tests and vet passed. New scenarios were established by code inspection; writable scratch and case-insensitive runtime fixtures were unavailable. No separate torn-write defect was established in atomic canonical publication. Repository remained unchanged.\\\",\\n  \\\"criteria\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assumption-integrity\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N14\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Verified the documented declaration assumptions and new guards. The implementation still assumes selection and recorded provenance observed the same HEAD, but captures that identity only after planning.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-concurrency\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N14\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Focused race tests passed and canonical publication remains guarded and atomic, but concurrent HEAD movement between selection and capture can produce falsely current carried evidence.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-contracts\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delivery-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Inspected additive JSON fields, flag restrictions, legacy parsing and per-check delivery origins. Existing records retain their interpretation.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-input-errors\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Verified incompatible-flag refusals, revision confinement, malformed-base fallback, metadata decoding errors and symlink fallback. Existing negative fixtures passed.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-integration-impact\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N12\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The producer clears material_clean while retaining bindings that the delivery parser and freshness consumer continue to accept independently of that flag.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-observability\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Inspected bounded result output, metadata errors, fallback reasons, selected-module explanations, carried counts and original observation fields. Existing diagnostic fixtures passed.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"compatibility\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Reviewed additive CLI/file fields, explicit flag combinations, old-base rejection and legacy delivery fallback. No MCP signature changed.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"correctness\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N11\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Existing regressions pass, but equivalent dependency lists can select different checks solely because their entries are ordered differently.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"design-causality\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N11\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Module reuse addresses repeated full execution, but D1 requires complete invalidation of declared inputs. First-match filtering can omit an eligible dependency even under the current R6 rules.\\\",\\n      \\\"mappings\\\": [\\n        {\\n          \\\"delta\\\": \\\"SD-a9e60b2a\\\",\\n          \\\"basis\\\": \\\"D1\\\",\\n          \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"mapped\\\",\\n          \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The ADR records original-observation reuse and the unchanged-input premise; D2 and D3 provide engine/matrix comparison and self-containment policy.\\\"\\n        }\\n      ]\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"documentation\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/distributed-instructions-parity-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Compared manuals, translations, help, embedded copies, spec and ADR. They consistently describe intended carry behavior and new guards. The English embedded difference is the instance-specific Contributor Mode section.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"operability\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Inspected actionable canonical-path refusals, metadata errors, symlink fallback and explain output. Existing diagnostic tests passed.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"requirements\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N11\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"R6 requires eligible declared dependency intersections to select consumers. A preceding discovered match can suppress a later eligible match. N14 also undermines the stable-subject requirement of R2.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"scope\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-521f324dfd05f797\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Compared implementation, tests, governance and documentation changes against the spec's affected areas and artifact declarations. Changes remain within the approved carry feature.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"security\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N12\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Revision and output-path confinement remain intact, but unverifiable observations can retain material bindings that later satisfy delivery freshness.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"solution-proportionality\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-521f324dfd05f797\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Reusing module selection and whole-matrix comparison remains smaller than per-check manifests or output caching. Evaluating all eligible dependency matches and pinning the subject are sufficient corrections within this design. The approach is invalid if dependency closure, filesystem identity or provenance cannot be established.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"tools\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"artifact-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks --strict\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Exited 0 with 15 claims, 20 observations and 985 reported findings. Trailer head 87515826 differs from the sealed checkout only in delivery-integrity.json, generation.json and spec-graph.json.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-design\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Used supplied sealed structural evidence and inspected the ADR and diff. Writable scratch for isolated assessment execution was unavailable.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-discover\\\",\\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Assessment publication would change files. Scratch creation failed with a read-only filesystem error.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-integrate\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Writable scratch was unavailable for this publishing assessment. Inspected producer, parser and material-freshness consumers directly.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-tech-debt\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Writable scratch was unavailable for this publishing assessment; no assessment output was written into the sealed checkout.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"closeout-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Completion-only tool requires the recorded review conclusion. No attestation was recorded.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"review-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Completion-only tool requires the recorded review conclusion. No attestation was recorded.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"suggest-review\\\",\\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Resolved and consulted backend-go, security and documentation-style rules; additionally applied delivery-evidence and consumed relevant knowledge.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"validate\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"failed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"This ref identifies the supplied sealed canonical pass, not a fresh local pass. Ran pose validate --strict; it exited 1 with 236 failures because child checks could not create build directories or write caches. The committed canonical record reports 236 passes.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"validate\\\",\\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"failed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"This ref identifies the supplied sealed canonical pass, not a fresh local pass. Ran pose validate --strict --module pose-mcp; it exited 1 with 233 failures caused by sandbox write restrictions. Independent focused and broader tests, focused race tests and vet passed.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\\n```\",\n.pose/review-runs/rrn-0dd98c4aab8b5918.json:108:  \"output\": \"decision: changes-requested\\n\\n**F1 — high, blocker:** [validate_carry.go:91](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-501794006/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry.go:91) checks the current worktree’s cleanliness but never establishes that the base validated its recorded commit.\\n\\nA full validation can pass against an uncommitted fix while recording the original `git_head` and unavailable material provenance. Restore the original failing source, retain the canonical result, then run `--carry`: selection sees no source changes and carries the pass. The new run assigns current material provenance to that result. This breaks D1’s premise and can turn invalid evidence into current evidence.\\n\\nReject bases whose validated material cannot be established, and cover this sequence with a regression test. This finding follows from code inspection; the additional reproduction fixture was blocked by unavailable writable scratch space.\\n\\nThe existing carry and delivery-parser fixtures passed, and `go vet ./...` passed. Full validation did not complete. `artifact-check` reported a range ending at `6be3a6f…`, inconsistent with the requested `883eb1e…`; I stopped verification and cancelled the remaining checks. The draft below therefore **cannot satisfy the required-tool gate**.\\n\\nRules applied: pose-review workflow, backend-go, security, documentation-style and delivery-evidence. No attestation was recorded.\\n\\nThe assessment commands unexpectedly modified four derived files: `.pose/assessments/{integrations,technical-debt}.md` and `.pose/state/{integrations,technical-debt}.json`. Restoration was rejected by the read-only sandbox; those modifications remain. No implementation files were changed.\\n\\n```pose-draft\\n{\\n  \\\"schema\\\": \\\"pose.review.draft/v1\\\",\\n  \\\"decision\\\": \\\"changes-requested\\\",\\n  \\\"findings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"F1\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"high\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"blocker\\\",\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry.go\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": 91,\\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"Carry eligibility establishes only current worktree cleanliness, not that the base validated its recorded HEAD. A pass produced against an uncommitted fix can be carried after restoring failing committed source; the new run then replaces unavailable base provenance with current material provenance. Reject unverifiable base material and add a dirty-base regression fixture.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"criteria\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assumption-integrity\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"F1\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Explicit selfContained declarations are a documented instance responsibility. The separate assumption that base results observed base.git_head is unverified and unsafe for dirty baseline runs.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-concurrency\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/validate-concurrent-steps-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Inspected dispatcher exclusion of silent carried entries, serial result accounting and existing cancellation handling. Carried entries do not execute or require worker completion channels.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-contracts\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delivery-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Inspected additive result fields, canonical-output flag restrictions and legacy parser fallback. Existing records retain their parsing behavior.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-input-errors\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Inspected incompatible flag refusals, revision confinement and conservative fallback paths; existing carry refusal fixtures passed.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-integration-impact\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"F1\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Delivery parsing combines carried outcomes with newly computed run-level provenance without establishing the base's validated material.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-observability\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Fallback reasons, selected-module reasons, carry origins and carried outcomes remain available in structured results.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"compatibility\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Inspected optional JSON fields, unchanged schema number, legacy delivery parsing and explicit --carry restrictions. The CLI and file changes are additive.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"correctness\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"F1\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"design-causality\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"F1\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Changed-scope reuse and whole-matrix engine comparison address repeated execution, but D1 also requires a trustworthy initial observation. Current eligibility does not establish that prerequisite.\\\",\\n      \\\"mappings\\\": [\\n        {\\n          \\\"delta\\\": \\\"SD-a9e60b2a\\\",\\n          \\\"basis\\\": \\\"D1\\\",\\n          \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"mapped\\\",\\n          \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The ADR defines reuse with original observation heads and explains why current material binding depends on unchanged carried inputs; D2 and D3 supply comparison and selection policy.\\\"\\n        }\\n      ]\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"documentation\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/distributed-instructions-parity-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Inspected English and Portuguese manual changes, embedded copies and CLI help. They describe implemented flags, eligibility, origins and explicit self-containment risk.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"operability\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Inspected refusal messages, full-run fallback explanations and --explain selection output. Existing diagnostic paths provide actionable context.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"requirements\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"F1\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The fixtures cover principal R1-R10 behaviors, but the constraints and D1 soundness premise fail when the base observed dirty material.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"scope\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-72d43b18e7c9f6a1\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Compared the listed implementation, tests, ADR and documentation against the spec artifacts and affected areas. Changes remain within the approved carry feature.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"security\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"F1\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Revision option confinement is preserved, but the evidence authority boundary permits an unverified base observation to receive fresh material provenance.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"solution-proportionality\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-72d43b18e7c9f6a1\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Reusing module selection and comparing the whole matrix is smaller than introducing per-check input manifests or command-output caching. It avoids speculative infrastructure. The choice remains appropriate only when baseline observations and declared module inputs are trustworthy; F1 identifies a missing baseline guard.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"tools\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"artifact-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"failed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks --strict\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Output evaluated a range ending at 6be3a6f7009c1d782198c74a24549f8ec41423df rather than the requested 883eb1ef143c3897e159011c19e8403eb1f022cf. Verification was stopped and the command cancelled.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-design\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-72d43b18e7c9f6a1\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Ran the requested design assessment; its structural digest and ADR delta match the sealed structure evidence.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-discover\\\",\\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Avoided further assessment publication after observing derived report mutations during a read-only review.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-integrate\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:pose assess integrate\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Completed; reported three unobserved HTTP consumers. These do not identify a defect introduced by this change.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-tech-debt\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"failed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:pose assess tech-debt\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Command completed but explicitly reported an incomplete scan because two existing spec sources were invalid. No complete debt-assurance claim is made.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"closeout-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Completion-only tool requires the recorded review conclusion; no attestation was authorized or recorded here.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"review-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Completion-only tool requires the recorded review conclusion; no attestation was authorized or recorded here.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"suggest-review\\\",\\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Resolved backend-go, security and documentation-style rules and consulted them.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"validate\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"failed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:pose validate --strict\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Started, then cancelled after the validation-binding mismatch was observed. Exited 1 with cancelled checks; no new passing sealed evidence was produced.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"validate\\\",\\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"failed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:pose validate --strict --module pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Started, then cancelled after the validation-binding mismatch was observed. Exited 1 with cancelled checks; no new passing sealed evidence was produced.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\\n```\",\n.pose/review-bundles/rvb-ff930370e6fde91f.json:356:          \"rationale\": \"observe bounded structural deltas on the canonical review subject\",\n.pose/review-bundles/rvb-ff930370e6fde91f.json:1935:      \"structural-causality\"\n.pose/review-bundles/rvb-56cdd4150522a191.json:444:          \"rationale\": \"observe bounded structural deltas on the canonical review subject\",\n.pose/review-bundles/rvb-56cdd4150522a191.json:995:      \"structural-causality\"\n.pose/review-runs/rrn-28e79db88aa1de66.json:106:  \"output\": \"decision: approved\\n\\nNo remaining defects found. Both prior findings are fixed under D2. The focused Go tests, artifact checks, and surface check passed. Broader validation uses the sealed evidence. The repository remains unchanged.\\n\\nApplied rules: backend-go, security, documentation-style, and delivery-evidence.\\n\\n```pose-draft\\n{\\n  \\\"schema\\\": \\\"pose.review.draft/v1\\\",\\n  \\\"decision\\\": \\\"approved\\\",\\n  \\\"findings\\\": [],\\n  \\\"prior_findings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R1-F1\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/strict_json_test.go:50-117 replaces the syntactic predicate with the D2 inventory. Decode(new(T)) and More() no longer qualify an unlisted reader. Independently ran TestStrictJSONReadersRequireTheEnd successfully and verified all 16 inventory explanations against their implementations.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R2-N1\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/strict_json_test.go:90-105 no longer accepts io.EOF comparisons or ignored errors.Is results as proof of an end check. Only the helper or an explicit reviewed inventory entry qualifies. The focused regression command passed.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"sweep\\\": \\\"Reviewed the complete specified change range, R1/R2 and D1/D2, helper behavior, all three production consumers and their error-before-effect ordering, regression tests, validation-matrix registration, and every one of the 16 inventory entries. Searched production Go sources for DisallowUnknownFields, checked the MCP RawMessage transport boundary, and examined existing second-decode, Token and json.Unmarshal end checks. Ran the focused integration command, artifact-check in default and explicitly bounded forms, surface-check, context resolution and suggest-review. Inspected sealed validation evidence and confirmed the final worktree is clean.\\\",\\n  \\\"criteria\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assumption-integrity\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/strict-json-readers-require-the-end-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Verified the 16 inventory explanations against code, including MCP arguments extracted as one RawMessage by callToolCtx. Broader validation is reused sealed evidence rather than a new full-suite execution. D2 explicitly accepts human review of inventory explanations; no unresolved material assumption remains for this change.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-concurrency\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The helper creates a local decoder over supplied bytes. No shared state, goroutine, cancellation or lifecycle mechanism is introduced.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-contracts\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/strict-json-readers-require-the-end-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Valid input contracts remain unchanged; rejecting trailing content is the specified correction. Positive controls and negative consumer regressions pass.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-input-errors\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/strict-json-readers-require-the-end-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The helper rejects unknown fields, malformed input and trailing values or garbage. Consumers return errors before recording evidence, fulfilling requests or running hooks.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-integration-impact\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/strict-json-readers-require-the-end-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Verified production wiring through release record, action fulfil and hookRunner. The registered integration command independently passed.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-observability\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/strict-json-readers-require-the-end-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Trailing-content errors are bounded and do not echo the trailing payload. Hook errors retain the policy path; action fulfil preserves its existing envelope diagnostic.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"compatibility\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/strict-json-readers-require-the-end-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Examined the three decoder replacements and existing validation paths. Valid JSON and surrounding whitespace retain their behavior; malformed suffixes are intentionally rejected. CLI flags, schemas and MCP contracts are unchanged.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"correctness\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/strict-json-readers-require-the-end-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Independently reran the exact registered focused command successfully. The first decode validates the value and the subsequent Token call must return EOF, rejecting both additional values and malformed suffixes.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"design-causality\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-c926a8f43e21c447\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"D1 centralizes the missing end check in DecodeStrictJSON and routes the three affected readers through it. D2 removes the unsound syntactic inference and makes R2 an explicit inventory obligation. Checked the helper, inventory and production composition against those decisions. No structural delta facts were enumerated in the brief.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"documentation\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/strict-json-readers-require-the-end-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The current R2 wording, D2, known-gap statement, guard comments and matrix command describe the implemented inventory design. No user-facing command or scaffold change is required.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"operability\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/strict-json-readers-require-the-end-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Reviewed refusal diagnostics and exit paths. Users receive a trailing-content or invalid-envelope error before effects; removing the suffix produces the existing valid-input behavior.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"requirements\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/strict-json-readers-require-the-end-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"R1 is covered by helper negatives and all three consumer regressions, with code inspection confirming effects occur after validation. R2 is covered by the passing source inventory guard and independent inspection of every exception.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"scope\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/strict-json-readers-require-the-end-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The implementation is limited to the shared decoder, three consumers, regression coverage and permanent validation registration. Existing strict readers and the deliberately permissive review-policy reader retain their behavior.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"security\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/strict-json-readers-require-the-end-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Malformed evidence, envelopes and hook policies are rejected before authority-bearing effects. Existing path confinement and downstream authorization remain intact. No dependencies, credentials or new execution capability are introduced.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"solution-proportionality\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-c926a8f43e21c447\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Compared the helper and reviewed inventory with three duplicated fixes and a semantic source analyzer. The chosen design is small and avoids speculative analysis machinery. Adding an arbitrary inventory explanation is the cheapest formal bypass; D2 explicitly assigns its truth to review, and all current entries were checked. This choice would need revisiting if automatic proof of exception semantics became a requirement.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"tools\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"artifact-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-strict-json-readers-require-the-end --strict\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Exited 0 with repository-wide orphan provenance warnings. Also ran the strict JSON form with explicit --from 6ea5394b3788f84b67a51fab99f5ed45719b77ed --to 788a1ded488f5c0d3d594bc8f9fc3a10415f14b4; it exited 0.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-design\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-c926a8f43e21c447\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Consumed the sealed design assessment and independently checked D1/D2 against the implementation; did not rerun the assessment producer.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-discover\\\",\\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"A fresh discovery report was unnecessary for this bounded decoder correction. Inspected the affected component directly and preserved the read-only checkout.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-integrate\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/strict-json-readers-require-the-end-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"No inter-module API or MCP schema changed. Inspected the consumer and transport boundaries and independently reran the focused integration tests instead of producing a new assessment.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-tech-debt\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Reviewed the complete diff and inventory directly. No new TODO, FIXME, stub or panic debt was introduced; no assessment files were generated.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"closeout-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Requires completion and recording of this review; the reviewer was instructed not to record an attestation.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"review-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Cannot establish this review's recorded approval before POSE processes the draft.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"suggest-review\\\",\\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Resolved backend-go, security and documentation-style rules and applied them.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"surface-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/strict-json-readers-require-the-end-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Ran pose surface-check --spec pose-strict-json-readers-require-the-end --strict: exited 0, one target, zero findings.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"validate\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/strict-json-readers-require-the-end-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Accepted the sealed strict pipeline validation evidence. Independently reran the registered focused integration command successfully; did not rerun the full validation producer.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"validate\\\",\\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Accepted the sealed component validation evidence, including unit and build results. The focused tests were independently rerun against the reviewed checkout and finished successfully.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\\n```\",\n.pose/review-bundles/rvb-f8c550d2797eb3c5.json:294:          \"rationale\": \"observe bounded structural deltas on the canonical review subject\",\n.pose/review-bundles/rvb-f8c550d2797eb3c5.json:867:      \"structural-causality\"\n.pose/review-runs/rrn-f159474ba8bf6bc9.json:106:  \"output\": \"decision: changes-requested\\n\\nThree defects remain:\\n\\n- **F21 — medium:** Successful Git warnings are discarded below the history threshold, allowing unreadable graph metadata to report `ok`.\\n- **F22 — low:** Empty HEAD trees below the threshold report a check instead of being excluded.\\n- **F23 — low:** The displayed manual repair omits `--max-new-filters=-1`, so it can leave the recommendation unresolved.\\n\\nRules applied: feature review workflow, backend-go, security, documentation-style and delivery-evidence. I inspected the implementation, tests, CI, validation metadata and prior findings. I used sealed test evidence; no builds, repairs, repository edits or attestations were performed.\\n\\n```pose-draft\\n{\\n  \\\"schema\\\": \\\"pose.review.draft/v1\\\",\\n  \\\"decision\\\": \\\"changes-requested\\\",\\n  \\\"findings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"F21\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"medium\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"blocker\\\",\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/doctor_commit_graph.go\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": 72,\\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"Successful rev-list stderr is discarded, and lines 81-82 return before the successful-lookup warning handling at lines 105-108. Consequently, a repository below 500 commits whose malformed commit-graph causes Git to warn and fall back to ordinary traversal reports ok. This leaves R3 and the below-threshold portion of R1-F5/R3-F14/R4-F20 unresolved. Preserve operational diagnostics before the threshold return and extend the corrupt-graph regression to a history below the threshold.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"F22\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"low\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"blocker\\\",\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/doctor_commit_graph.go\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": 81,\\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"The short-history return precedes the empty-tree detection at lines 84-90. A committed empty HEAD tree with fewer than 500 commits therefore emits git.commit-graph at ok, although R3 explicitly excludes roots with no file in HEAD. The new empty-tree test lowers the threshold through longHistoryRepo and misses this branch. Apply the exclusion independently of the threshold and cover a short empty-tree history.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"F23\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"low\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"blocker\\\",\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/doctor.go\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": 379,\\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"The recommended manual command omits --max-new-filters=-1, as does the repair preview at line 94. With commitGraph.maxNewFilters=0 and no existing filters, following that command succeeds without producing the filters and leaves the check at next. The automatic repair correctly overrides the limit at doctor_commit_graph.go:175. Git's installed git-config and git-commit-graph manuals confirm the inherited default and override semantics. Make the displayed commands match the effective repair and test the displayed remediation under the restrictive configuration.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"prior_findings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R1-F5\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"partial\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"doctor_commit_graph.go:47-78 distinguishes expected exclusions from command failures, and doctor.go:370-371 reports failures. Successful-command stderr is handled at doctor_commit_graph.go:107 only after the threshold return; F21 remains.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R3-F9\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"doctor_commit_graph.go:65-70 excludes shallow repositories. doctor_commit_graph_test.go:252-260 covers a shallow clone above the reduced threshold; sealed integration:pose-mcp/go/doctor-recommends-the-commit-graph-integration passed.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R3-F10\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"doctor_commit_graph.go:175 explicitly supplies --max-new-filters=-1. doctor_commit_graph_test.go:265-275 verifies filter use after repair with maxNewFilters=0; sealed integration:pose-mcp/go/doctor-recommends-the-commit-graph-integration passed. F23 concerns the separately displayed manual command.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R3-F11\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"partial\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"doctor_commit_graph.go:88-90 now excludes an empty tree above the threshold, covered by doctor_commit_graph_test.go:280-286. The earlier return at lines 81-82 bypasses this exclusion for short histories; see F22.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R3-F12\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"doctor_commit_graph.go:159-166 resolves changedPathsVersion before deprecated readChangedPaths. doctor_commit_graph_test.go:291-298 covers conflicting settings with a missing graph; sealed integration:pose-mcp/go/doctor-recommends-the-commit-graph-integration passed.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R3-F13\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"doctor_commit_graph.go:186 supplies GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH=1 to every diagnostic Git invocation. doctor_commit_graph_test.go:303-326 checks failure without object-count changes in a tree-filtered partial clone; sealed integration:pose-mcp/go/doctor-recommends-the-commit-graph-integration passed.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R3-F14\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"partial\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"doctor_commit_graph.go:190-197 preserves bounded stderr on success, and lines 107-108 classify lookup stderr as a warning. doctor_commit_graph_test.go:331-340 covers a corrupt graph above the reduced threshold. The short-history branch still discards diagnostics; F21 remains.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R4-F15\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"doctor_commit_graph.go:65-70 and TestDoctorCommitGraphSkipsAShallowClone at doctor_commit_graph_test.go:252 establish the shallow exclusion; sealed integration:pose-mcp/go/doctor-recommends-the-commit-graph-integration passed.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R4-F16\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"doctor_commit_graph.go:175 overrides every configured generation limit with --max-new-filters=-1. TestDoctorCommitGraphFixIgnoresMaxNewFilters at doctor_commit_graph_test.go:265 covers zero; sealed integration:pose-mcp/go/doctor-recommends-the-commit-graph-integration passed.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R4-F17\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"partial\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"doctor_commit_graph.go:88-90 fixes the long-history empty-tree recommendation, with regression coverage at doctor_commit_graph_test.go:280. The threshold return at lines 81-82 still bypasses the spec's empty-tree exclusion; F22 remains.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R4-F18\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"doctor_commit_graph.go:159-166 follows configuration precedence. TestDoctorCommitGraphFollowsConfigurationPrecedence at doctor_commit_graph_test.go:291 verifies a fixable recommendation with changedPathsVersion=1 and readChangedPaths=false; sealed integration:pose-mcp/go/doctor-recommends-the-commit-graph-integration passed.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R4-F19\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"doctor_commit_graph.go:186 disables lazy fetching. TestDoctorCommitGraphNeverFetches at doctor_commit_graph_test.go:303 verifies that missing promised trees produce a failure without adding objects; sealed integration:pose-mcp/go/doctor-recommends-the-commit-graph-integration passed.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R4-F20\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"partial\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"doctor_commit_graph.go:190-197 retains successful-command stderr and lines 107-108 warn on lookup diagnostics. The corrupt-graph test at doctor_commit_graph_test.go:331 exercises only the above-threshold path. F21 identifies the remaining below-threshold loss.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"sweep\\\": \\\"Reviewed all six subject paths, the scope's requirements and D1, the complete commit-graph implementation and tests, doctor reporting and repair registration, both full-history CI jobs, validation-matrix additions and edits, and start metadata. Checked prior findings, raw-history environment handling, literal pathspecs, partial-clone authority, shallow and empty histories, configuration precedence, successful and failing stderr paths, trace cleanup, manual remediation and sealed validation. Ran read-only context, suggestion, bundle inspection, recurrence, artifact and surface commands plus Git trace probes. Fresh builds and tests were not attempted in the read-only sandbox. Live gate recomputation selected a different change-set head, so the supplied sealed-subject gate outputs remain the relevant evidence. No repository changes or attestation were made.\\\",\\n  \\\"criteria\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assumption-integrity\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/doctor-recommends-the-commit-graph-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Examined the actual Git-based fixtures and implementation rather than relying on implementer claims. Local read-only probes verified Git 2.56 trace statistics and graph readability. Sealed tests support alternate and split graphs, disabled reads and partial clones. Trace event stability across future Git versions remains the explicitly documented technical risk; no new risk is accepted by this review.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-concurrency\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/doctor-recommends-the-commit-graph-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The new diagnostic runs sequential subprocesses, introduces no concurrent production mutation, uses a unique trace file per invocation and defers its removal after creation. Repair remains inside the existing explicit doctor repair lifecycle.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-contracts\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/doctor-recommends-the-commit-graph-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The existing doctor report shape and repair registry are preserved. Added check names use the existing finding and remediation contracts; no MCP, REST or event schema changes were introduced.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-input-errors\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"F21\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-integration-impact\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/doctor-recommends-the-commit-graph-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The integration test invokes the production doctor command and explicit repair path. Both full-history CI jobs write their graph before gates, and the validation matrix registers the real-Git integration suite.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-observability\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"F21\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"compatibility\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/doctor-recommends-the-commit-graph-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Examined doctor finding serialization, registry composition and raw-history Git execution. The CLI adds findings within the existing format and preserves existing file and MCP contracts. No migration is required.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"correctness\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"F22\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"design-causality\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-7bc4e45827de3581\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"D1 places repository maintenance behind an explicit doctor repair rather than governance reads. Delegating graph selection and filter-use judgment to Git avoids reimplementing alternate-directory, graph-chain and format precedence. The required integration check supplies evidence for R1-R3. The matrix path also contains adjacent specs' checks; those neighboring edits have no independent requirement in this scope.\\\",\\n      \\\"mappings\\\": [\\n        {\\n          \\\"delta\\\": \\\"SD-28db7861\\\",\\n          \\\"basis\\\": \\\"R1\\\",\\n          \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"mapped\\\",\\n          \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The changed validation-matrix path registers the permanent doctor integration check declared by the scope's delivery plan, exercising recommendation and repair behavior.\\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"delta\\\": \\\"SD-9fc0fe4e\\\",\\n          \\\"basis\\\": \\\"R2\\\",\\n          \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"mapped\\\",\\n          \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The changed validation-matrix path runs the doctor integration suite, including production repair and post-repair verification. Neighboring checks in this co-owned file belong to adjacent scopes.\\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"delta\\\": \\\"SD-d29398e6\\\",\\n          \\\"basis\\\": \\\"R3\\\",\\n          \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"mapped\\\",\\n          \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The changed validation-matrix path selects all TestDoctorCommitGraph regressions, providing durable negative-path coverage for exclusions, configuration and diagnostic failures.\\\"\\n        }\\n      ]\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"documentation\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"F23\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"operability\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"F23\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"requirements\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"F21\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"scope\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-7bc4e45827de3581\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The semantic implementation is confined to the doctor check and repair, its tests, CI setup and declared validation metadata. The start record is governance metadata. Other commits in the range explain adjacent co-owned matrix edits and are not treated as new doctor functionality.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"security\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/doctor-recommends-the-commit-graph-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Examined fixed repair arguments, raw-history execution, literal path handling, bounded returned stderr and GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH. The partial-clone regression verifies no added objects during diagnosis. No new credentials, remote authority or dependency was introduced.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"solution-proportionality\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-7bc4e45827de3581\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Compared the implementation with documentation-only advice and direct commit-graph parsing. Existing doctor repair composition plus Git's own trace is a proportionate solution that avoids a new graph-format parser, daemon or maintenance scheduler. A stable Git API for reporting effective filter availability would justify replacing trace parsing; a trace-format change would invalidate the present probe and should fail the real-Git integration test.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"tools\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"artifact-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-doctor-recommends-the-commit-graph --strict\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Inspected the pipeline output at /var/tmp/closeout/ac-dc.out: it identifies the requested sealed range and reports warning-level provenance findings. A live rerun was invoked, but its different selected change-set head makes the supplied sealed-subject output authoritative for this review.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-design\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-7bc4e45827de3581\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Did not rerun the assessment producer under the no-write boundary. Reviewed the sealed structural evidence and independently inspected the design and metadata changes.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-discover\\\",\\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Discovery writes assessment artifacts and was not rerun. The scope and component were resolved read-only; implementation and sealed component evidence were inspected directly.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-integrate\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/doctor-recommends-the-commit-graph-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Did not invoke the assessment producer under the no-write boundary. No public inter-module schema changed; production command composition and integration tests were inspected.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-tech-debt\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Did not run the assessment producer because it writes governed artifacts. Inspected the complete new implementation and tests for debt markers and reviewed the spec's existing performance follow-up.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"closeout-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:pose context --task spec:pose-doctor-recommends-the-commit-graph --json\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Completion-only gate is deferred until POSE records and verifies this review conclusion. This review does not record an attestation.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"review-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:pose context --task spec:pose-doctor-recommends-the-commit-graph --json\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Deferred until the review conclusion is recorded; it cannot establish approval before that prerequisite.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"suggest-review\\\",\\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Executed successfully and applied its selected backend-go, security and documentation-style rules.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"surface-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/doctor-recommends-the-commit-graph-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Inspected /var/tmp/closeout/sc-dc.out for the sealed subject: one target, 232 results and zero findings. The live read-only rerun also exited zero with zero findings; sealed evidence remains the subject-bound basis.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"validate\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/doctor-recommends-the-commit-graph-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Used the sealed strict pipeline execution as required by the sandbox boundary. The delivery validation report records 232 passed checks and zero failures. No fresh build or test execution was attempted.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"validate\\\",\\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Used sealed pose-mcp validation evidence and inspected the package-test output and new regression tests. The sealed module build and doctor integration check also passed; those passing tests do not cover F21-F23.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\\n```\",\n.pose/review-runs/rrn-93ce7f7f0467fa87.json:106:  \"output\": \"decision: changes-requested\\n\\nThe medium blocker remains: tree listings are retained without an output bound before entry limits apply. Both prior findings remain unfixed. I also found stale cleanup-limit documentation.\\n\\nReviewed as a Go bugfix under the review workflow, backend-go, security, documentation-style, and delivery-evidence rules. The surface check passed. I inspected the sealed tests and validation results; no builds, edits, or attestations were made. The local artifact-check rerun was interrupted without a result; its supplied pipeline output contains 975 warnings and no error markers.\\n\\n```pose-draft\\n{\\n  \\\"schema\\\": \\\"pose.review.draft/v1\\\",\\n  \\\"decision\\\": \\\"changes-requested\\\",\\n  \\\"findings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"N1\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"low\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"follow-up\\\",\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\".pose/specs/2026-11-16-pose-git-snapshot-budget-scales-with-the-tree.md\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": 40,\\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"R1 still promises complete coverage for every clean tree below the ceiling, but the formula measures stored blob bytes while snapshots and cleanup consume materialized bytes. CRLF or smudge expansion beyond the margin, populated submodules, and ignored files can exhaust the budget. This fails closed, but the coverage promise needs qualification. Qualify R1 and the corresponding cleanup coverage assumptions without weakening fail-closed behavior.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"N2\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"medium\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"blocker\\\",\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_snapshot_integrity.go\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": 67,\\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"dispatchDiskSnapshot still calls exec.Cmd.Output for the entire recursive tree listing before its 100000-entry guard. gitCommittedTreeBytes then splits the entire retained listing. Arbitrarily many empty files or sufficiently large path metadata can therefore consume unbounded memory despite a near-margin content budget. The new cleanup-budget capture also uses unbounded snapshotGit at review_adapter_containment.go:474, before the bounded cleanup inventory. These commands use a background context, so cancellation does not bound this new work either. Bound or stream listing output before retaining it, reject excessive metadata or entries, and add a negative regression covering both snapshot and cleanup-budget capture.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"N3\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"low\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"follow-up\\\",\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"POSE.md\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": 1023,\\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"The operational manual still states that workspace cleanup has a fixed 256 MiB inventory cap, although cleanup now uses committed blob bytes plus the margin, capped at 4 GiB. The shipped English scaffold manual at pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/POSE.md:1010 and Portuguese scaffold manual at pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/locales/pt-BR/POSE.md:1020 repeat the stale limit. Update all three descriptions while preserving the separate registration and runtime limits.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"prior_findings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R1-F2\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"not-fixed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"The unrestricted clean-tree promise remains at .pose/specs/2026-11-16-pose-git-snapshot-budget-scales-with-the-tree.md:40. git_snapshot_integrity.go:44 sums stored blob sizes, while dispatchDiskSnapshot walks materialized and ignored contents. Reported as N1.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R1-F3\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"not-fixed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_snapshot_integrity.go:67 still uses unbounded Output before the entry guard at line 98; line 46 splits the complete listing. Cleanup adds another unbounded listing at review_adapter_containment.go:474. Reported as N2.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"sweep\\\": \\\"Reviewed R1-R4 and D1; both implementation files; all new budget tests; validation-matrix changes; listing parsing for blobs, symlinks and gitlinks; governed output-overflow handling; byte and entry limits; ignored files and materialization expansion; cleanup ownership capture, dispatch ordering and confined removal; package-variable test isolation; public CLI/MCP compatibility; relevant knowledge; root and shipped operational manuals; supplied artifact/surface outputs and sealed validation. Verified the current tree listing contains 8272 entries and 273300097 blob bytes. Confirmed the repository remains unchanged.\\\",\\n  \\\"criteria\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assumption-integrity\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N1\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-concurrency\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N2\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-contracts\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/cli-mcp-operation-results-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Examined the changed internal helpers and their callers. No public signature, persisted schema, CLI option or MCP contract changes; snapshot failures retain the existing typed error boundary.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-input-errors\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N2\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-integration-impact\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/git-snapshot-budget-scales-with-the-tree-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Inspected closeout comparison, dispatch snapshots and cleanup integration. Cleanup captures its budget from the coordinator registration before the reviewer starts and preserves confined ownership checks.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-observability\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Snapshot budget errors include the numeric budget and retain GitSnapshotError context. Cleanup retains its bounded, non-sensitive operational failure message. Listing failure falls back to the margin as R3 specifies.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"compatibility\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/git-dispatch-snapshot-integrity-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Examined four-field ls-tree parsing, gitlink '-' sizes, symlink handling and callers. Existing public contracts remain intact, and the byte allowance never drops below the previous margin.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"correctness\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N2\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"design-causality\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-8abb5c2c6ab55a2a\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"R1-R4 and D1 connect the observed fixed-cap failure to the minimum work required to read a committed checkout. The shared budget helper scales that allowance and preserves a ceiling; cleanup captures the corresponding initial commit budget before reviewer execution. No individual structural delta facts were listed in the brief.\\\",\\n      \\\"mappings\\\": []\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"documentation\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N3\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"operability\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-adapter-containment-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Examined budget-exhaustion errors, fallback behavior and cleanup retention. Snapshot errors identify the byte budget, uncertain cleanup retains resources, and existing ownership diagnostics remain available.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"requirements\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N1\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"scope\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/git-snapshot-budget-scales-with-the-tree-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The scoped implementation changes the two snapshot budgets and delegated-worktree cleanup budget required by R1-R4. It preserves entry limits and does not introduce retention, new public APIs or unrelated refactoring.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"security\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N2\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"solution-proportionality\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-8abb5c2c6ab55a2a\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Compared D1's alternatives. A fixed 1 GiB cap postpones the same failure; retention changes governed data and exceeds this repair's scope. A shared clamped budget and captured cleanup allowance are proportionate. The choice requires revisiting when materialization expansion exceeds the margin or the committed tree reaches the ceiling; unbounded listing capture remains separately blocking in N2.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"tools\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"artifact-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-git-snapshot-budget-scales-with-the-tree --strict\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Disposition uses the supplied pipeline execution output /var/tmp/closeout/ac-bg.out: 4 claims, 19 observations, 975 warnings and no error markers. The local read-only rerun was interrupted without a result and is not claimed as a passing rerun.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-design\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-8abb5c2c6ab55a2a\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Did not rerun a writing assessment in the read-only review. Examined the sealed design evidence, spec decision D1 and implementation directly.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-discover\\\",\\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Assessment reruns write repository artifacts. Used sealed module validation and direct code inspection.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-integrate\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Avoided assessment writes. Inspected internal callers and sealed contract/integration evidence; no public inter-module contract changed.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-tech-debt\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Avoided assessment writes. Inspected the changed code and tests for unfinished implementation; no new TODO, FIXME, stub or panic marker was introduced.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"closeout-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Requires completion and recording of the review; this request prohibits recording an attestation.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"review-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Requires the completed recorded conclusion; POSE must execute it after processing this draft.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"suggest-review\\\",\\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Executed successfully and applied the selected backend-go, security and documentation rules.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"surface-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/git-snapshot-budget-scales-with-the-tree-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Executed pose surface-check --spec pose-git-snapshot-budget-scales-with-the-tree --strict successfully: one target, 232 results and zero findings.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"validate\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Used the sealed pipeline execution and inspected .pose/results/delivery-validation.json: strict validation reports 232 executed checks, all passing. The reviewed implementation files have no diff between that report's Git head and the sealed head. Did not rerun build-producing validation in the read-only sandbox.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"validate\\\",\\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/git-snapshot-budget-scales-with-the-tree-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Used sealed module validation and inspected the focused check selecting TestGitSnapshotBudget and TestReviewWorktreeCleanup. Read all five new tests; they cover clean oversized trees, growth rejection and budget clamps, but not excessive listing output.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\\n```\",\n.pose/review-runs/rrn-f64458878e6490e0.json:106:  \"output\": \"decision: changes-requested\\n\\n**N4 — medium, blocker:** [git_snapshot_integrity.go:247](pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_snapshot_integrity.go:247) bypasses the new listing bounds when `producer` is present. Production closeout supplies a producer, so its listing permits up to 512 MiB and has no deadline, violating R5. Apply the bounds through the governed capture API and cover that path with a regression.\\n\\nRules applied during review: pose-review workflow; Go backend, security, documentation-style, and delivery-evidence rules. Reviewed the sealed range and all listed implementation, governance, test, and documentation changes. No repository changes or attestations were made.\\n\\nTests and builds were assessed from sealed evidence and test inspection. The artifact-check rerun reported a different head, so its result was excluded; the supplied report matches the sealed head.\\n\\n```pose-draft\\n{\\n  \\\"schema\\\": \\\"pose.review.draft/v1\\\",\\n  \\\"decision\\\": \\\"changes-requested\\\",\\n  \\\"findings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"N4\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"medium\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"blocker\\\",\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_snapshot_integrity.go\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": 247,\\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"The producer branch replaces the bounded listing runner with captureGovernanceGit. Production closeout supplies a producer at closeout_plan.go:303-308. captureGovernanceGit uses the 512 MiB governanceReadViewMaxInputBytes limit (governance_read_view_git.go:78-79 and governance_read_view.go:25) and context.Background (governance_read_view_git.go:114-115), so its recursive listing has neither R5's 64 MiB limit nor its two-minute deadline. It can retain oversized metadata before the entry guard and wait indefinitely for Git. TestGitTreeListingIsBounded exercises only calls without a producer and misses this production route. Apply the listing-specific limit and deadline through the governed context capture API while preserving read-view provenance, and add producer-path byte-limit and deadline regressions.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"prior_findings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R1-F2\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"Spec line 40 now explicitly qualifies coverage by materialized bytes and names smudge/CRLF expansion, populated submodules and ignored files as fail-closed cases.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R1-F3\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"git_snapshot_integrity.go:53-63 bounds the disk snapshot's listing before retention; dispatchDiskSnapshot uses it at lines 83-85. The shared runner bounds combined output before buffering at governance_read_view_git.go:693-707.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R2-N1\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"Spec line 40 qualifies the stored-versus-materialized byte assumption. Cleanup uses the same captured budget at review_adapter_containment.go:471-475 and 569-573; expansion beyond it remains retained.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R2-N2\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"partial\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"Disk snapshot, non-producer comparison and cleanup-budget capture now use listCommittedTree with byte and time bounds; git_snapshot_budget_test.go:162-183 covers their oversized-listing behavior. The producer comparison still bypasses those bounds at git_snapshot_integrity.go:245-247; see N4.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R2-N3\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"POSE.md:1023, locales/pt-BR/POSE.md:1020, internal/scaffold/dist/POSE.md:1010 and internal/scaffold/dist/locales/pt-BR/POSE.md:1020 now describe committed-tree bytes plus 256 MiB, bounded between 256 MiB and 4 GiB, while preserving registration/runtime limits.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"sweep\\\": \\\"Swept the sealed range's scoped implementation, tests, validation-matrix changes, start record, spec requirements and D1, and all four manual copies. Traced production closeout, producer and non-producer comparison, nested comparisons, disk snapshot, cleanup ownership capture and confined deletion; inspected Git output buffering, deadlines, error propagation, entry guards, budget floor/ceiling, fallback behavior and test coverage. Consulted applicable rules and prior snapshot knowledge. Inspected sealed validation evidence and supplied artifact/surface reports. No builds or tests were executed in the read-only sandbox. The artifact rerun reported an unrelated head and was excluded. No additional established defects were found.\\\"\\n  ,\\n  \\\"criteria\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assumption-integrity\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-0637e028bd14425d\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Examined R1-R5, D1, byte accounting and reduced-margin fixtures. Stored blob bytes are the verified budget basis; materialized expansion and the absolute ceiling are explicit coverage limits. Retention remains spec follow-up F1. Dynamic timeout behavior was not independently executed; the producer-path omission is recorded as N4.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-concurrency\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N4\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-contracts\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/git-and-dispatch-snapshot-integrity-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Public CLI, MCP and persisted schemas are unchanged. Internal ls-tree parsing was updated consistently for the size column.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-input-errors\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N4\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-integration-impact\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/git-snapshot-budget-scales-with-the-tree-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Inspected production closeout and delegated cleanup callers. The shared budget reaches both snapshot readers and captured cleanup ownership; N4 separately records the governed listing-bound gap.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-observability\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/git-snapshot-budget-scales-with-the-tree-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Snapshot growth errors include the effective byte budget; listing errors propagate through existing bounded Git diagnostics. Cleanup preserves its existing retained-resource error behavior.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"compatibility\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/git-and-dispatch-snapshot-integrity-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Examined public entrypoints, persisted cleanup representation and raw-history Git configuration. No public signature or schema migration is introduced; small-repository content budgets retain their existing floor.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"correctness\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N4\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"design-causality\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-0637e028bd14425d\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"D1 ties the budget to the committed bytes the readers must inspect, removing the fixed-cap failure while preserving a growth margin and absolute ceiling. Capturing the cleanup budget from the coordinator before adapter execution preserves its authority boundary. The permanent integration check provides regression evidence for R1-R5.\\\",\\n      \\\"mappings\\\": [\\n        {\\n          \\\"delta\\\": \\\"SD-29e3919f\\\",\\n          \\\"basis\\\": \\\"R5\\\",\\n          \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"mapped\\\",\\n          \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The validation matrix registers the required snapshot-budget integration check, including TestGitTreeListingIsBounded, to retain regression coverage for bounded tree listings alongside R1-R4 budget behavior.\\\"\\n        }\\n      ]\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"documentation\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/distributed-instructions-parity-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Compared English and Portuguese operational manuals and both scaffold copies. All state the scaled workspace budget and preserve the separate entry, registration, runtime and depth limits. R1 now states materialization assumptions explicitly.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"operability\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/git-snapshot-budget-scales-with-the-tree-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Inspected budget errors, fail-closed fallback, retained-resource behavior and operational instructions. Growth remains diagnosable and uncertain cleanup resources remain available for inspection.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"requirements\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N4\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"scope\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-0637e028bd14425d\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The scoped changes implement R1-R5 and D1 through shared budgeting, bounded listings, cleanup capture, regression registration and matching manuals. No retention mechanism, entry-limit change or public API expansion was added.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"security\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N4\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"solution-proportionality\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-0637e028bd14425d\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Compared D1's scaled budget with raising a constant and retaining fewer records. Reusing ls-tree sizes and the existing bounded runner is a small sufficient design without new configuration or abstractions. Trees or materialized expansion beyond the documented limits invalidate coverage and remain a separate retention concern. N4 is an implementation omission within this design.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"tools\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"artifact-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:cat /var/tmp/closeout/ac-bg.out /var/tmp/closeout/sc-bg.out\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Inspected supplied pipeline output for the exact sealed head 8cbf1620 and change set cs-669ad20935c7. It reports eight claims and repository-wide orphan warnings. The independent rerun reported a different head and was excluded from sealed-subject evidence.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-design\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-0637e028bd14425d\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Used the sealed design evidence and independently inspected D1 and structural changes; did not rerun an assessment that can write repository state.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-discover\\\",\\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-0637e028bd14425d\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Read-only review boundary prohibits assessment-state writes. Inspected component implementation and sealed validation evidence instead.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-integrate\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/git-snapshot-budget-scales-with-the-tree-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Did not rerun state-writing assessments. Traced production integration directly and inspected sealed integration results.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-tech-debt\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:rg -n 'TODO|FIXME|stub|panic' pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_snapshot_integrity.go pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_snapshot_budget_test.go pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_adapter_containment.go\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Did not run a state-writing assessment. Direct marker scan found no markers in the scoped Go files; inspected the spec's existing retention follow-up F1.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"closeout-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Requires the recorded review conclusion; this review neither records an attestation nor closes the spec.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"review-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Requires POSE to record and verify this review's conclusion first.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"suggest-review\\\",\\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Selected the review workflow and security, documentation-style and backend-go rules.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"surface-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/git-snapshot-budget-scales-with-the-tree-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Inspected the supplied sealed-head surface report: one target, 232 results, zero findings. Also executed the requested command; it returned zero findings. Used sealed integration evidence for the conclusion.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"validate\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"build:pose-mcp/go/build\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Disposed from the supplied sealed strict-validation run and inspected delivery-validation.json and relevant test source. No local build or test writes were attempted.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"validate\\\",\\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/git-snapshot-budget-scales-with-the-tree-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Sealed module validation passes the focused real-Git regression suite and broader module checks. Inspection establishes that the focused listing regression omits the producer branch, reported as N4.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\\n```\",\n.pose/review-runs/rrn-243366b14aa5fea4.json:86:  \"brief_notes\": \"Implementer notes (Claude Opus 5.5, the lead in this session). Use them as context only; the judgment is yours.\\n\\n- The feature was motivated by the Harne8 batch of 2026-11-22. There, every review round re-ran a 72-check matrix of about 35 minutes, and intermittent suites failed roughly one run in three.\\n- In this repository `pose-mcp` holds 233 of the 236 checks and is high criticality, so `--carry` saves little here. The dogfood record at c4182727 carried five of six modules with zero changed files.\\n- Please challenge the soundness argument of D1 in particular. A carried result is bound to the material computed at HEAD, and that is only safe when the selection guarantees the carried module's inputs did not change.\\n- Please also check the derived-record exclusion (`carryExclusions` with `posemodel.IsAdministrativePath`) and the engine identity, which is the version plus the VCS revision.\\n- Report every finding you see in this round, each classified as blocker or follow-up.\\n\\nRound 2 notes:\\n- F1 from round 1 (rrn-0dd98c4aab8b5918) is addressed in d601fbe1. The record now has `material_clean`, set when the working copy matched HEAD at the start and at the end of the run. `planCarry` refuses a base without it, or with any unavailable material binding. `TestCarryRefusesABaseThatValidatedADirtyWorkingCopy` reproduces your sequence: a pass over an uncommitted fix, a commit of the record alone, the restored failing file, then `--carry`. The test failed with the check mutated out. Account for F1 in prior_findings.\\n- Round 1 also changed files in the sealed worktree because `pose assess integrate` and `pose assess tech-debt` persist their outputs: `.pose/assessments/*`, `.pose/state/*`. Run every `assess` command on a copy in the operation's scratch, never in the sealed checkout, and keep the Bash working directory at the checkout root. Example: `scratch=$(mktemp -d \\\"$TMPDIR/pose-assess.XXXXXX\\\")`, `git archive HEAD | tar -x -C \\\"$scratch\\\"`, `sh -c 'cd \\\"$1\\\" \\u0026\\u0026 exec \\\"$2\\\" assess integrate --json' sh \\\"$scratch\\\" \\\"$(command -v pose)\\\"`.\\n- The `artifact-check` head differs from the bundle subject because the index commits also carry this spec's trailer. `artifact-check` resolves the change set range to the last trailer commit, which is an index-only commit. The bundle subject skips commits that only touch derived records, whose material digest is unchanged. That is existing engine behaviour, which the lead will take up separately. Judge it as you see fit.\\n- The full matrix takes about 13 minutes. If you cannot complete it in the sandbox, cite the sealed canonical result for the `validate` tool and state your own run's limits.\\n\\nRound 3 notes: round 2 (rrn-1c033e4c349d7794) found N1–N4. 2077731b fixes them:\\n- The changed set uses `git diff -z --no-renames` and `ls-files -z`, so a rename names both sides and a quoted name keeps its owner.\\n- The root module `.` is never exempt from root files.\\n- A build with `vcs.modified=true` is not a verifiable identity: it never carries, and a base with a `.dirty` identity is refused.\\n\\nThe regression tests are `TestCarrySelectsBothSidesOfARename`, `TestCarryKeepsTheOwnerOfAQuotedName`, `TestCarryRootModuleOwnsRootFiles` and `TestEngineIdentityRefusesModifiedBuilds`. Each one failed with its fix mutated out. Account for R2-N1..R2-N4 in prior_findings.\\n\\nRound 4 notes: round 3 (rrn-3461f6ff36909419) found N5 and N6.\\n- N5: a declared `dependsOn` path now owns its files even when the dependency is no longer discovered (`underDeclaredDependency`).\\n- N6: module metadata that does not decode is now an error. It means a full run under `--carry` and exit 2 under `--changed-from`.\\nThe regression tests are `TestCarryDeletedDependencySelectsItsDependents` and `TestCarryRejectsUndecodableMetadata`. Both failed with their fix mutated out. Account for R3-N5 and R3-N6 in prior_findings.\\n\\nPlease make this round an exhaustive sweep and report every remaining issue in it, each classified as blocker or follow-up, so the scope can converge. Cover at least:\\n- gitlinks and submodules;\\n- symlinks;\\n- paths that differ only by case;\\n- `moduleOverrides` modules that have no manifest;\\n- nested modules;\\n- a module whose matrix checks or stack change while the matrix digest does not;\\n- criticality and policy widening;\\n- chained carries over many bases;\\n- concurrent runs writing the canonical file.\\n- The lead's own sweep before this round found a gitlink case: a changed gitlink above a declared dependency selected nothing under it. A changed path now selects the modules and dependencies under it, tested by `TestChangedScopeGitlinkAboveADependencySelectsItsDependents`.\\n\\nRound 5 notes: round 4 (rrn-4b28f2ff95acf9c4) found N7–N10. The selection in `computeChangedScope` was rewritten instead of patched. Each changed file now independently selects:\\n- its most specific owner;\\n- every module beneath it;\\n- every module whose declared dependency contains it, lies beneath it or is the root `.`, when that dependency is not a discovered module, which the transitive widening covers;\\n- for a file no module owns, the root module and every module that is not self-contained.\\n\\n`planCarry` refuses when any module is reached through a symlink. `material_clean` now also requires the HEAD at the end of the run to equal the recorded head. The regression tests are `TestCarryDeletedNestedDependencySelectsItsDependents`, `TestCarryRootDependencyIsChangedByRootFiles`, `TestCarryRefusesModulesReachedThroughASymlink` and `TestValidateHeadMovingDuringTheRunIsNotClean`. Each failed with its fix mutated out. Account for R4-N7..R4-N10 in prior_findings, and again report every remaining issue in this round.\\n\\nRound 6 notes: round 5 (rrn-b07ee93779a65e40) found N11–N14.\\n- N11: every eligible dependency now counts (`declaredDependencyHits`).\\n- N12: a run whose HEAD moved, or that is otherwise not `material_clean`, records every material binding as unavailable.\\n- N13: `aliasedModule` also refuses modules that share a physical directory (`os.SameFile`).\\n- N14: the head is pinned before planning, and `planCarry`, the selection and the exclusions use that SHA.\\nThe regression tests are `TestChangedScopeEvaluatesEveryDeclaredDependency`, `TestValidateHeadMovingDuringTheRunBindsNoMaterial`, `TestCarryRefusesModulesSharingADirectory` and `TestCarryPlansAgainstThePinnedHead`. Each failed with its fix mutated out. Account for R5-N11..R5-N14 and the remaining partials R3-N9/R3-N10 in prior_findings, and report every remaining issue in this round.\\n\\nRound 7 notes: round 6 (rrn-88e0428bda9bc9c7) found N15 and N16.\\n- N15: a declared dependency now selects its consumer whenever a changed file intersects it, discovered or not, unless it is the file's own owner, which the transitive widening covers.\\n- N16: `planCarry` refuses when a declared dependency path is reached through a symlink.\\nThe regression tests are `TestChangedScopeDiscoveredAncestorDependencySelectsItsDependents`, which covers a parent and a discovered root dependency, and `TestCarryRefusesDependenciesReachedThroughASymlink`. Account for R6-N15 and R6-N16, and report every remaining issue in this round.\\n\\nRound 8 notes: round 7 (rrn-85704a129332a685) found N17–N19. Instead of chasing alias forms one path at a time, `planCarry` now applies global rules:\\n- `caseInsensitiveFilesystem` refuses on case-folding filesystems.\\n- `aliasingSymlink` refuses any tracked symlink whose path or target lies in a non-root module or intersects a declared dependency, or whose target leaves the repository. Symlinks between unowned paths, such as `.claude/skills` to `.agents/skills`, stay allowed, since a change on either side already selects the root and every non-self-contained module.\\n- `duplicateCheckID` and a base-id check refuse duplicate check ids.\\nThe tests are `TestCarryRefusesASymlinkInsideAModule`, `TestCarryRefusesASymlinkFromAModuleToAnUnownedPath`, `TestCarryAllowsSymlinksBetweenUnownedPaths`, `TestCarryDetectsACaseInsensitiveFilesystem` and `TestCarryRefusesDuplicateCheckIDs`. Account for R7-N17..R7-N19, and report every remaining issue in this round.\\n\\nRound 9 notes: round 8 (rrn-0375009e985e6a3d) found N20–N23.\\n- N23: both diffs force `-c diff.ignoreSubmodules=none diff --ignore-submodules=none`.\\n- N21: `material_clean` also requires `materialWorktreeClean` at the end, so untracked unignored material counts.\\n- N20: `submoduleAliases` scans each submodule that holds a module or a dependency, at its recorded commit. It refuses when that submodule is not checked out at the commit or has nested submodules.\\n- N22: `casefoldedDirectory` probes every module directory and the nearest existing directory of every dependency.\\nThe regression tests are `TestChangedScopeIgnoresSubmoduleHidingConfiguration`, `TestValidateUntrackedMaterialCreatedDuringTheRunIsNotClean`, `TestCarryRefusesAnAliasingSymlinkInsideASubmodule` and `TestCarryDetectsACaseFoldedDirectory`. Each failed with its fix mutated out. Account for R7-N20..R7-N23 and the partials, and report every remaining issue in this round.\\n\\nRound 10 notes: round 9 (rrn-dfc7e3348240ce19) found N24–N26.\\n- N24: `submoduleAliases` scans every gitlink, not only those holding a module or dependency.\\n- N25: the selection also picks every module enclosing the owner. The lead extended this: the root module encloses every module.\\n- N26: `carryRelevantDirs` probes every existing directory from the root to each module and dependency.\\nThe regression tests are `TestChangedScopeSelectsTheEnclosingModule`, `TestChangedScopeRootModuleEnclosesEveryModule`, `TestCarryScansAGitlinkInsideAModule` and `TestCarryRelevantDirsIncludeEveryAncestor`. Account for R9-N24..R9-N26 and report every remaining issue in this round.\\n\\nRound 11 notes: round 10 (rrn-29af03286365811e) found N27–N29.\\n- N27: `casefoldedDirectory` probes with `Lstat`, skips unusable entries and treats an unreadable directory as folding.\\n- N28: `planCarry` refuses absolute or root-escaping dependencies.\\n- N29: the ADR consequences paragraph and the spec summary now describe the selection accurately.\\nThe tests are `TestCarryCaseProbeSkipsUnusableEntries` and `TestCarryRefusesDependenciesOutsideTheRepository`. Account for R10-N27..R10-N29 and report every remaining issue in this round.\\n\\nRound 12 notes: round 11 (rrn-c0b4006e2a8ff303) found N30–N32. All are refused conservatively:\\n- N30: a dependency that is not already a clean path.\\n- N32: non-ASCII module or dependency paths.\\n- N31: any index entry marked assume-unchanged or skip-worktree, in the repository or a checked-out submodule. It also clears `material_clean`.\\nThe tests are `TestCarryRefusesUncleanDependencies`, `TestCarryRefusesNonASCIIPaths` and `TestCarryRefusesHiddenIndexEntries`. Account for R11-N30..R11-N32 and report every remaining issue in this round.\\n\\nRound 13 notes: round 12 (rrn-abb61f059dc6d700) found N33–N35.\\n- N33: `physicallyLexical` resolves each dependency and its existing ancestors, tracked or ignored symlinks alike.\\n- N34: `material_clean` requires HEAD's reflog length to be unchanged and readable.\\n- N35: `casefoldedDirectory` probes only ASCII-letter entries and treats a directory without one as folding.\\nThe tests are `TestCarryRefusesDependenciesThroughAnIgnoredSymlink`, `TestValidateHeadMovingAndReturningIsNotClean` and `TestCarryCaseProbeUsesOnlyASCIILetters`. Account for R12-N33..R12-N35 and report every remaining issue in this round.\\n\\nRound 14 notes: round 13 (rrn-f6546af4c9e5625e) found N36–N39.\\n- N36: the cleanliness status reads force `-c core.fileMode=true`.\\n- N37: HEAD and its reflog are pinned before the matrix is read and modules are discovered. This is structural ordering; a race before planning cannot be reproduced deterministically.\\n- N38: `submodulesCheckedOut` requires every gitlink to be checked out at its recorded commit, both for `material_clean` and for the carry.\\n- N39 is recorded as follow-up F2 in the spec.\\nThe tests are `TestValidateModeChangeHiddenByConfigurationIsNotClean` and `TestValidateUninitializedSubmoduleIsNotClean`. Account for R13-N36..R13-N39 and report every remaining issue in this round.\\n\\nRound 15 notes: round 14 (rrn-db44fd7f02f7b981) found N40 and N41, and N42 restated F2. One predicate, `validationMaterialClean`, now covers status, hidden index entries and submodule checkouts. It runs at the pin, before the matrix is read and modules are discovered, and again at the end. The test is `TestValidateConditionClearedDuringTheRunIsNotClean`. Account for R14-N40..R14-N42 and report every remaining issue in this round.\\n\\nRepeat note for this bundle: the previous attempt (rrn-7d33ba9fc274421f) stopped without a draft because building the CLI and creating scratch copies hit a read-only filesystem. That is a known limit of this review sandbox. Earlier rounds handled it by running the focused Go tests, which passed here before (`go test ./internal/cli -run 'Carry|ChangedScope|Validate|Material'`, `go vet`), and by citing the sealed canonical result for the `validate` and `assess` tools with the limitation stated in each disposition. Please do the same instead of stopping: give your judgment on the code and record every tool limitation honestly in the draft.\\n\\nRound 16 notes: round 15 (rrn-16091dd78a12cc0b) found N43 and N45, and N44 restated F2.\\n- N43: `movementWitness` records the reflog lengths of HEAD and of every checked-out submodule at the pin and at the end. They must match and be readable.\\n- N45: a cancelled context, or any cancelled check, sets the run-level `cancelled`, clears `material_clean` and is refused as a base.\\nThe tests are `TestValidateSubmoduleMovingAndReturningIsNotClean` and `TestCarryRefusesABaseCancelledAtRunLevel`. If building or scratch creation is read-only here, run the focused Go tests and cite the sealed canonical result rather than stopping. Account for R15-N43..R15-N45 and report every remaining issue in this round.\\n\\nRound 17 notes: round 16 (rrn-328651cf23a32126) found N46–N48, and F2 was restated.\\n- N46: `planCarry` refuses when the working `module-metadata.json` differs from HEAD's.\\n- N47: `finalizeCancellation` clears `material_clean` and makes every binding unavailable.\\n- N48: `validationMaterialClean` fails when a submodule has nested submodules.\\nThe tests are `TestCarryRefusesWorkingMetadataThatDiffersFromHead`, `TestCancellationMakesBindingsUnavailable` and `TestValidateNestedSubmodulesAreNotClean`. If building or scratch creation is read-only, run the focused Go tests and cite the sealed canonical result rather than stopping. Account for R16-N46..R16-N48 and report every remaining issue in this round.\\n\\nRepeat note for this bundle: the previous attempt (rrn-6741de0e146e3777) approved, but its conclusion was refused for format. The preflight said: \\\"finding id \\\\\\\"R17-N49\\\\\\\" is not a unique identifier without a round prefix\\\". A finding you report in `findings` must use a new unprefixed ID that no earlier round used, for example `N50`. The round-prefixed IDs belong only in `prior_findings`, for findings listed by the brief. Judge the subject independently; the format is the only reason for this repeat.\\n\",\n.pose/review-runs/rrn-c2966cb8e4ff258c.json:106:  \"output\": \"decision: changes-requested\\n\\nAll five prior findings are fixed. Two new medium blockers remain:\\n\\n- **N1 — Lost failure diagnostics**, [artifact_integrity.go:246](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-3082417445/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/cli/artifact_integrity.go:246): streamed patch failures omit Git’s stderr from collection-gap messages.\\n- **N2 — Retained-memory budget bypass**, [governance_read_view_stream.go:143](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-3082417445/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view_stream.go:143): warning text retained in `errText` is charged to neither retained-input nor metadata capacity.\\n\\nThe streamed tests passed with `-race`; artifact-check and surface-check passed. Full validation uses the supplied sealed evidence. The repository remains unchanged.\\n\\nRules applied: pose-review workflow, backend-go, security, documentation-style, and delivery-evidence. Reviewed bundle: `rvb-5364a11b6d7e041d`, digest `sha256:5364a11b6d7e041dcb42642925dba23411347dec8f6814cdb4d92bef865a451e`.\\n\\n```pose-draft\\n{\\n  \\\"schema\\\": \\\"pose.review.draft/v1\\\",\\n  \\\"decision\\\": \\\"changes-requested\\\",\\n  \\\"findings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"N1\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"medium\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"blocker\\\",\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/artifact_integrity.go\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": 246,\\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"The governed streamed-patch path returns StreamGovernanceRawHistoryGitIn's error directly, removing the stderr enrichment previously supplied by gitOutputBoundedIn. runGovernanceGitStreamContext attaches stderr to exec.ExitError, but GitSnapshotError.Error formats only the exit error, so a failed git show becomes 'Git snapshot unavailable (show ...): exit status 128'. collectArtifactGraphInputsWithGapsIn stores only err.Error() at line 586, permanently losing the missing-object, permission or other forensic cause. Preserve bounded stderr in the reported collection-gap error while preserving ErrGitUnknown, and cover failure of the streamed show command. The existing collection-gaps regression passes but injects failure into diff-tree, so it does not cover this new path.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"N2\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"medium\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"blocker\\\",\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view_stream.go\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": 143,\\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"A successful Git command with stderr becomes a GitSnapshotError containing up to 64 KiB of warning text at lines 243-248. stream then retains the entire error string in each observation's errText, while reserveRecord charges only root/key/producer plus 128 bytes and reserveStreamed charges only stdout. These retained strings therefore bypass both the 512 MiB retained-input budget and the 16 MiB metadata budget. Thousands of distinct warning-producing reads can retain hundreds of MiB beyond the declared limits while their counters remain below capacity. A read-only native-Git probe using core.attributesFile=/dev/stdin with invalid attribute entries exited 0 and emitted 258893 stderr bytes, establishing that this path does not require a fake Git executable. Charge retained diagnostics to the appropriate shared budget before storing them, or retain only an error digest with separately budgeted diagnostic context; add a regression for repeated warning-producing observations.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"prior_findings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R1-F1\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"governance_read_view_stream.go:151-200 now audits every streamed observation without a configuration-based skip. TestTheStreamedAuditStreamsEveryReadAgain changes .git/info/attributes and verifies detection; passed under go test -race ./internal/pose ./internal/cli -run Streamed -count=1.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R1-F2\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"governance_read_view_stream.go:130-145 performs the post-run lookup, comparison and first insertion under state.mu. TestConcurrentFirstStreamedReadsAreCompared passed with the race detector and requires one differing concurrent read to fail.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R1-F3\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"governance_read_view_stream.go:107-146 no longer associates streamed observations with effectiveGitConfig; lines 180-200 rerun every observation. Spec decision D2 explicitly rejects configuration-based skipping.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R1-F4\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"The streamed audit no longer executes git config. governance_read_view_stream.go:182-189 restores the saved deadline before the remaining patch audit. The race-enabled streamed and existing caller-cancellation tests passed.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R1-F5\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\".pose/specs/2026-11-14-pose-read-view-streamed-object-digests.md:150 records both operation boundaries: 21758777 retained bytes and zero streaming for the first operation; 32163095 retained bytes, 1263513529 streamed bytes and 522736985 audit-streamed bytes for the second. It identifies temporary counter instrumentation and distinguishes the successful run from the Git-shim measurement. This review verified the record, not a fresh full-corpus reproduction.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"sweep\\\": \\\"Swept the supplied implementation range, spec R1-R6 and decisions D1/D2, ADR D11, validation-matrix registration, operation root routing, lifecycle joining, concurrent first and repeated reads, capture/audit budgets, deadline restoration, raw-history environment, error propagation, change-set hash ordering, fallback range behavior, tests, and English/Portuguese runtime and scaffold documentation. Checked prior governance knowledge. Independently ran streamed tests with -race, additional existing cancellation and shared-budget tests with -race, the collection-gaps regression, artifact-check, surface-check, suggest-review and recurrence-check. Probed native Git's warning-producing attributes path without repository writes. Full-suite evidence is reused from the sealed bundle; assessment producers were not rerun because they persist repository artifacts. git status remained clean. No additional established defects were found.\\\",\\n  \\\"criteria\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assumption-integrity\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/read-view-streamed-object-digests-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Examined immutable-object versus mutable-rendering assumptions, concurrent observation initialization, budget separation and corpus measurements. Rendering stability is now checked by rerunning rather than assumed from configuration. Tests independently verified the corrected paths. Corpus byte-equivalence and counters remain documented implementer measurements rather than independently reproduced corpus results. Continued history-proportional I/O is explicitly scoped and tracked.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-concurrency\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/read-view-streamed-object-digests-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Inspected state.mu, budgetMu, target.begin/end and audit joining. Streamed tests and existing cancellation/shared-budget tests passed with the race detector; post-run comparison now covers concurrent first observations.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-contracts\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/read-view-streamed-object-digests-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The patch bytes and their ordering into SHA-256 remain unchanged. No persisted change-set, CLI or MCP schema is migrated.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-input-errors\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N1\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-integration-impact\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/read-view-streamed-object-digests-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Traced production change-set collection through the stream helper and operation-owned Git state; inspected native fallback and unchanged explicit-range behavior. Surface-check found one target and no findings.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-observability\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N1\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"compatibility\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/read-view-streamed-object-digests-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Compared old and new digest construction and the equivalence fixture, including binary content. Public file, CLI and MCP schemas remain compatible; normal successful reads preserve change-set IDs.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"correctness\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N2\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"design-causality\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-338e543875a0589e\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"D1 directly addresses retained commit-patch growth by hashing streamed bytes while retaining digest and length. D2 restores complete audit reruns because object identity does not establish rendering purity. This preserves digest compatibility without persistent caching or a new digest formula.\\\",\\n      \\\"mappings\\\": [\\n        {\\n          \\\"delta\\\": \\\"SD-048277a6\\\",\\n          \\\"basis\\\": \\\"R5\\\",\\n          \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"mapped\\\",\\n          \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"ADR amendment D11 supersedes D10 and restores the captured-input ceiling to 512 MiB, documenting separate stream budgets and measured retention as R5 requires.\\\"\\n        }\\n      ]\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"documentation\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N2\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"English and Portuguese budget text matches its scaffold copies, and ADR D11 matches the intended implementation. The claimed retained limits are not enforced for stored warning text.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"operability\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N1\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"requirements\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N2\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"R1/R3/R4 have relevant streamed and equivalence tests; R6 measurements are now recorded. The retained diagnostic allocation bypass undermines the budget separation and restoration required by R2/R5.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"scope\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-338e543875a0589e\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Examined the declared artifacts and implementation diff. Changes remain confined to streamed hash-only Git reads, change-set integration, budget restoration, supporting tests, validation registration and synchronized documentation.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"security\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N2\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Raw-history environment sanitization and authorized-root checks are preserved, but repository-controlled Git warnings can allocate retained strings outside the shared memory limits.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"solution-proportionality\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-338e543875a0589e\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Compared streaming against raising capacity, changing digest identity and introducing persistent caching. Streaming is the smallest compatible structural solution; unconditional audit reruns preserve the prior correctness model without speculative dependency tracking. Persistent caching or versioned digest storage would need a separate decision if measured I/O becomes unacceptable. The implementation still needs the two reported corrections.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"tools\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"artifact-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-read-view-streamed-object-digests --strict\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Executed independently; exit 0. Output included existing provenance warnings.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-design\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-338e543875a0589e\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Inspected the sealed structural assessment and independently mapped the ADR delta; did not rerun an assessment producer in the read-only review.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-discover\\\",\\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Selected component rules and inspected the source directly. Discovery persists assessment artifacts, contrary to the no-repository-changes boundary.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-integrate\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/read-view-streamed-object-digests-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Used sealed integration evidence plus direct producer/consumer inspection and local race-enabled tests; did not rerun the persisting assessment producer.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-tech-debt\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:git diff d724738b53a8fe94ec9b2eb749a5242958f06d4a c6ec137582ad69f001b47d9b2cbf36539b899441 -- pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view.go pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view_git.go pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view_stream.go pose-mcp/internal/cli/artifact_integrity.go\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Manually inspected the changed code and documented I/O follow-up. Did not run the assessment producer because repository writes are prohibited.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"closeout-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:pose context --task spec:pose-read-view-streamed-object-digests --json\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Completion gate requires the review conclusion to be recorded first; this review only returns a draft and requests changes.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"review-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:pose context --task spec:pose-read-view-streamed-object-digests --json\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Requires the resulting attestation; recording one is explicitly outside this review's boundary.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"suggest-review\\\",\\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Executed; selected backend-go, security and documentation-style rules.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"surface-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/read-view-streamed-object-digests-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Independently ran pose surface-check --spec pose-read-view-streamed-object-digests --strict: exit 0, one target, 214 results, zero findings.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"validate\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Disposition uses the supplied sealed successful validation producer, not a claimed local full-suite rerun. Independently reran the relevant streamed tests with -race and the existing collection-gap regression.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"validate\\\",\\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/read-view-streamed-object-digests-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Uses the module's supplied sealed validation evidence. Local go test -race ./internal/pose ./internal/cli -run Streamed -count=1 passed; additional race-enabled cancellation and shared-budget tests also passed. Passing fixtures do not cover N1 or N2.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\\n```\",\n.pose/review-runs/rrn-36680493b6fa0955.json:106:  \"output\": \"decision: approved\\n\\nNo new defects established. R6-F24 is fixed by the version whitelist and regression test.\\n\\nReviewed the feature under the review workflow and backend-go, security, documentation-style, and delivery-evidence rules. No repository changes or attestation were made. Tests were assessed from their source and sealed evidence.\\n\\nBoth read-only gate reruns exited successfully. The artifact rerun resolved a different change-set head, so I used the supplied exact-range artifact output for subject attribution.\\n\\n```pose-draft\\n{\\n  \\\"schema\\\": \\\"pose.review.draft/v1\\\",\\n  \\\"decision\\\": \\\"approved\\\",\\n  \\\"findings\\\": [],\\n  \\\"prior_findings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R6-F24\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/doctor_commit_graph.go:167-176 accepts only -1, 1 and 2 and names unsupported values. doctor.go:375 routes that result to git.commit-graph-reads at warn without a fix. doctor_commit_graph_test.go:406-428 verifies version 3 produces that warning and no graph rewrite finding. A read-only Git 2.56 trace probe also confirmed version 3 consults no filters.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"sweep\\\": \\\"Swept all six declared changed paths against R1-R4 and D1, including doctor production dispatch, remediation classification and recheck, Git execution and environment isolation, trace parsing, temporary-file cleanup, configuration precedence, split and alternate graphs, literal paths, shallow/unborn/empty repositories, missing objects without fetching, successful-command warnings, all new regression tests, both full-history CI jobs, validation-matrix history and the start record. Inspected supplied exact-range artifact and surface outputs, sealed validation results and applicable rules. No edits, builds, writing assessments or attestation were performed.\\\",\\n  \\\"criteria\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assumption-integrity\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/doctor-recommends-the-commit-graph-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Examined real-Git fixtures and independently probed version-dependent Bloom statistics. Git graph selection and unsupported-version behavior have evidence. The 500-commit threshold rests on D1's recorded measurements, which I did not rebenchmark. Trace2 event stability remains an explicitly documented design risk; the integration test detects incompatible changes.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-concurrency\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The production path is synchronous and introduces no workers or shared mutable runtime state. Each probe creates its own private trace file and defers removal. Threshold-changing tests restore the value and do not run in parallel.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-contracts\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/doctor-recommends-the-commit-graph-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The new check uses the existing doctor finding schema and remediation registry. CLI composition is exercised through Main; no MCP, event or public file schema changes.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-input-errors\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/doctor-recommends-the-commit-graph-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Inspected non-repository, unborn, shallow, empty-tree, unreadable-history, malformed-graph, disabled-read and unsupported-version paths. Failures retain command context and bounded Git stderr; filenames are passed as literal pathspecs.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-integration-impact\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/doctor-recommends-the-commit-graph-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Verified composition through doctor diagnostics, the existing fix registry and post-fix recheck. Both full-history CI jobs write the graph before their gates.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-observability\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/doctor-recommends-the-commit-graph-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Failures identify the failed operation, bound Git diagnostic text and pass through existing secret-shaped-content redaction. Configuration warnings name the setting that prevents remediation.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"compatibility\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/doctor-recommends-the-commit-graph-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Examined doctor schema version 2, finding classification and fix dispatch. Checks are additive, existing output fields remain unchanged, and the repair is confined to Git's commit-graph maintenance command.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"correctness\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/doctor-recommends-the-commit-graph-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Read the positive and negative real-repository tests, including the new unsupported-version regression. Checked production branches, effective repair arguments and configuration precedence against R1-R4.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"design-causality\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-6c06a1c768240be8\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"D1 places repository maintenance in the existing explicit doctor repair flow, addressing repeated history walks while preserving governance reads. Asking Git through trace2 follows the graph Git actually loads and avoids duplicating alternate and split-graph selection logic. The three material metadata facts broaden regression selection without weakening check severity or evidence class.\\\",\\n      \\\"mappings\\\": [\\n        {\\n          \\\"delta\\\": \\\"SD-28db7861\\\",\\n          \\\"basis\\\": \\\"R3\\\",\\n          \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"mapped\\\",\\n          \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Commit ac7610d7 broadens the required integration selector to TestDoctorCommitGraph, covering shallow and empty histories, no-fetch diagnostics, configuration precedence and successful-command warnings.\\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"delta\\\": \\\"SD-9fc0fe4e\\\",\\n          \\\"basis\\\": \\\"R3\\\",\\n          \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"mapped\\\",\\n          \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Commit 5c1c5658 adds the unreadable-history regression to the required integration selector so failed state reads cannot silently pass.\\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"delta\\\": \\\"SD-d29398e6\\\",\\n          \\\"basis\\\": \\\"R3\\\",\\n          \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"mapped\\\",\\n          \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Commit 2e30bb53 adds unborn-versus-broken, literal-path and disabled-read regressions to the required integration selector.\\\"\\n        }\\n      ]\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"documentation\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/doctor-recommends-the-commit-graph-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Examined the spec, requirement trace, operator messages, repair description and CI comments. The documented effective repair includes --max-new-filters=-1 and matches the command executed. No scaffold or public schema update is required.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"operability\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/doctor-recommends-the-commit-graph-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Missing graphs receive an executable remediation command; disabled reads receive a warning naming the configuration rather than an ineffective repair. Read failures preserve bounded diagnostic context, and existing doctor logic rechecks applied fixes.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"requirements\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/doctor-recommends-the-commit-graph-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"R1-R3 are covered by real-Git diagnostic and repair tests, including negative paths and the prior finding's regression. R4 is satisfied by the two graph-writing steps immediately after full-history checkout and before CI gates.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"scope\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-6c06a1c768240be8\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The declared implementation delivers the doctor check, explicit repair, CI preparation and permanent validation required by the spec. The start record is governance metadata. Separately attributed work visible in the aggregate commit range was distinguished from this scope's declared artifacts.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"security\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/doctor-recommends-the-commit-graph-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Examined fixed command arguments, RawHistoryGit environment isolation, literal pathspec handling, disabled lazy fetching, private trace creation and existing diagnostic redaction. No credentials, new dependencies or remote authority are introduced.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"solution-proportionality\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-6c06a1c768240be8\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Compared D1's doctor repair with documentation alone, implicit governance writes and custom graph parsing. The existing repair registry plus a Git-owned probe is sufficient without a background service or persistence layer. Loss of compatible trace2 Bloom statistics would invalidate the probe choice and require revision.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"tools\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"artifact-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-doctor-recommends-the-commit-graph --strict\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Executed read-only and exited 0 with warning-level provenance diagnostics. The rerun resolved a different change-set head, so exact sealed-subject attribution was checked against /var/tmp/closeout/ac-dc.out, which names cs-478564f2eee3 and the requested base/head.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-design\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-6c06a1c768240be8\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Did not invoke the assessment producer under the no-write boundary. Used sealed structural evidence and independently traced each material matrix delta to its commit and requirement.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-discover\\\",\\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Assessment producers were excluded by the read-only review boundary. Resolved the component and examined its code and sealed validation evidence.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-integrate\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/doctor-recommends-the-commit-graph-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Did not run a writing assessment. Independently inspected production composition and real-Git integration tests; no public inter-module schema changed.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-tech-debt\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Did not invoke the writing assessment producer. Independently searched the new implementation and tests for TODO, FIXME, stub and panic markers and inspected documented residual risks.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"closeout-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:pose context --task spec:pose-doctor-recommends-the-commit-graph --json\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Completion-only gate must follow POSE's recording and verification of this conclusion. This independent review does not record an attestation.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"review-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:pose context --task spec:pose-doctor-recommends-the-commit-graph --json\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"A verified review conclusion cannot be checked before POSE records it.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"suggest-review\\\",\\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Executed successfully and applied its backend-go, security and documentation-style rule selection.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"surface-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/doctor-recommends-the-commit-graph-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The read-only strict rerun exited 0 with one target, 233 results and zero findings. Also inspected /var/tmp/closeout/sc-dc.out and independently checked doctor production reachability.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"validate\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/doctor-recommends-the-commit-graph-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Used the supplied sealed strict pipeline evidence under the read-only boundary. The validation report records 233 executed checks, all passing, with no failures, errors or skips. No build or test rerun was attempted.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"validate\\\",\\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Used sealed module build, unit and integration evidence and independently read the package regression tests, including unsupported changedPathsVersion coverage.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\\n```\",\n.pose/review-runs/rrn-c5171f8ff89f3ebb.json:106:  \"output\": \"decision: changes-requested\\n\\nF1 — **medium, blocker** — [governance_read_view_stream.go:230](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-2375405296/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view_stream.go:230): the streaming governance runner still inherits `LC_ALL` and `LANGUAGE`. `StreamGovernanceRawHistoryGitIn`, used by artifact-integrity reads and their final audits, bypasses the changed captured-output runner. Consequently, R1’s requirement that **every** governance Git command force both variables to `C` remains unmet. Apply the locale override to this runner and cover both execution paths.\\n\\nThe pt_BR regression test passed without skipping. The coordinator test and six streaming tests also passed; they do not detect this missing override. No repository files were changed.\\n\\nRules applied: bugfix review workflow, backend Go, security, documentation style, and delivery evidence. Reviewed bundle: `rvb-e2837d870a9dbb3a`, digest `sha256:e2837d870a9dbb3a2570e54da818ca81f3a07a942416514fc4a781649dded3ae`.\\n\\nGate limitation: the installed artifact check reported a different change-set head; its result does not verify this sealed subject. The surface-check attempt has not returned a usable result. Building the checkout’s CLI was blocked by the read-only filesystem. These limitations are recorded below without treating them as implementation defects.\\n\\n```pose-draft\\n{\\n  \\\"schema\\\": \\\"pose.review.draft/v1\\\",\\n  \\\"decision\\\": \\\"changes-requested\\\",\\n  \\\"findings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"F1\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"medium\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"blocker\\\",\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view_stream.go\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": 230,\\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"R1 requires every Git command run by the governance read view to set LC_ALL=C and LANGUAGE=C, but runGovernanceGitStreamContext appends only GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=0. gitCommandContext preserves inherited locale variables. StreamGovernanceRawHistoryGitIn reaches this runner for both streamed observations and their final audits, and internal/cli/artifact_integrity.go:243 uses it in production. Thus streamed governance failures remain translated under pt_BR even though captured reads are now untranslated. Add both locale overrides to the streaming runner and regression coverage for both runner paths; the new coordinator test exercises only the captured path.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"criteria\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assumption-integrity\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/governance-git-reads-untranslated-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Examined R1, D1, environment construction, both governance runners and the locale probe. The appended overrides work for captured reads, and the pt_BR test passed without skipping locally. The assumption that the changed runner covers every governance command is disproved by F1. The documented skip on machines without Git translations remains an explicit coverage limitation.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-concurrency\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/read-view-streamed-object-digests-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The change modifies per-command environment slices, not process-global state. Context cancellation, WaitDelay, synchronized output admission and lifecycle handling remain intact. Local coordinator and concurrent streaming tests passed.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-contracts\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/cli-mcp-operation-results-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"No public API, event, file schema or MCP signature changes. Existing error wrappers and output bounds are preserved.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-input-errors\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/governance-read-view-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Inspected the captured runner's byte admission, ExitError stderr propagation, GitSnapshotError wrapping and nonempty-stderr handling. The locale override preserves these bounded error paths.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-integration-impact\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/check-shares-the-federated-material-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Module discovery still consumes the same captured Git interface. The coordinator test passed locally under pt_BR and under the ordinary environment.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-observability\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/typed-diagnostics-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Returned operation context, bounded stderr and typed error propagation remain intact. No new logging or sensitive environment disclosure is introduced.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"compatibility\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/cli-mcp-operation-results-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Examined the complete implementation diff and callers. Public CLI, MCP and persisted contracts are unchanged; the intended behavioral change is internal Git diagnostic normalization.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"correctness\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"F1\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"design-causality\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-58391a9fb0946b4e\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"D1 selects locale normalization rather than enumerating Git translations. The captured runner's appended C overrides directly address module_discovery.go:402's English stderr classification and follow the existing untranslated-reader design. The design is causally appropriate, but its implementation omits the streaming path as reported in F1. No structural fact IDs were supplied in the brief.\\\",\\n      \\\"mappings\\\": []\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"documentation\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/governance-git-reads-untranslated-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Examined the scope spec, runtime comment and validation-matrix entry. The declared command matches the regression tests, and the spec explicitly documents skipping where Git lacks pt_BR translations. No operational command or scaffold contract changes require migration.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"operability\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/typed-diagnostics-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Examined module discovery's unknown-context diagnostic and the runner's bounded GitSnapshotError handling. Diagnostic context remains available and the captured non-repository failure is now recognized under pt_BR.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"requirements\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"F1\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"scope\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"F1\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"security\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/governance-read-view-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Examined changed code and adjacent execution boundaries. Fixed locale values introduce no shell interpolation, dependencies or new authority. Raw-history protections, optional-lock suppression and output budgets remain intact. No secrets were found in the changed artifacts.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"solution-proportionality\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-58391a9fb0946b4e\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"A local environment override is the smallest sufficient mechanism and avoids maintaining translated diagnostic dictionaries or changing unrelated Git commands. No speculative abstraction is added. Completing the same override in the streaming runner is sufficient for F1. This choice would need reconsideration if governance intentionally consumed locale-dependent presentation output.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"tools\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"artifact-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"failed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-governance-git-reads-untranslated --strict\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Executed, but the installed binary reported change-set head 967cb9415e461a277a6de7bfea58a56110110d83 rather than the supplied acb136cbfdcfbdb8e424f0f709418dea0d187937 subject. It therefore did not establish artifact assurance for this review.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-design\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-58391a9fb0946b4e\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Reviewed the sealed design evidence and inspected both execution paths directly. Did not rerun assessments that could write repository state.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-discover\\\",\\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"No component rediscovery was needed for the bounded environment change; avoided assessment writes under the read-only review boundary.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-integrate\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/governance-read-view-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"No public inter-module contract changed. Inspected provider-consumer paths and sealed integration evidence instead of running a state-writing assessment.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-tech-debt\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Inspected the changed code and adjacent paths for debt markers; the patch adds none. Did not run an assessment that writes repository state.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"closeout-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Completion check requires the recorded review conclusion and subsequent closeout state; no attestation was recorded during this review.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"review-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Requires POSE to record this review conclusion first. Recording an attestation is outside the authorized review.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"suggest-review\\\",\\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Executed and applied the selected backend-go, security and documentation-style rules.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"surface-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Started pose surface-check --spec pose-governance-git-reads-untranslated --strict, but no completed usable result was available. The installed gate's preceding artifact result selected an unexpected subject, so surface assurance cannot be claimed.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"validate\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/governance-git-reads-untranslated-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Disposed from the supplied sealed strict-validation producer and its listed passing results. No full local rerun was attempted under the read-only review environment. Independently reran the locale regression, coordinator and streaming tests successfully.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"validate\\\",\\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Disposed from the sealed pose-mcp validation results, including unit, build and integration evidence. Local targeted Go test runs finished successfully without interruption.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\\n```\",\n.pose/review-runs/rrn-310cb38b6bc9840e.json:86:  \"brief_notes\": \"Review of spec pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit, implemented by Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic). The ADR `.pose/adr/2026-11-12-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-and-benefit.md` is Accepted; judge the implementation against it and the spec, not the decision itself.\\n\\nMechanism. Review policy schema 5 adds `milestone_review_required` / `roadmap_review_required` (`never|when-justified|always`), validated in `parseReviewPolicy` via `validateCloseoutReviewPolicyKeys` (closeout_review_policy.go). One evaluator `evaluateCloseoutReview` (closeout-review@1): canonical members `xref:\\u003cproject\\u003e/spec:\\u003cslug\\u003e` (aliases, verified redirects, federated resolver, unknown = diagnostic, never zero) and ADR associations (closeout_adr_associations.go: roadmap `adrs:`, ADR `roadmaps:`, local Markdown links both ways; malformed/missing/unreadable = unknown). `closeoutReviewGate` is the single entry for readers: receipt first, roadmap done before adoption = legacy (nil decision), else evaluate + `protectCloseoutDecision` (baseline policy at the change set base when the scope changes the review contract); exemption only when not required AND no review recorded on the scope (`scopeReviewRecorded`, unreadable counts as recorded). Consumers: `reviewCheck` (review_closeout.go, Required=false + ApprovalOrigin), `proportionalReviewVerification` (review_bundle.go; under adoption the legacy singleton inheritance and `unreviewed_milestones` are skipped), `getCloseoutState` (CloseRequired, receipt, terminal only with receipt, new diagnostics), `ReachedMilestones`/`RoadmapsReachedBy`/`roadmapReachedApartFrom` (roadmaps.go), `milestoneReachedObligations`, `ReviewPlan.CloseoutReview` (out of the digest), doctor (`CloseoutReviewsOwed`), setup and `pose adopt` (capability_catalog.go `closeoutReviewPolicyCatalogEntry`, `SetCloseoutReviewPolicy`; refs/transfer adopt/retire no longer lower schema 5). CLI close (cli/review_closeout.go `closeoutReceiptPreflight`, `publishCloseoutReceipt`): milestone and roadmap close publish an immutable receipt (closeout_receipt.go, ExpectAbsent publish, strict parse); a done roadmap without receipt is completed by a new close. `milestoneMember` now maps `spec:\\u003cslug\\u003e` to its slug (was `spec:spec:\\u003cslug\\u003e` in closeout state). Existing tests changed on purpose: catalog lists, schema after adopt (fresh install is now schema 5), progressive_review fixtures that force schema 2, and the previous-release compatibility test (a fresh install is refused by v7.4.0 by its schema, by ADR design; an updated legacy instance stays readable).\\n\\nPlease do an exhaustive sweep in this round and report ALL findings together, classified blocker vs follow-up. Inventory every entry point that answers \\\"is this aggregate scope approved / closed / reached\\\" (CLI close, closeout-check, review-check, review verify, review-plan, attention/obligations, reached, nextCloses, roadmap check, MCP closeout state, federated acceptance, doctor) and check each one reads the same gate, cannot launder a recorded rejection under `never`, cannot let `always` be weakened by inheritance or `unreviewed_milestones`, and never treats an unknown member/association as an exemption. Also check: receipts are never overwritten nor fabricated for history; `pose update` never adopts; no schema-5 downgrade path; the recovery path for a roadmap done without receipt cannot close a scope whose review is required and unapproved.\\n\\nKnown pre-existing state: `pose check --strict` reports 19 delivery-contract errors of other specs (runtime worktree, common-domain handoff, governance performance, bounded graph caches), identical line by line on the base commit 956153f1; they are follow-up F4, not this spec.\\n\\nRequired tools: run `pose artifact-check --spec pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit --strict` and `pose surface-check --spec pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit --strict`; declare each `passed` only after running it (evidence `command:\\u003cthe command\\u003e`, rationale quoting its result). The surface-check disposition must cite both an `integration:` and a `reachability:` sealed evidence id. Cite sealed `unit:`/`integration:` ids for criteria, never `SD-…` structural facts or requirement ids. Send each shell command alone in its own call (no pipes, `;`, `\\u0026\\u0026`, redirects). `validate` of a component with registered checks is `passed` with the sealed run's evidence; `review-check` and `closeout-check` are `deferred`. New findings have bare ids (F1, F2 …); follow-ups carry `action`, `owner`, `review_by`; only low-severity risks may be accepted.\\n\\nRound 13. The engine refused your round-12 run rrn-da6e5287b19f2087 because its draft cited R11-N37: a refused run opens no findings, so N37 … N41 are not open findings of this scope and must NOT appear in `prior_findings`; account in `prior_findings` exactly for the findings the brief lists as open (round-10 run rrn-8b1997980713c10a: R9-N34 … R9-N36, plus any earlier partial the brief shows), each with whether it stands. Report the state of N38 … N41 as new findings only if they still stand. Since round 12: N38 under the adopted policy `unreviewed_milestones` no longer suppresses a child's terminal failure, legacy-attempt approval included; N39 `adrs:`/`roadmaps:` are read strictly from the raw frontmatter (duplicate key, key without value, outside a list or with an empty item is unknown; explicit `[]` declares none); N40 links in fenced code, inline code or comments are not associations; N41 the D10 amendment ends without a trailing blank line. Earlier in this cycle: doctor's closeout diagnostic uses the bound store (cliGovernedStore), and the governance read view captured-input budget is 1 GiB by measured amendment D10 of ADR governance-reads-use-bounded-operation-scoped-views, with follow-up F5. A finding object accepts exactly `id`, `severity`, `disposition`, `file`, `line`, `summary`, and for an accepted follow-up `action`, `owner`, `review_by`; put any rationale inside `summary`. Do NOT run `pose assess`, `pose state`, `pose index` or anything else that writes under `.pose/`; dispose assess-* tools from the sealed evidence and the code. Leave the worktree as you found it. Sweep the whole surface again and report every remaining finding in one pass, classified blocker vs follow-up; a remote variant of a threat the ADR does not promise to defend is a follow-up, and so is a pre-existing gap of the federation or transfer engine that this spec did not introduce and does not claim to close.\\n\",\n.pose/review-runs/rrn-310cb38b6bc9840e.json:106:  \"output\": \"decision: changes-requested\\n\\nFour medium blockers remain: historical-roadmap misclassification, an invalid template default, incorrect Markdown fence handling, and whitespace-sensitive association keys. R11-N39 is partial; the other three prior findings are fixed.\\n\\nFocused tests, artifact-check, surface-check, and diff hygiene passed. Both full validation reruns failed: the module run encountered HTTP 403 fetching published releases; the global run also exceeded its 600-second unit-test limit. Extra Go probes could not start in the read-only sandbox. The findings below rest on source traces.\\n\\nApplied the review workflow and backend-go, security, documentation-style, delivery-evidence, and knowledge-governance rules. The repository remains unchanged; no attestation was recorded.\\n\\n```pose-draft\\n{\\n  \\\"schema\\\": \\\"pose.review.draft/v1\\\",\\n  \\\"decision\\\": \\\"changes-requested\\\",\\n  \\\"findings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"N42\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"medium\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"blocker\\\",\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_review_policy.go\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": 720,\\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"Require evidence that a roadmap actually closed before adoption before classifying it as historical. closeoutScopeHistorical accepts the current legacy enabled/cutoff shortcut or any recorded bundle approval, without checking whether that bundle sealed CloseoutReview. A roadmap approved under schema 5 and subsequently marked done without a receipt therefore becomes historical: closeoutReviewGate returns nil, getCloseoutState does not require a receipt, and CLI close can report already-satisfied. The enabled=false branch can also suppress adopted always and recorded negative reviews on a done roadmap. This violates R2/R4/R5 and the prospective-history contract. Apply the sealed pre-adoption-plan distinction used by milestoneClosedBeforeAdoption and cover both post-adoption approval and disabled-policy cases.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"N43\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"medium\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"blocker\\\",\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\".pose/templates/roadmap.md\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": 6,\\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"Emit a valid optional association default. The new template writes adrs: followed only by an inline explanatory comment; the distributed scaffold has the same line. cmdNewRoadmap preserves it, but associationList reads the raw comment as the value and rejects it as outside a list. Filling the required roadmap fields while leaving this optional field untouched consequently makes when-justified evaluation unknown and prevents close. Omit the optional declaration or emit a parseable empty list with its explanation on a separate comment line, and exercise the generated template through the evaluator.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"N44\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"medium\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"blocker\\\",\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_adr_associations.go\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": 88,\\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"Preserve the complete Markdown fence delimiter and validate its closing syntax. markdownWithoutCode truncates every opener to three characters. For valid Markdown consisting of an opening four-backtick fence, a literal three-backtick line inside it, example text, the closing four-backtick fence, and then a real ADR link, the three-backtick line prematurely closes this filter's fence and the real closing delimiter opens another one. The actual association is discarded without a diagnostic. A two-member roadmap whose sole ADR association is that link consequently receives Known=true and Required=false under when-justified, violating R3. Cover longer fences and real links following them.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"N45\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"medium\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"blocker\\\",\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_adr_associations.go\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": 112,\\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"Normalize association keys consistently with SplitFrontmatter before tracking their presence and duplicates. SplitFrontmatter splits at the colon and trims the key, whereas associationList recognizes only a literal unindented key followed immediately by a colon. Thus adrs : [adr:decision.md], or the equivalent roadmaps declaration, is silently absent here despite being recognized by the repository's frontmatter reader. With two canonical members and no other association, when-justified grants an exemption without a diagnostic. Differently spaced duplicate keys also escape duplicate detection. This is the remaining R11-N39 gap: recognize normalized keys and reject ambiguity before proving association absence.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"prior_findings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R11-N38\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_closeout.go:2747 restricts the declaredUnreviewed exception to !closeoutAdopted. go test ./internal/pose -run '^TestCloseoutReviewPolicyRoundTwelve$' -count=1 -v passed, including the legacy-attempt child-rejection subtest without skipping.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R11-N39\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"partial\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_adr_associations.go:119 rejects repeated literal keys; lines 123-137 reject missing values, nonlists and empty items. RoundTwelve association-declaration tests passed. However line 112 does not normalize keys as SplitFrontmatter does at pose-mcp/internal/pose/spec.go:593, leaving the whitespace and duplicate-key bypass reported as N45.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R11-N40\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_adr_associations.go:45 applies markdownWithoutCode. The RoundTwelve fenced, tilde, inline-code and comment regression cases all passed. N44 reports a distinct undercount caused by longer fence delimiters.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R11-N41\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"git diff --check 8e3009b2c7305cd94500009875ddc1b7880d8331 38e6d16ae90f6e8266c56d2e12b2465269fdb4ac exited 0 with no output.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"sweep\\\": \\\"Reviewed R1-R7, decisions D1/D2, the accepted ADR, changed implementation, schemas, templates and English/Portuguese scaffold documentation. Traced policy parsing and adoption, protected baseline and mandatory-human enforcement, canonical members and transfers, both ADR association directions, voluntary-review vetoes, receipts and interrupted-close recovery. Swept CLI close, review-check, review verification, review-plan, closeout state/MCP, reached and nextCloses, roadmap acceptance checks, obligations/attention, readiness, portfolio dependencies, federated acceptance and doctor. Examined bounded reads, operation-scoped state, writer guards and immutable publication. Ran the full TestCloseoutReviewPolicy prefix across domain/CLI/MCP and the verbose RoundTwelve regressions; all passed. Ran artifact-check, surface-check, suggest-review, diff hygiene and both required validate commands. Validation reruns failed as detailed in tools. Additional in-memory Go probes could not start because the sandbox refused a temporary build directory; the new findings are established by source traces. A read-only Python trace confirmed the template value, key-normalization disagreement and longer-fence state transitions. Final git status was clean. No repository edits, attestation, contribution staging or upstream submission occurred.\\\",\\n  \\\"criteria\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assumption-integrity\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-41a20ef8e08d77e3\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Compared implementer claims with the spec, accepted ADR, source and executed checks. Distinguished sealed successful validation from the failed fresh reruns and source-established defects from the blocked extra probes. Historical classification is an implementation defect in N42, not an accepted assumption; no new residual risk is accepted.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-concurrency\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/writer-coordination-and-atomic-publication-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Inspected copied operation-local traversal state, root guards, publication revalidation, ExpectAbsent receipt publication and intent/status/receipt ordering. Found no new concurrent-access or overwrite defect within the participating-writer contract.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-contracts\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N43\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The shipped roadmap producer emits an optional field that the new runtime rejects.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-input-errors\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N45\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Recognized association-key spellings can disappear without an unknown-input diagnostic.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-integration-impact\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N42\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The incorrect historical classification propagates through closeout, reached/dependency projections and CLI close.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-observability\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N45\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The association declaration is silently treated as absent, so consumers receive a known exemption instead of actionable missing-knowledge context.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"compatibility\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N42\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The historical compatibility exception also admits closures made after adoption and can re-enable legacy shortcuts.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"correctness\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N42\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"An adopted roadmap can become terminal without its required explicit-close receipt.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"design-causality\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-41a20ef8e08d77e3\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The accepted design separates lifecycle close from aggregate review, uses deterministic canonical-member/ADR thresholds, and centralizes policy decisions while preserving member review and vetoes. Schema 5 makes adoption explicit and receipts provide a distinct terminal marker. The findings concern implementation gaps in these decisions.\\\",\\n      \\\"mappings\\\": [\\n        {\\n          \\\"delta\\\": \\\"SD-3ce6ee69\\\",\\n          \\\"basis\\\": \\\"D2\\\",\\n          \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"mapped\\\",\\n          \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The technical-plan reconciliation explicitly includes the measured D10 read-view capacity adjustment needed by governance reads supporting closeout. The amendment retains a finite bound and records the digest-only scaling follow-up.\\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"delta\\\": \\\"SD-607ff681\\\",\\n          \\\"basis\\\": \\\"R3\\\",\\n          \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"mapped\\\",\\n          \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The roadmap template adds the explicit ADR association metadata consumed by when-justified. Its invalid empty default is N43.\\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"delta\\\": \\\"SD-ec2d86f4\\\",\\n          \\\"basis\\\": \\\"R1\\\",\\n          \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"mapped\\\",\\n          \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The new accepted ADR records policy location, defaults, deterministic modes, explicit close, veto preservation and historical compatibility.\\\"\\n        }\\n      ]\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"documentation\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N43\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The installed and distributed roadmap templates disagree with the strict runtime declaration grammar.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"operability\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N43\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Leaving the documented optional association field untouched blocks a normally populated generated roadmap.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"requirements\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N44\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"R3 is not satisfied for valid Markdown containing longer fences; N42 also violates the explicit-close and prospective-history requirements.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"scope\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The reviewed artifacts implement the approved schema/evaluator/receipt/configuration/projection scope. The budget adjustment is explicitly reconciled in the technical plan and measured ADR amendment. No unrelated refactor or new global ADR identity/configuration framework was introduced.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"security\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N45\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Association-input normalization can lower an aggregate's review obligation without reporting unknown authority inputs. N42 supplies another route around the adopted gate.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"solution-proportionality\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-41a20ef8e08d77e3\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Compared the implementation with a boolean toggle or projection-only exemption. Neither supplies the required middle mode, explicit-close marker and historical semantics. Reusing the capability catalog, resolver and publication guards is proportionate; owner-local ADR inventory avoids speculative global discovery. Remote backlink requirements would invalidate that boundary. The 1 GiB adjustment buys measured headroom rather than scalability, as the ADR and spec follow-up explicitly disclose.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"tools\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"artifact-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit --strict\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Ran the required command; exit 0. It emitted warning orphan diagnostics for governed tracked paths without provenance claims, rather than failing the gate.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-design\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-41a20ef8e08d77e3\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Used sealed structural evidence and direct spec/ADR/source inspection without regenerating assessment artifacts.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-discover\\\",\\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Used the supplied component scope, sealed evidence and direct source inspection; did not refresh writing assessment state.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-integrate\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Avoided the writing assessment under the immutable-checkout boundary. Traced CLI, Store, MCP, dependency and federation consumers directly.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-tech-debt\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Inspected changed code, marker search results and the spec's recorded follow-ups without writing debt reports.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"closeout-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-terminal-verification-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Completion gate requires POSE to verify and record this review conclusion first.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"review-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-brief-conclusion-rules-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Deferred until POSE records the verified review conclusion; this reviewer must not attest.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"suggest-review\\\",\\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Exit 0; selected the review workflow and backend-go, security and documentation-style rules.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"surface-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Ran pose surface-check --spec pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit --strict; exit 0: surface.targets=1, surface.results=213, surface.findings=0. Sealed composition evidence: integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration. Sealed reachability evidence: reachability:pose-mcp/go/closeout-plan-reachability.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"validate\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"failed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:pose validate --strict\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Fresh invocation exited 1: 213 steps, 211 pass, 1 fail, 1 error. The pose-mcp unit check timed out after 600 seconds. This is not reported as a successful rerun; the bundle's sealed successful validation remains separate historical evidence.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"validate\\\",\\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"failed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:pose validate --strict --module pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Fresh invocation exited 1: 210 steps, 209 pass, 1 fail. Unit tests, build, vet and closeout-review-policy integration passed. install-and-upgrade-journeys-integration failed at TestJourneysInstallAndUpgradeFromThePublishedRelease because curl received HTTP 403 while listing published releases. That external prerequisite prevents claiming a successful fresh component validation; it does not establish another scoped code defect.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\\n```\",\n.pose/review-runs/rrn-7d33ba9fc274421f.json:86:  \"brief_notes\": \"Implementer notes (Claude Opus 5.5, the lead in this session). Use them as context only; the judgment is yours.\\n\\n- The feature was motivated by the Harne8 batch of 2026-11-22. There, every review round re-ran a 72-check matrix of about 35 minutes, and intermittent suites failed roughly one run in three.\\n- In this repository `pose-mcp` holds 233 of the 236 checks and is high criticality, so `--carry` saves little here. The dogfood record at c4182727 carried five of six modules with zero changed files.\\n- Please challenge the soundness argument of D1 in particular. A carried result is bound to the material computed at HEAD, and that is only safe when the selection guarantees the carried module's inputs did not change.\\n- Please also check the derived-record exclusion (`carryExclusions` with `posemodel.IsAdministrativePath`) and the engine identity, which is the version plus the VCS revision.\\n- Report every finding you see in this round, each classified as blocker or follow-up.\\n\\nRound 2 notes:\\n- F1 from round 1 (rrn-0dd98c4aab8b5918) is addressed in d601fbe1. The record now has `material_clean`, set when the working copy matched HEAD at the start and at the end of the run. `planCarry` refuses a base without it, or with any unavailable material binding. `TestCarryRefusesABaseThatValidatedADirtyWorkingCopy` reproduces your sequence: a pass over an uncommitted fix, a commit of the record alone, the restored failing file, then `--carry`. The test failed with the check mutated out. Account for F1 in prior_findings.\\n- Round 1 also changed files in the sealed worktree because `pose assess integrate` and `pose assess tech-debt` persist their outputs: `.pose/assessments/*`, `.pose/state/*`. Run every `assess` command on a copy in the operation's scratch, never in the sealed checkout, and keep the Bash working directory at the checkout root. Example: `scratch=$(mktemp -d \\\"$TMPDIR/pose-assess.XXXXXX\\\")`, `git archive HEAD | tar -x -C \\\"$scratch\\\"`, `sh -c 'cd \\\"$1\\\" \\u0026\\u0026 exec \\\"$2\\\" assess integrate --json' sh \\\"$scratch\\\" \\\"$(command -v pose)\\\"`.\\n- The `artifact-check` head differs from the bundle subject because the index commits also carry this spec's trailer. `artifact-check` resolves the change set range to the last trailer commit, which is an index-only commit. The bundle subject skips commits that only touch derived records, whose material digest is unchanged. That is existing engine behaviour, which the lead will take up separately. Judge it as you see fit.\\n- The full matrix takes about 13 minutes. If you cannot complete it in the sandbox, cite the sealed canonical result for the `validate` tool and state your own run's limits.\\n\\nRound 3 notes: round 2 (rrn-1c033e4c349d7794) found N1–N4. 2077731b fixes them:\\n- The changed set uses `git diff -z --no-renames` and `ls-files -z`, so a rename names both sides and a quoted name keeps its owner.\\n- The root module `.` is never exempt from root files.\\n- A build with `vcs.modified=true` is not a verifiable identity: it never carries, and a base with a `.dirty` identity is refused.\\n\\nThe regression tests are `TestCarrySelectsBothSidesOfARename`, `TestCarryKeepsTheOwnerOfAQuotedName`, `TestCarryRootModuleOwnsRootFiles` and `TestEngineIdentityRefusesModifiedBuilds`. Each one failed with its fix mutated out. Account for R2-N1..R2-N4 in prior_findings.\\n\\nRound 4 notes: round 3 (rrn-3461f6ff36909419) found N5 and N6.\\n- N5: a declared `dependsOn` path now owns its files even when the dependency is no longer discovered (`underDeclaredDependency`).\\n- N6: module metadata that does not decode is now an error. It means a full run under `--carry` and exit 2 under `--changed-from`.\\nThe regression tests are `TestCarryDeletedDependencySelectsItsDependents` and `TestCarryRejectsUndecodableMetadata`. Both failed with their fix mutated out. Account for R3-N5 and R3-N6 in prior_findings.\\n\\nPlease make this round an exhaustive sweep and report every remaining issue in it, each classified as blocker or follow-up, so the scope can converge. Cover at least:\\n- gitlinks and submodules;\\n- symlinks;\\n- paths that differ only by case;\\n- `moduleOverrides` modules that have no manifest;\\n- nested modules;\\n- a module whose matrix checks or stack change while the matrix digest does not;\\n- criticality and policy widening;\\n- chained carries over many bases;\\n- concurrent runs writing the canonical file.\\n- The lead's own sweep before this round found a gitlink case: a changed gitlink above a declared dependency selected nothing under it. A changed path now selects the modules and dependencies under it, tested by `TestChangedScopeGitlinkAboveADependencySelectsItsDependents`.\\n\\nRound 5 notes: round 4 (rrn-4b28f2ff95acf9c4) found N7–N10. The selection in `computeChangedScope` was rewritten instead of patched. Each changed file now independently selects:\\n- its most specific owner;\\n- every module beneath it;\\n- every module whose declared dependency contains it, lies beneath it or is the root `.`, when that dependency is not a discovered module, which the transitive widening covers;\\n- for a file no module owns, the root module and every module that is not self-contained.\\n\\n`planCarry` refuses when any module is reached through a symlink. `material_clean` now also requires the HEAD at the end of the run to equal the recorded head. The regression tests are `TestCarryDeletedNestedDependencySelectsItsDependents`, `TestCarryRootDependencyIsChangedByRootFiles`, `TestCarryRefusesModulesReachedThroughASymlink` and `TestValidateHeadMovingDuringTheRunIsNotClean`. Each failed with its fix mutated out. Account for R4-N7..R4-N10 in prior_findings, and again report every remaining issue in this round.\\n\\nRound 6 notes: round 5 (rrn-b07ee93779a65e40) found N11–N14.\\n- N11: every eligible dependency now counts (`declaredDependencyHits`).\\n- N12: a run whose HEAD moved, or that is otherwise not `material_clean`, records every material binding as unavailable.\\n- N13: `aliasedModule` also refuses modules that share a physical directory (`os.SameFile`).\\n- N14: the head is pinned before planning, and `planCarry`, the selection and the exclusions use that SHA.\\nThe regression tests are `TestChangedScopeEvaluatesEveryDeclaredDependency`, `TestValidateHeadMovingDuringTheRunBindsNoMaterial`, `TestCarryRefusesModulesSharingADirectory` and `TestCarryPlansAgainstThePinnedHead`. Each failed with its fix mutated out. Account for R5-N11..R5-N14 and the remaining partials R3-N9/R3-N10 in prior_findings, and report every remaining issue in this round.\\n\\nRound 7 notes: round 6 (rrn-88e0428bda9bc9c7) found N15 and N16.\\n- N15: a declared dependency now selects its consumer whenever a changed file intersects it, discovered or not, unless it is the file's own owner, which the transitive widening covers.\\n- N16: `planCarry` refuses when a declared dependency path is reached through a symlink.\\nThe regression tests are `TestChangedScopeDiscoveredAncestorDependencySelectsItsDependents`, which covers a parent and a discovered root dependency, and `TestCarryRefusesDependenciesReachedThroughASymlink`. Account for R6-N15 and R6-N16, and report every remaining issue in this round.\\n\\nRound 8 notes: round 7 (rrn-85704a129332a685) found N17–N19. Instead of chasing alias forms one path at a time, `planCarry` now applies global rules:\\n- `caseInsensitiveFilesystem` refuses on case-folding filesystems.\\n- `aliasingSymlink` refuses any tracked symlink whose path or target lies in a non-root module or intersects a declared dependency, or whose target leaves the repository. Symlinks between unowned paths, such as `.claude/skills` to `.agents/skills`, stay allowed, since a change on either side already selects the root and every non-self-contained module.\\n- `duplicateCheckID` and a base-id check refuse duplicate check ids.\\nThe tests are `TestCarryRefusesASymlinkInsideAModule`, `TestCarryRefusesASymlinkFromAModuleToAnUnownedPath`, `TestCarryAllowsSymlinksBetweenUnownedPaths`, `TestCarryDetectsACaseInsensitiveFilesystem` and `TestCarryRefusesDuplicateCheckIDs`. Account for R7-N17..R7-N19, and report every remaining issue in this round.\\n\\nRound 9 notes: round 8 (rrn-0375009e985e6a3d) found N20–N23.\\n- N23: both diffs force `-c diff.ignoreSubmodules=none diff --ignore-submodules=none`.\\n- N21: `material_clean` also requires `materialWorktreeClean` at the end, so untracked unignored material counts.\\n- N20: `submoduleAliases` scans each submodule that holds a module or a dependency, at its recorded commit. It refuses when that submodule is not checked out at the commit or has nested submodules.\\n- N22: `casefoldedDirectory` probes every module directory and the nearest existing directory of every dependency.\\nThe regression tests are `TestChangedScopeIgnoresSubmoduleHidingConfiguration`, `TestValidateUntrackedMaterialCreatedDuringTheRunIsNotClean`, `TestCarryRefusesAnAliasingSymlinkInsideASubmodule` and `TestCarryDetectsACaseFoldedDirectory`. Each failed with its fix mutated out. Account for R7-N20..R7-N23 and the partials, and report every remaining issue in this round.\\n\\nRound 10 notes: round 9 (rrn-dfc7e3348240ce19) found N24–N26.\\n- N24: `submoduleAliases` scans every gitlink, not only those holding a module or dependency.\\n- N25: the selection also picks every module enclosing the owner. The lead extended this: the root module encloses every module.\\n- N26: `carryRelevantDirs` probes every existing directory from the root to each module and dependency.\\nThe regression tests are `TestChangedScopeSelectsTheEnclosingModule`, `TestChangedScopeRootModuleEnclosesEveryModule`, `TestCarryScansAGitlinkInsideAModule` and `TestCarryRelevantDirsIncludeEveryAncestor`. Account for R9-N24..R9-N26 and report every remaining issue in this round.\\n\\nRound 11 notes: round 10 (rrn-29af03286365811e) found N27–N29.\\n- N27: `casefoldedDirectory` probes with `Lstat`, skips unusable entries and treats an unreadable directory as folding.\\n- N28: `planCarry` refuses absolute or root-escaping dependencies.\\n- N29: the ADR consequences paragraph and the spec summary now describe the selection accurately.\\nThe tests are `TestCarryCaseProbeSkipsUnusableEntries` and `TestCarryRefusesDependenciesOutsideTheRepository`. Account for R10-N27..R10-N29 and report every remaining issue in this round.\\n\\nRound 12 notes: round 11 (rrn-c0b4006e2a8ff303) found N30–N32. All are refused conservatively:\\n- N30: a dependency that is not already a clean path.\\n- N32: non-ASCII module or dependency paths.\\n- N31: any index entry marked assume-unchanged or skip-worktree, in the repository or a checked-out submodule. It also clears `material_clean`.\\nThe tests are `TestCarryRefusesUncleanDependencies`, `TestCarryRefusesNonASCIIPaths` and `TestCarryRefusesHiddenIndexEntries`. Account for R11-N30..R11-N32 and report every remaining issue in this round.\\n\\nRound 13 notes: round 12 (rrn-abb61f059dc6d700) found N33–N35.\\n- N33: `physicallyLexical` resolves each dependency and its existing ancestors, tracked or ignored symlinks alike.\\n- N34: `material_clean` requires HEAD's reflog length to be unchanged and readable.\\n- N35: `casefoldedDirectory` probes only ASCII-letter entries and treats a directory without one as folding.\\nThe tests are `TestCarryRefusesDependenciesThroughAnIgnoredSymlink`, `TestValidateHeadMovingAndReturningIsNotClean` and `TestCarryCaseProbeUsesOnlyASCIILetters`. Account for R12-N33..R12-N35 and report every remaining issue in this round.\\n\\nRound 14 notes: round 13 (rrn-f6546af4c9e5625e) found N36–N39.\\n- N36: the cleanliness status reads force `-c core.fileMode=true`.\\n- N37: HEAD and its reflog are pinned before the matrix is read and modules are discovered. This is structural ordering; a race before planning cannot be reproduced deterministically.\\n- N38: `submodulesCheckedOut` requires every gitlink to be checked out at its recorded commit, both for `material_clean` and for the carry.\\n- N39 is recorded as follow-up F2 in the spec.\\nThe tests are `TestValidateModeChangeHiddenByConfigurationIsNotClean` and `TestValidateUninitializedSubmoduleIsNotClean`. Account for R13-N36..R13-N39 and report every remaining issue in this round.\\n\\nRound 15 notes: round 14 (rrn-db44fd7f02f7b981) found N40 and N41, and N42 restated F2. One predicate, `validationMaterialClean`, now covers status, hidden index entries and submodule checkouts. It runs at the pin, before the matrix is read and modules are discovered, and again at the end. The test is `TestValidateConditionClearedDuringTheRunIsNotClean`. Account for R14-N40..R14-N42 and report every remaining issue in this round.\\n\",\n.pose/review-bundles/rvb-1542644802dce882.json:3104:      \"structural-causality\"\n.pose/review-runs/rrn-581c7da6558f85b3.json:84:  \"brief_notes\": \"Implementer notes — factual context, not a review judgment\\n\\nThe generated sealed brief and its exact IDs are authoritative. Perform one bounded read-only review yourself: do not delegate subagents, watchers or ultrareview, edit project files, record attestations or invoke contributor submission. Return the typed judgment the generated brief requests. Report all blocking findings and use only sealed evidence IDs; do not infer approval from a successful command.\\n\\nThe implementing execution is OpenAI, exact model unknown. The selected reviewer is the user-requested Claude Code Opus 5.5. The local signer declares the executor's protected identity; it does not certify an Anthropic receipt or human authority.\\n\\nThe current source checkpoint is bff2b6e7, with the executable-provenance correction in 448a7504. Its canonical strict matrix passed 189/189 checks (367.8s), including the uncached full Go suite, B34 production integration with race, CLI/MCP parity, writer publication and enabled installation journey. Focused RunProvenance tests with race passed in 11.093s. Current discover/update-state, integrate, tech-debt, knowledge, lint, index, design, artifact and surface checks exited 0; surface findings 0. Integration inventory is static, not functional proof. Tech-debt remains INCOMPLETE because two historical specs cannot be read; no uncovered marker was found in scanned content. Keep that limitation.\\n\\nThe real global strict check on the prior read-view source b7b5680f passed with 35 historical warnings and no errors. Preserve that source identity; do not relabel it a current structural run after D9. A final global structural check is reserved for the final administrative/documentation boundary. The full monolithic race command passed every other package but domain timed out at 10m; a 30m domain-only attempt also timed out while the global corpus gate ran. Neither is a pass. All 1,425 domain tests on b7 then passed in four disjoint complete groups of 357/356/356/356 (214.656/136.488/168.012/191.100s), with no Fuzz/Example functions. Since then the Go delta is only the streaming executable hash limit and its two tests, covered by current focused race and the canonical suite; no new concurrency was added.\\n\\nPrior native review runs never invoked a vendor: rrn-accfce117640c7af failed because its sealed commit held an old index without B34 attribution;42c8891f persisted the real indexes and results. rrn-bef40df473391d0c then passed checkout setup but rejected the 337,814,032-byte native Claude Code 2.1.318 executable against the 256 MiB transcript bound reused for executable hashing. Accepted D9 separates a 512 MiB streaming executable bound while preserving real target/regular-file/identity/overflow checks. Transcript retention stays 256 MiB and all read-view limits stay unchanged. No wrapper was substituted and no approval or old receipt was reconstructed.\\n\\nB34 recovery preserves historical failures and the prospective native start b2eb2d34. D5 retains 64 local edges and 256 unique graph nodes/entries, with eight composed project crossings including redirects; D6 bounds an aggregate operation to 25,000 records, 512 MiB input and 8 MiB retained metadata across at most 16 authorized roots. D7 separates audited global selection/catalogue from independently bounded scope closures with bounded concurrency and exact Files/root/authority bindings. The final audit lists a directory once per root audit while still checking consumed Info metadata; roadmap children retain their authorized context. D8 excludes only instance delegation policy from the scaffold through its established exclusion path. External uncooperative ABA remains outside the guarantee: no universal filesystem transaction, persistent authorization, daemon, watcher or cross-operation cache is claimed.\\n\\nInspect actual production writer guard/CAS/receipt paths, final audits and retries, changed/unknown distinctions, retained-review negatives, index outputs and bindings from one captured build. Give explicit structural mappings for the deltas in the current sealed brief. The component tests validation matrix declares producer_coverage none: use a supported not-used disposition and rationale for that tool rather than pretending it ran; the current global validation can support pose-mcp only as sealed native coverage permits. Remote CI was waived by the user; Harne8 engine/gitlink adoption is outside this change.\\n\",\n.pose/review-bundles/rvb-4a16800ce7a4c813.json:350:          \"rationale\": \"observe bounded structural deltas on the canonical review subject\",\n.pose/review-bundles/rvb-4a16800ce7a4c813.json:557:      \"structural-causality\"\n.pose/review-runs/rrn-fc6566de3c7eedf0.json:86:  \"brief_notes\": \"Implementer notes (Claude Opus 5.5, the lead in this session). Use them as context only; the judgment is yours.\\n\\n- The feature was motivated by the Harne8 batch of 2026-11-22. There, every review round re-ran a 72-check matrix of about 35 minutes, and intermittent suites failed roughly one run in three.\\n- In this repository `pose-mcp` holds 233 of the 236 checks and is high criticality, so `--carry` saves little here. The dogfood record at c4182727 carried five of six modules with zero changed files.\\n- Please challenge the soundness argument of D1 in particular. A carried result is bound to the material computed at HEAD, and that is only safe when the selection guarantees the carried module's inputs did not change.\\n- Please also check the derived-record exclusion (`carryExclusions` with `posemodel.IsAdministrativePath`) and the engine identity, which is the version plus the VCS revision.\\n- Report every finding you see in this round, each classified as blocker or follow-up.\\n\\nRound 2 notes:\\n- F1 from round 1 (rrn-0dd98c4aab8b5918) is addressed in d601fbe1. The record now has `material_clean`, set when the working copy matched HEAD at the start and at the end of the run. `planCarry` refuses a base without it, or with any unavailable material binding. `TestCarryRefusesABaseThatValidatedADirtyWorkingCopy` reproduces your sequence: a pass over an uncommitted fix, a commit of the record alone, the restored failing file, then `--carry`. The test failed with the check mutated out. Account for F1 in prior_findings.\\n- Round 1 also changed files in the sealed worktree because `pose assess integrate` and `pose assess tech-debt` persist their outputs: `.pose/assessments/*`, `.pose/state/*`. Run every `assess` command on a copy in the operation's scratch, never in the sealed checkout, and keep the Bash working directory at the checkout root. Example: `scratch=$(mktemp -d \\\"$TMPDIR/pose-assess.XXXXXX\\\")`, `git archive HEAD | tar -x -C \\\"$scratch\\\"`, `sh -c 'cd \\\"$1\\\" \\u0026\\u0026 exec \\\"$2\\\" assess integrate --json' sh \\\"$scratch\\\" \\\"$(command -v pose)\\\"`.\\n- The `artifact-check` head differs from the bundle subject because the index commits also carry this spec's trailer. `artifact-check` resolves the change set range to the last trailer commit, which is an index-only commit. The bundle subject skips commits that only touch derived records, whose material digest is unchanged. That is existing engine behaviour, which the lead will take up separately. Judge it as you see fit.\\n- The full matrix takes about 13 minutes. If you cannot complete it in the sandbox, cite the sealed canonical result for the `validate` tool and state your own run's limits.\\n\\nRound 3 notes: round 2 (rrn-1c033e4c349d7794) found N1–N4. 2077731b fixes them:\\n- The changed set uses `git diff -z --no-renames` and `ls-files -z`, so a rename names both sides and a quoted name keeps its owner.\\n- The root module `.` is never exempt from root files.\\n- A build with `vcs.modified=true` is not a verifiable identity: it never carries, and a base with a `.dirty` identity is refused.\\n\\nThe regression tests are `TestCarrySelectsBothSidesOfARename`, `TestCarryKeepsTheOwnerOfAQuotedName`, `TestCarryRootModuleOwnsRootFiles` and `TestEngineIdentityRefusesModifiedBuilds`. Each one failed with its fix mutated out. Account for R2-N1..R2-N4 in prior_findings.\\n\\nRound 4 notes: round 3 (rrn-3461f6ff36909419) found N5 and N6.\\n- N5: a declared `dependsOn` path now owns its files even when the dependency is no longer discovered (`underDeclaredDependency`).\\n- N6: module metadata that does not decode is now an error. It means a full run under `--carry` and exit 2 under `--changed-from`.\\nThe regression tests are `TestCarryDeletedDependencySelectsItsDependents` and `TestCarryRejectsUndecodableMetadata`. Both failed with their fix mutated out. Account for R3-N5 and R3-N6 in prior_findings.\\n\\nPlease make this round an exhaustive sweep and report every remaining issue in it, each classified as blocker or follow-up, so the scope can converge. Cover at least:\\n- gitlinks and submodules;\\n- symlinks;\\n- paths that differ only by case;\\n- `moduleOverrides` modules that have no manifest;\\n- nested modules;\\n- a module whose matrix checks or stack change while the matrix digest does not;\\n- criticality and policy widening;\\n- chained carries over many bases;\\n- concurrent runs writing the canonical file.\\n- The lead's own sweep before this round found a gitlink case: a changed gitlink above a declared dependency selected nothing under it. A changed path now selects the modules and dependencies under it, tested by `TestChangedScopeGitlinkAboveADependencySelectsItsDependents`.\\n\\nRound 5 notes: round 4 (rrn-4b28f2ff95acf9c4) found N7–N10. The selection in `computeChangedScope` was rewritten instead of patched. Each changed file now independently selects:\\n- its most specific owner;\\n- every module beneath it;\\n- every module whose declared dependency contains it, lies beneath it or is the root `.`, when that dependency is not a discovered module, which the transitive widening covers;\\n- for a file no module owns, the root module and every module that is not self-contained.\\n\\n`planCarry` refuses when any module is reached through a symlink. `material_clean` now also requires the HEAD at the end of the run to equal the recorded head. The regression tests are `TestCarryDeletedNestedDependencySelectsItsDependents`, `TestCarryRootDependencyIsChangedByRootFiles`, `TestCarryRefusesModulesReachedThroughASymlink` and `TestValidateHeadMovingDuringTheRunIsNotClean`. Each failed with its fix mutated out. Account for R4-N7..R4-N10 in prior_findings, and again report every remaining issue in this round.\\n\\nRound 6 notes: round 5 (rrn-b07ee93779a65e40) found N11–N14.\\n- N11: every eligible dependency now counts (`declaredDependencyHits`).\\n- N12: a run whose HEAD moved, or that is otherwise not `material_clean`, records every material binding as unavailable.\\n- N13: `aliasedModule` also refuses modules that share a physical directory (`os.SameFile`).\\n- N14: the head is pinned before planning, and `planCarry`, the selection and the exclusions use that SHA.\\nThe regression tests are `TestChangedScopeEvaluatesEveryDeclaredDependency`, `TestValidateHeadMovingDuringTheRunBindsNoMaterial`, `TestCarryRefusesModulesSharingADirectory` and `TestCarryPlansAgainstThePinnedHead`. Each failed with its fix mutated out. Account for R5-N11..R5-N14 and the remaining partials R3-N9/R3-N10 in prior_findings, and report every remaining issue in this round.\\n\\nRound 7 notes: round 6 (rrn-88e0428bda9bc9c7) found N15 and N16.\\n- N15: a declared dependency now selects its consumer whenever a changed file intersects it, discovered or not, unless it is the file's own owner, which the transitive widening covers.\\n- N16: `planCarry` refuses when a declared dependency path is reached through a symlink.\\nThe regression tests are `TestChangedScopeDiscoveredAncestorDependencySelectsItsDependents`, which covers a parent and a discovered root dependency, and `TestCarryRefusesDependenciesReachedThroughASymlink`. Account for R6-N15 and R6-N16, and report every remaining issue in this round.\\n\\nRound 8 notes: round 7 (rrn-85704a129332a685) found N17–N19. Instead of chasing alias forms one path at a time, `planCarry` now applies global rules:\\n- `caseInsensitiveFilesystem` refuses on case-folding filesystems.\\n- `aliasingSymlink` refuses any tracked symlink whose path or target lies in a non-root module or intersects a declared dependency, or whose target leaves the repository. Symlinks between unowned paths, such as `.claude/skills` to `.agents/skills`, stay allowed, since a change on either side already selects the root and every non-self-contained module.\\n- `duplicateCheckID` and a base-id check refuse duplicate check ids.\\nThe tests are `TestCarryRefusesASymlinkInsideAModule`, `TestCarryRefusesASymlinkFromAModuleToAnUnownedPath`, `TestCarryAllowsSymlinksBetweenUnownedPaths`, `TestCarryDetectsACaseInsensitiveFilesystem` and `TestCarryRefusesDuplicateCheckIDs`. Account for R7-N17..R7-N19, and report every remaining issue in this round.\\n\\nRound 9 notes: round 8 (rrn-0375009e985e6a3d) found N20–N23.\\n- N23: both diffs force `-c diff.ignoreSubmodules=none diff --ignore-submodules=none`.\\n- N21: `material_clean` also requires `materialWorktreeClean` at the end, so untracked unignored material counts.\\n- N20: `submoduleAliases` scans each submodule that holds a module or a dependency, at its recorded commit. It refuses when that submodule is not checked out at the commit or has nested submodules.\\n- N22: `casefoldedDirectory` probes every module directory and the nearest existing directory of every dependency.\\nThe regression tests are `TestChangedScopeIgnoresSubmoduleHidingConfiguration`, `TestValidateUntrackedMaterialCreatedDuringTheRunIsNotClean`, `TestCarryRefusesAnAliasingSymlinkInsideASubmodule` and `TestCarryDetectsACaseFoldedDirectory`. Each failed with its fix mutated out. Account for R7-N20..R7-N23 and the partials, and report every remaining issue in this round.\\n\\nRound 10 notes: round 9 (rrn-dfc7e3348240ce19) found N24–N26.\\n- N24: `submoduleAliases` scans every gitlink, not only those holding a module or dependency.\\n- N25: the selection also picks every module enclosing the owner. The lead extended this: the root module encloses every module.\\n- N26: `carryRelevantDirs` probes every existing directory from the root to each module and dependency.\\nThe regression tests are `TestChangedScopeSelectsTheEnclosingModule`, `TestChangedScopeRootModuleEnclosesEveryModule`, `TestCarryScansAGitlinkInsideAModule` and `TestCarryRelevantDirsIncludeEveryAncestor`. Account for R9-N24..R9-N26 and report every remaining issue in this round.\\n\\nRound 11 notes: round 10 (rrn-29af03286365811e) found N27–N29.\\n- N27: `casefoldedDirectory` probes with `Lstat`, skips unusable entries and treats an unreadable directory as folding.\\n- N28: `planCarry` refuses absolute or root-escaping dependencies.\\n- N29: the ADR consequences paragraph and the spec summary now describe the selection accurately.\\nThe tests are `TestCarryCaseProbeSkipsUnusableEntries` and `TestCarryRefusesDependenciesOutsideTheRepository`. Account for R10-N27..R10-N29 and report every remaining issue in this round.\\n\\nRound 12 notes: round 11 (rrn-c0b4006e2a8ff303) found N30–N32. All are refused conservatively:\\n- N30: a dependency that is not already a clean path.\\n- N32: non-ASCII module or dependency paths.\\n- N31: any index entry marked assume-unchanged or skip-worktree, in the repository or a checked-out submodule. It also clears `material_clean`.\\nThe tests are `TestCarryRefusesUncleanDependencies`, `TestCarryRefusesNonASCIIPaths` and `TestCarryRefusesHiddenIndexEntries`. Account for R11-N30..R11-N32 and report every remaining issue in this round.\\n\\nRound 13 notes: round 12 (rrn-abb61f059dc6d700) found N33–N35.\\n- N33: `physicallyLexical` resolves each dependency and its existing ancestors, tracked or ignored symlinks alike.\\n- N34: `material_clean` requires HEAD's reflog length to be unchanged and readable.\\n- N35: `casefoldedDirectory` probes only ASCII-letter entries and treats a directory without one as folding.\\nThe tests are `TestCarryRefusesDependenciesThroughAnIgnoredSymlink`, `TestValidateHeadMovingAndReturningIsNotClean` and `TestCarryCaseProbeUsesOnlyASCIILetters`. Account for R12-N33..R12-N35 and report every remaining issue in this round.\\n\\nRound 14 notes: round 13 (rrn-f6546af4c9e5625e) found N36–N39.\\n- N36: the cleanliness status reads force `-c core.fileMode=true`.\\n- N37: HEAD and its reflog are pinned before the matrix is read and modules are discovered. This is structural ordering; a race before planning cannot be reproduced deterministically.\\n- N38: `submodulesCheckedOut` requires every gitlink to be checked out at its recorded commit, both for `material_clean` and for the carry.\\n- N39 is recorded as follow-up F2 in the spec.\\nThe tests are `TestValidateModeChangeHiddenByConfigurationIsNotClean` and `TestValidateUninitializedSubmoduleIsNotClean`. Account for R13-N36..R13-N39 and report every remaining issue in this round.\\n\\nRound 15 notes: round 14 (rrn-db44fd7f02f7b981) found N40 and N41, and N42 restated F2. One predicate, `validationMaterialClean`, now covers status, hidden index entries and submodule checkouts. It runs at the pin, before the matrix is read and modules are discovered, and again at the end. The test is `TestValidateConditionClearedDuringTheRunIsNotClean`. Account for R14-N40..R14-N42 and report every remaining issue in this round.\\n\\nRepeat note for this bundle: the previous attempt (rrn-7d33ba9fc274421f) stopped without a draft because building the CLI and creating scratch copies hit a read-only filesystem. That is a known limit of this review sandbox. Earlier rounds handled it by running the focused Go tests, which passed here before (`go test ./internal/cli -run 'Carry|ChangedScope|Validate|Material'`, `go vet`), and by citing the sealed canonical result for the `validate` and `assess` tools with the limitation stated in each disposition. Please do the same instead of stopping: give your judgment on the code and record every tool limitation honestly in the draft.\\n\\nRound 16 notes: round 15 (rrn-16091dd78a12cc0b) found N43 and N45, and N44 restated F2.\\n- N43: `movementWitness` records the reflog lengths of HEAD and of every checked-out submodule at the pin and at the end. They must match and be readable.\\n- N45: a cancelled context, or any cancelled check, sets the run-level `cancelled`, clears `material_clean` and is refused as a base.\\nThe tests are `TestValidateSubmoduleMovingAndReturningIsNotClean` and `TestCarryRefusesABaseCancelledAtRunLevel`. If building or scratch creation is read-only here, run the focused Go tests and cite the sealed canonical result rather than stopping. Account for R15-N43..R15-N45 and report every remaining issue in this round.\\n\\nRound 17 notes: round 16 (rrn-328651cf23a32126) found N46–N48, and F2 was restated.\\n- N46: `planCarry` refuses when the working `module-metadata.json` differs from HEAD's.\\n- N47: `finalizeCancellation` clears `material_clean` and makes every binding unavailable.\\n- N48: `validationMaterialClean` fails when a submodule has nested submodules.\\nThe tests are `TestCarryRefusesWorkingMetadataThatDiffersFromHead`, `TestCancellationMakesBindingsUnavailable` and `TestValidateNestedSubmodulesAreNotClean`. If building or scratch creation is read-only, run the focused Go tests and cite the sealed canonical result rather than stopping. Account for R16-N46..R16-N48 and report every remaining issue in this round.\\n\\nRepeat note for this bundle: the previous attempt (rrn-6741de0e146e3777) approved, but its conclusion was refused for format. The preflight said: \\\"finding id \\\\\\\"R17-N49\\\\\\\" is not a unique identifier without a round prefix\\\". A finding you report in `findings` must use a new unprefixed ID that no earlier round used, for example `N50`. The round-prefixed IDs belong only in `prior_findings`, for findings listed by the brief. Judge the subject independently; the format is the only reason for this repeat.\\n\\nRound 18 notes: round 17's repeat (rrn-243366b14aa5fea4, attestation rva-b084f3e3849f1ed5) found N50, and N51 restated F2. N50: `planCarry` reads the module metadata once, from the pinned commit (`scopeMetadataAt`), and passes that snapshot to `computeChangedScopeWith`. The working copy must still equal it. The test is `TestCarrySelectsWithThePinnedMetadataSnapshot`. New findings use unprefixed IDs; prior ones go in `prior_findings`. Account for R17-N50 and R17-N51 and report every remaining issue.\\n\\nRound 19 notes: round 18 (rrn-5ed84b0f66cce29b, attestation rva-f39a887e59b3aaaa) found N52, and N53/N54 restated F2/F1. `scopeMetadataAt` and `workingFileDiffersFromHead` now read absence from the pinned tree (`inTree`, via `ls-tree`), and a listed blob that cannot be read is an error. The test is `TestCarryRefusesAnUnreadableMetadataBlob`. New findings use unprefixed IDs. Account for R18-N52..R18-N54 and report every remaining issue.\\n\",\n.pose/review-runs/rrn-fc6566de3c7eedf0.json:106:  \"output\": \"decision: approved\\n\\nNo remaining blocker established. The unreadable-metadata defect is fixed. Two existing low-severity follow-ups remain accepted through **2026-12-15**:\\n\\n- **N55:** `--carry --report` presents carried checks as executed commands without their original head and time.\\n- **N56:** Dedicated end-to-end coverage for sealing, verifying and closing over a carried record remains missing.\\n\\nIndependent focused tests, `go vet ./...`, `go build ./...` and artifact-check passed. Full-matrix validation relies on the sealed evidence under the brief’s sandbox allowance. The checkout remains unchanged; no attestation was recorded.\\n\\nApplied the review workflow and backend-go, security, documentation-style and delivery-evidence rules. Consulted knowledge governance and existing follow-ups.\\n\\n```pose-draft\\n{\\n  \\\"schema\\\": \\\"pose.review.draft/v1\\\",\\n  \\\"decision\\\": \\\"approved\\\",\\n  \\\"findings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"N55\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"low\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"follow-up\\\",\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": 1623,\\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"validationSummaryOf includes carried checks in Commands and renders their prior outcomes and durations without carried_from or carried_generated_at. A newly dated --carry --report therefore presents reused observations as commands executed by this run. This remains spec follow-up F2.\\\",\\n      \\\"action\\\": \\\"Implement F2: exclude carried checks from the executed-command summary and label reused results with their original head and time.\\\",\\n      \\\"owner\\\": \\\"@pose-maintainers\\\",\\n      \\\"review_by\\\": \\\"2026-12-15\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"N56\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"low\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"follow-up\\\",\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\".pose/specs/2026-11-22-pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks.md\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": 255,\\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"The delivery reader directly tests carried head and time, but no dedicated end-to-end fixture seals a bundle, verifies it and checks closeout over a carried record. This remains spec follow-up F1.\\\",\\n      \\\"action\\\": \\\"Implement F1: add the carried-record seal, verify and closeout-check fixture, including rejection of misattributed evidence.\\\",\\n      \\\"owner\\\": \\\"@pose-maintainers\\\",\\n      \\\"review_by\\\": \\\"2026-12-15\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"prior_findings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R12-N39\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"not-fixed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go:1623-1636 still includes carried commands and omits their origin. The owned remediation remains F2 at spec line 256; retained as N55.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R13-N42\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"not-fixed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"Source inspection of validationSummaryOf at pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go:1619-1636 confirms the report-provenance defect remains; retained as N55 under F2.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R14-N44\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"not-fixed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go:1623 appends every non-skipped command without testing CarriedFrom, and lines 1626-1636 omit original head and time; retained as N55.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R16-N51\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"not-fixed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"validationSummaryOf at pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go:1619-1636 remains unchanged in the relevant behavior. F2 at spec line 256 owns the remediation; retained as N55.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R17-N52\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"scopeMetadataAt at pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry.go:769-778 determines presence from the pinned tree and returns an error when a listed blob cannot be read. workingFileDiffersFromHead at lines 710-721 does likewise. Independently ran go test ./internal/cli -run 'CarryRefusesAnUnreadableMetadataBlob|CarrySelectsWithThePinnedMetadataSnapshot|DeliveryValidation' -count=1 in pose-mcp; passed.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R17-N53\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"not-fixed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go:1623-1636 still loses carried provenance in the report projection. This is the existing F2 risk retained as N55.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R17-N54\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"not-fixed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"The spec explicitly retains the missing end-to-end fixture at lines 237-238 and 255. delivery_validation_run_test.go directly covers parsing head and time, rather than seal/verify/closeout. Retained as N56.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"sweep\\\": \\\"Reviewed the complete implementation diff, requirements R1-R10, decisions D1-D3, ADR, CLI help, English and pt-BR manuals and embedded copies. Swept flag confinement, base eligibility, unreadable metadata, pinned metadata selection, dirty material and unavailable bindings, cancellation, HEAD and submodule movement, gitlinks, nested submodules, symlinks, case and Unicode aliases, hidden index entries, clean and escaping dependency paths, renames and quoted names, manifest-free moduleOverrides, nested and root ownership, stack/check identity changes, criticality and transitive dependency widening, administrative exclusions, chained carries, failures and counts, delivery consumption, scheduler behavior and canonical publication. Concurrent readers receive a complete atomic record; publication retains its governance guard and policy recheck. Independently ran focused carry/scope/validate/material tests, engine identity and concurrency/publication tests, delivery-reader/material tests, the latest metadata regressions with -count=1, go vet ./..., go build ./..., artifact-check, assess-design, suggest-review and recurrence-check. Recurrence-check flagged zero keys. Reviewed changed debt markers directly. Scratch creation and go run failed with Read-only file system, preventing assessment-copy and full-matrix reruns; used the explicitly permitted sealed canonical validation evidence. No new blocker was established. Report provenance and dedicated carried-record closeout coverage remain the two owned low risks. Final git status was clean.\\\",\\n  \\\"criteria\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assumption-integrity\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-c044141caf6521ee\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Examined D1-D3 and their eligibility and selection premises. Verified pinned metadata, conservative alias refusals and material-clean checks in source and focused tests. Actual check inputs respecting declared module/dependency boundaries remain an explicit instance assumption; arbitrary external inputs and environmental nondeterminism are outside this cache contract. N55 and N56 are accepted low risks. Full-matrix verification relies on sealed evidence, not an independent rerun.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-concurrency\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/writer-coordination-and-atomic-publication-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Inspected carried entries, scheduler exclusion, cancellation finalization and canonical publication. Carried entries are silent and bypass execution; publication retains the governance write guard, policy recheck and authoritative atomic writer. Focused cancellation, concurrency and publication tests passed.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-contracts\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delivery-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Result fields and CLI functionality are additive. Legacy records remain readable and cannot become carry bases without the required identity and cleanliness fields. The delivery reader uses original carried head and time; its direct regression passed.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-input-errors\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Reviewed incompatible flags, revision confinement, absent and unreadable metadata, unusable bases and conservative fallback reasons. The latest unreadable-blob and pinned-metadata regressions passed independently with -count=1.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-integration-impact\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delivery-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Traced canonical JSON through ParseDeliveryValidationRun into delivery results and material provenance. Direct carried-head/time tests passed. Dedicated carried-record sealing and closeout coverage remains accepted follow-up N56.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-observability\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N55\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"compatibility\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/cli-mcp-operation-results-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Examined flag parsing, result schema additions, old-record parsing and engine identity comparison. Existing CLI, file and MCP consumers retain compatible contracts. Invalid selection metadata now errors or forces a full run as explicitly required.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"correctness\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Focused carry, changed-scope, material, engine identity, cancellation, concurrency, publication and delivery-reader tests passed. go vet ./... and go build ./... passed. Reviewed negative selection and provenance paths; no remaining correctness blocker was established.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"design-causality\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-c044141caf6521ee\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"D1 addresses repeated whole-matrix execution by preserving original observations while selecting changed inputs. D2 rejects matrix and engine drift; D3 makes root-change exemptions explicit. The cheapest unsupported shortcut would reuse an observation for changed or unverified material; eligibility and selection regressions cover those shortcuts. There is no dedicated carried-record seal/verify/closeout adversarial journey yet; that boundary is retained as N56.\\\",\\n      \\\"mappings\\\": [\\n        {\\n          \\\"delta\\\": \\\"SD-253b523c\\\",\\n          \\\"basis\\\": \\\"D1\\\",\\n          \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"mapped\\\",\\n          \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The added ADR records the structural evidence decision: carried checks retain their original head while the current run computes material bindings, justified by sound changed-scope selection and explicit declarations.\\\"\\n        }\\n      ]\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"documentation\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/distributed-instructions-parity-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Compared requirements, ADR, help and both language manuals with runtime selection, eligibility and provenance behavior. Changed carry documentation is mirrored in embedded copies. The root English manual's contributor-mode section differs from the scaffold by an existing instance-specific section outside this change. F1 and F2 are explicitly owned and dated.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"operability\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N55\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"requirements\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Mapped R1-R10 to implementation and relevant regressions, including refusal flags, fallback eligibility, selection, preserved outcomes and origins, counts, declarations, delivery reading, all-carried behavior and compatibility. Focused tests passed; N56 preserves the disclosed end-to-end coverage gap.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"scope\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-c044141caf6521ee\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The source changes stay within validation planning/results, shared changed-scope selection, delivery consumption, tests and corresponding documentation. The ADR is justified by the evidence contract. Derived records in the broader Git range were distinguished from the sealed implementation scope.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"security\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Examined revision confinement, path containment, dependency escapes, symlink and case aliases, hidden index entries, unreadable Git objects and publication authority. Uncertainty conservatively refuses reuse. No new dependency or sensitive-data exposure was identified in the reviewed diff.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"solution-proportionality\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-c044141caf6521ee\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Module-level reuse extends the existing selector and uses whole-matrix and engine comparison instead of introducing an arbitrary-input cache. Per-check input hashing would require a larger declaration contract; manual merging would lose provenance. Conservative alias refusals trade optimization coverage for simpler safety reasoning. Revisit this choice if actual inputs cannot be represented by the declared boundaries or finer reuse becomes a requirement.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"tools\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"artifact-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks --strict\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The required command exited 0. It reported 985 warnings and resolved the trailer range through a later derived-record commit, as disclosed in the brief. This is not evidence that the sealed implementation scope expanded.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-design\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-c044141caf6521ee\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Ran pose assess design --spec pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks --json successfully. Its digest matches the sealed structural evidence and it reports SD-253b523c.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-discover\\\",\\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:mktemp -d /tmp/pose-review-assess.XXXXXX\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Scratch creation failed with Read-only file system. Discovery was not run in the sealed checkout because it can persist assessment outputs.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-integrate\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:mktemp -d /tmp/pose-review-assess.XXXXXX\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The required assessment copy could not be created. Avoided modifying the sealed checkout; integration judgment uses source tracing, focused delivery tests and sealed integration evidence.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-tech-debt\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:mktemp -d /tmp/pose-review-assess.XXXXXX\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The assessment copy could not be created. Reviewed changed implementation markers and the spec's owned follow-ups directly; did not persist assessment or state files.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"closeout-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:pose closeout-check spec:pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Completion gate must run after POSE records and verifies this conclusion. The reviewer did not record an attestation or apply closeout.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"review-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:pose review-check spec:pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Deferred until POSE records this review's attestation, as required by the brief.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"suggest-review\\\",\\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Ran successfully and applied the selected review workflow, backend-go, security and documentation-style rules, with delivery-evidence guidance.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"validate\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"build:pose-mcp/go/build\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Uses the sealed canonical strict-validation result under the brief's explicit sandbox allowance. An independent full-matrix rerun was not completed: scratch creation and go run failed with Read-only file system. Independently ran focused tests, go vet ./... and go build ./... successfully.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"validate\\\",\\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Uses the sealed canonical component-validation result under the brief's sandbox allowance. Independently passed go test ./internal/cli -run 'Carry|ChangedScope|Validate|Material'; focused engine identity, cancellation, concurrency and canonical-publication tests; go test ./internal/pose -run 'DeliveryValidationRun|Material'; the latest metadata regressions with -count=1; go vet ./...; and go build ./.... This does not claim an independent full component-matrix rerun.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\\n```\",\n.pose/review-runs/rrn-9f528bb5bec8a10b.json:86:  \"brief_notes\": \"Review of spec pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit, implemented by Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic). The ADR `.pose/adr/2026-11-12-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-and-benefit.md` is Accepted; judge the implementation against it and the spec, not the decision itself.\\n\\nMechanism. Review policy schema 5 adds `milestone_review_required` / `roadmap_review_required` (`never|when-justified|always`), validated in `parseReviewPolicy` via `validateCloseoutReviewPolicyKeys` (closeout_review_policy.go). One evaluator `evaluateCloseoutReview` (closeout-review@1): canonical members `xref:\\u003cproject\\u003e/spec:\\u003cslug\\u003e` (aliases, verified redirects, federated resolver, unknown = diagnostic, never zero) and ADR associations (closeout_adr_associations.go: roadmap `adrs:`, ADR `roadmaps:`, local Markdown links both ways; malformed/missing/unreadable = unknown). `closeoutReviewGate` is the single entry for readers: receipt first, roadmap done before adoption = legacy (nil decision), else evaluate + `protectCloseoutDecision` (baseline policy at the change set base when the scope changes the review contract); exemption only when not required AND no review recorded on the scope (`scopeReviewRecorded`, unreadable counts as recorded). Consumers: `reviewCheck` (review_closeout.go, Required=false + ApprovalOrigin), `proportionalReviewVerification` (review_bundle.go; under adoption the legacy singleton inheritance and `unreviewed_milestones` are skipped), `getCloseoutState` (CloseRequired, receipt, terminal only with receipt, new diagnostics), `ReachedMilestones`/`RoadmapsReachedBy`/`roadmapReachedApartFrom` (roadmaps.go), `milestoneReachedObligations`, `ReviewPlan.CloseoutReview` (out of the digest), doctor (`CloseoutReviewsOwed`), setup and `pose adopt` (capability_catalog.go `closeoutReviewPolicyCatalogEntry`, `SetCloseoutReviewPolicy`; refs/transfer adopt/retire no longer lower schema 5). CLI close (cli/review_closeout.go `closeoutReceiptPreflight`, `publishCloseoutReceipt`): milestone and roadmap close publish an immutable receipt (closeout_receipt.go, ExpectAbsent publish, strict parse); a done roadmap without receipt is completed by a new close. `milestoneMember` now maps `spec:\\u003cslug\\u003e` to its slug (was `spec:spec:\\u003cslug\\u003e` in closeout state). Existing tests changed on purpose: catalog lists, schema after adopt (fresh install is now schema 5), progressive_review fixtures that force schema 2, and the previous-release compatibility test (a fresh install is refused by v7.4.0 by its schema, by ADR design; an updated legacy instance stays readable).\\n\\nPlease do an exhaustive sweep in this round and report ALL findings together, classified blocker vs follow-up. Inventory every entry point that answers \\\"is this aggregate scope approved / closed / reached\\\" (CLI close, closeout-check, review-check, review verify, review-plan, attention/obligations, reached, nextCloses, roadmap check, MCP closeout state, federated acceptance, doctor) and check each one reads the same gate, cannot launder a recorded rejection under `never`, cannot let `always` be weakened by inheritance or `unreviewed_milestones`, and never treats an unknown member/association as an exemption. Also check: receipts are never overwritten nor fabricated for history; `pose update` never adopts; no schema-5 downgrade path; the recovery path for a roadmap done without receipt cannot close a scope whose review is required and unapproved.\\n\\nKnown pre-existing state: `pose check --strict` reports 19 delivery-contract errors of other specs (runtime worktree, common-domain handoff, governance performance, bounded graph caches), identical line by line on the base commit 956153f1; they are follow-up F4, not this spec.\\n\\nRequired tools: run `pose artifact-check --spec pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit --strict` and `pose surface-check --spec pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit --strict`; declare each `passed` only after running it (evidence `command:\\u003cthe command\\u003e`, rationale quoting its result). The surface-check disposition must cite both an `integration:` and a `reachability:` sealed evidence id. Cite sealed `unit:`/`integration:` ids for criteria, never `SD-…` structural facts or requirement ids. Send each shell command alone in its own call (no pipes, `;`, `\\u0026\\u0026`, redirects). `validate` of a component with registered checks is `passed` with the sealed run's evidence; `review-check` and `closeout-check` are `deferred`. New findings have bare ids (F1, F2 …); follow-ups carry `action`, `owner`, `review_by`; only low-severity risks may be accepted.\\n\\nRound 16. Account in `prior_findings` exactly for the findings the brief lists as open for this scope (your round-15 run rrn-4a37964df583131c: R14-N48, plus any earlier partial the brief shows), each with whether it stands. Since round 15, N48: a link destination is decoded as Markdown resolves it (character references, backslash escapes, then fragment and query, then URL escapes) before the namespace and extension tests, in both directions, and an escape that does not decode leaves the answer unknown. Since round 14 the association reader is fail-closed by design: the code/comment filter added for N40 is gone, so code and comments are read like prose and a link shown as an example still counts (over-enforcement: the answer may become unknown or require review; accepted residual risk, follow-up F6), and a destination with parentheses, which the extractor may cut short, leaves the answer unknown in both directions (N47). Classify accordingly: a Markdown form in which a real association is silently dropped and an exemption follows is a blocker; a form that makes the reader require review or report unknown where a perfect parser would not is a follow-up under F6. Dispose the `validate` tools from the sealed evidence: the pipeline ran `pose validate --strict` on a clean clone of the sealed commit with a GitHub token (`.pose/results/delivery-validation.json`); a rerun in your sandbox fails for environment reasons and is not evidence about the code. A finding object accepts exactly `id`, `severity`, `disposition`, `file`, `line`, `summary`, and for an accepted follow-up `action`, `owner`, `review_by`; put any rationale inside `summary`. Do NOT run `pose assess`, `pose state`, `pose index` or anything else that writes under `.pose/`; dispose assess-* tools from the sealed evidence and the code. Leave the worktree as you found it. Sweep the whole surface again and report every remaining finding in one pass, classified blocker vs follow-up; a remote variant of a threat the ADR does not promise to defend is a follow-up, and so is a pre-existing gap of the federation or transfer engine that this spec did not introduce and does not claim to close.\\n\",\n.pose/review-runs/rrn-9f528bb5bec8a10b.json:106:  \"output\": \"decision: changes-requested\\n\\nThree medium blockers remain in ADR association parsing:\\n\\n- **N50, line 37:** valid reference definitions with multiline labels, escaped brackets, or blockquote prefixes disappear silently.\\n- **N51, line 35:** valid angle-bracket links containing an escaped `\\u003e` can disappear silently.\\n- **N52, line 56:** entity decoding incorrectly interprets backslash-escaped character references.\\n\\nEach can grant an incorrect `when-justified` exemption. Read-only probes compared the extracted production expressions with CommonMark rendering. These forms are supported by the [CommonMark specification](https://spec.commonmark.org/0.31.2/#links).\\n\\nThe closeout-policy tests passed across domain, CLI, and MCP packages; `go vet ./...` passed. Surface-check reported zero findings. The exact artifact-check exited 0, with provenance warnings and an older recorded change set; an additional explicit-range invocation failed with `signal: broken pipe`.\\n\\nRules applied: backend-go, security, documentation-style, and delivery-evidence under the review workflow. No repository changes or attestation were made.\\n\\n```pose-draft\\n{\\n  \\\"schema\\\": \\\"pose.review.draft/v1\\\",\\n  \\\"decision\\\": \\\"changes-requested\\\",\\n  \\\"findings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"N50\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"medium\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"blocker\\\",\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_adr_associations.go\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": 37,\\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"Recognize valid reference definitions or report them as unknown. The expression excludes multiline labels and escaped closing brackets, and its line anchor excludes definitions inside blockquotes. Read-only probes using the extracted production expressions returned no destinations for '[decision][decision label]\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n[decision\\\\\\\\nlabel]: ../adr/decision.md', '[decision][d]\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\u003e [d]: ../adr/decision.md', and an escaped-bracket label; CommonMark rendering resolves each to decision.md. Equivalent backlinks to pair.md also disappear. Because no match reaches add(), no diagnostic is produced. With two canonical members and no other association, the evaluator returns Known=true and Required=false, violating R3. Cover both directions and ensure unsupported local association syntax cannot prove absence.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"N51\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"medium\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"blocker\\\",\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_adr_associations.go\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": 35,\\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"Handle escaped angle brackets inside angle-bracket destinations without silently dropping the link. For '[decision](\\u003c../adr/decision.md#f\\\\\\\\\\u003e with space\\u003e)', CommonMark resolves the destination to decision.md with a fragment, but the extracted production expressions return no destinations. The angle branch stops at the escaped '\\u003e', while the bare branch cannot consume the spaces. '[program](\\u003c../roadmaps/pair.md#f\\\\\\\\\\u003e with space\\u003e)' fails identically in the reverse direction. No undecodable diagnostic is generated, so a two-member roadmap with only this association receives a known exemption. Parse the complete destination or fail closed and add forward/backward regression cases.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"N52\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"medium\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"blocker\\\",\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_adr_associations.go\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": 56,\\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"Preserve backslash-escaped ampersands while decoding character references. CommonMark resolves '[decision](../adr/decision\\\\\\\\\\u0026num;name.md)' to '../adr/decision\\u0026num;name.md', a permitted ADR basename. The implementation first applies html.UnescapeString, turning '\\u0026num;' into '#', then removes the backslash and strips the supposed fragment. A read-only decoding probe confirmed that the production path becomes '../adr/decision'; the extension predicate silently skips it. With that regular ADR present and no other association, the result is a known exemption rather than required review. Decode Markdown escapes and entities with their actual precedence, and cover escaped entity introducers. This is an unresolved part of R14-N48.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"N53\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"low\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"follow-up\\\",\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_adr_associations.go\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": 45,\\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"The existing F6 residual risk remains: links in code/comments count as associations, and destinations containing parentheses can become unknown. This conservatively requires extra review and does not itself grant an exemption. Inspection and the independently passing RoundTwelve/RoundFourteen regressions support retaining this limited over-enforcement risk.\\\",\\n      \\\"action\\\": \\\"Complete spec follow-up F6 with context-aware Markdown parsing while preserving fail-closed handling of unsupported local associations.\\\",\\n      \\\"owner\\\": \\\"@pose-maintainers\\\",\\n      \\\"review_by\\\": \\\"2026-12-13\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"prior_findings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R14-N48\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"partial\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"The exact percent-escape and character-reference examples now normalize correctly at closeout_adr_associations.go:50-65; TestCloseoutReviewPolicyRoundFifteen passed in the independently executed three-package test run. However, line 56 still decodes backslash-escaped entity introducers incorrectly. The read-only CommonMark/production-decoding probe for decision\\\\\\\\\\u0026num;name.md demonstrates the remaining silent exemption described in N52.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R14-N49\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"not-fixed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"closeout_adr_associations.go:45-47 deliberately reads code/comments as prose, and lines 191-193 and 266-268 conservatively reject parentheses. RoundTwelve and RoundFourteen regressions passed. Existing spec follow-up F6 remains applicable and is retained as accepted low risk N53.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"sweep\\\": \\\"Reviewed R1-R7, D1/D2, the accepted closeout ADR, the bounded-read ADR amendment, declared production changes, schemas, templates, manuals and scaffold copies. Traced CLI close and recovery, closeout-check, review-check, review verification, review-plan, attention/obligations, reached, nextCloses, roadmap gates, MCP closeout state, federated acceptance, readiness, portfolio projection and doctor through the shared decision and terminal projections. Checked recorded-review vetoes under never, always against singleton inheritance and unreviewed_milestones, mandatory-human and baseline protection, canonical members/transfers, unknown associations, receipt immutability, intent/status/receipt sequencing, historical closure, install/update/adopt/setup and schema preservation. Independently ran closeout-policy tests across pose/cli/mcpserver and go vet; compared production Markdown extraction and decoding against CommonMark for forward and reverse forms. Inspected sealed strict validation: 213 checks passed. Ran required artifact/surface commands and suggest-review. No further established blocker was found outside N50-N52; no repository changes or attestation were made.\\\",\\n  \\\"criteria\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assumption-integrity\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Distinguished independently verified code/tests from the sealed full-validation run. The original N48 examples pass, but escaped entity introducers remain unresolved. F6 is accepted only for conservative over-enforcement. Global remote backlink discovery and nonparticipating external writers remain outside the accepted design. Artifact-command limitations are disclosed rather than treated as proof of current-range reconciliation.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-concurrency\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/writer-coordination-and-atomic-publication-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Inspected guarded authorization rechecks, ExpectAbsent receipt publication and intent/status/receipt sequencing. Existing coordination and bounded read-view mechanisms remain in use; interrupted publication stays incomplete and existing receipts are not overwritten.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-contracts\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Schema 5 explicitly migrates policy semantics, schemas 1-4 preserve legacy behavior, CLI configuration writes the pair together, and MCP additions remain projections. Reviewed receipt and review-plan schema additions and transport parity tests.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-input-errors\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N50\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"N50-N52 show supported association inputs becoming silent absence rather than resolved associations or actionable unknown diagnostics.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-integration-impact\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Traced shared domain evaluation through CLI/MCP, receipt-backed producer proof, canonical transfer targets and aggregate dependency closure. The established parser defects affect the common domain result rather than creating transport-specific behavior.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-observability\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N50\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Missed reference definitions produce no unknown-association diagnostic, concealing why review was incorrectly exempted.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"compatibility\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-policy-adoption-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Inspected explicit adoption, update preservation, legacy sealed-plan recognition, reference/transfer toggles and previous-release tests. Older engines intentionally refuse newly adopted schema-5 instances; existing legacy instances are not silently adopted.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"correctness\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N51\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Valid local Markdown associations can disappear and incorrectly exempt aggregate review; N50 and N52 establish additional cases.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"design-causality\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"D1 separates explicit closure from independent review using deterministic thresholds. D2 reuses the resolver and adoption surfaces and adds receipts because milestone close previously lacked a persisted transition. Shared evaluation addresses inconsistent projections; the remaining defects concern association recognition within that design.\\\",\\n      \\\"mappings\\\": [\\n        {\\n          \\\"delta\\\": \\\"SD-3ce6ee69\\\",\\n          \\\"basis\\\": \\\"R4\\\",\\n          \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"mapped\\\",\\n          \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The spec's implementation reconciliation links explicit-close delivery to the measured read-budget refusal. The ADR amendment documents the bounded increase to 1 GiB and the separate digest-only follow-up.\\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"delta\\\": \\\"SD-c74440ab\\\",\\n          \\\"basis\\\": \\\"R3\\\",\\n          \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"mapped\\\",\\n          \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The roadmap template exposes adrs: [] for the explicit associations used by the when-justified rule.\\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"delta\\\": \\\"SD-ec2d86f4\\\",\\n          \\\"basis\\\": \\\"R1\\\",\\n          \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"mapped\\\",\\n          \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The accepted ADR records policy location, deterministic modes, defaults, historical compatibility and authority protections.\\\"\\n        }\\n      ]\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"documentation\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/distributed-instructions-parity-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Compared English/Portuguese manuals, scaffold copies and roadmap templates with policy names, thresholds, adoption, explicit close and receipt behavior. The documented association contract is clear; N50-N52 are implementation failures against it.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"operability\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N50\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"An operator receives a known exemption without the missing-association explanation needed to correct the input or require review.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"requirements\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N50\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"R3 is not fully satisfied: explicit reference-style associations can be lost. N51-N52 establish further R3 failures despite the passing registered suite.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"scope\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Compared declared artifacts and implementation with R1-R7 and D1/D2. Policy, receipts, reader integration, setup/doctor and documentation support aggregate closeout. The bounded-read change is explicitly reconciled in the spec. No global ADR identity framework or MCP configuration/write tool was introduced.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"security\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N52\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Incorrect destination decoding can weaken the review authority gate by interpreting a real association as absent.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"solution-proportionality\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"A shared evaluator and immutable terminal receipt are proportionate to separating review from close. Reusing adopt/setup and the resolver avoids unnecessary new frameworks. Metadata alone would lose existing Markdown associations. A narrow extractor is sufficient only if unsupported local forms fail closed; N50-N52 identify violations requiring correction. Remote backlink inventory remains deliberately excluded.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"tools\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"artifact-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit --strict\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Ran the exact command; exit 0. Output included artifact.claims=46, artifact.observed=195 and artifact.findings=920, with provenance warnings. It reported recorded change set cs-b4c4da227b9c ending at 9b8eb4c0, so this is a successful command exit, not proof of warning-free reconciliation of the sealed range. An additional --from/--to invocation failed with 'git diff failed: signal: broken pipe'.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-design\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Did not run an assessment writer under the read-only boundary. Examined the spec, ADRs, code and sealed structure:design-584572eae6be33ac, and supplied all structural mappings.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-discover\\\",\\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Did not regenerate assessment artifacts. Inspected component sources, validation registration and sealed pose-mcp evidence directly.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-integrate\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Did not run the assessment writer. Traced CLI/MCP/federation integration and inspected sealed integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration; independently reran the three-package policy tests.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-tech-debt\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Did not write assessment artifacts. Inspected changed production markers and explicit spec follow-ups, including F5 bounded-read capacity debt and F6 parser over-enforcement.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"closeout-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Completion gate depends on POSE recording and verifying this review conclusion; no attestation was recorded by this review.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"review-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Completion gate must follow the recorded review conclusion.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"suggest-review\\\",\\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Exit 0; selected backend-go, security and documentation-style under the review workflow. Also applied delivery-evidence and consulted knowledge governance.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"surface-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Ran pose surface-check --spec pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit --strict; exit 0 with surface.targets=1, surface.results=213 and surface.findings=0. Composition evidence: integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration. Reachability evidence: reachability:pose-mcp/go/closeout-plan-reachability. This does not cover the newly established parser cases.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"validate\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Disposed from the sealed strict producer run as requested. Inspected delivery-validation.json: 213 executed, 213 passed, zero failed/errored/skipped. Did not rerun the repository-writing validation producer. Independently executed go test ./internal/pose ./internal/cli ./internal/mcpserver -run TestCloseoutReviewPolicy -count=1; all three packages passed. go vet ./... also passed.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"validate\\\",\\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"build:pose-mcp/go/build\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The sealed strict run supplies the component's registered build, unit, integration and e2e evidence. Current targeted domain/CLI/MCP tests and go vet passed independently. Passing checks do not resolve the uncovered R3 cases N50-N52.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\\n```\",\n.pose/review-runs/rrn-c904db5a26d63b93.json:106:  \"output\": \"decision: approved\\n\\nR3-N3 is fixed. No new defects found.\\n\\nThe cache tests passed under the race detector, including 100 repetitions of the concurrency regressions. `go vet ./internal/pose`, the exact-range artifact check, and the surface check passed. The artifact check reported only repository-wide provenance warnings.\\n\\nApplied the review workflow and Go, security, documentation, and delivery-evidence rules. Full validation uses the sealed evidence; the reported 249-second benchmark was not independently reproduced. The repository remains unchanged.\\n\\n```pose-draft\\n{\\n  \\\"schema\\\": \\\"pose.review.draft/v1\\\",\\n  \\\"decision\\\": \\\"approved\\\",\\n  \\\"findings\\\": [],\\n  \\\"prior_findings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R3-N3\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/kept_cache.go:55-77 counts completed kept values and enforces the bound on completion while preserving pending entries. TestAConcurrentBurstKeepsNoMoreThanTheBound passed under go test -race, including 100 repetitions alongside the other coordination regressions.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"sweep\\\": \\\"Reviewed R1-R6, D1, the full implementation diff, all four cache keys and callers, completion-time eviction, concurrent misses, declined-result recovery, shallow and unresolved HEAD handling, moved refs, tag-list versus standalone resolution, snapshot copy isolation, bundle-loss attribution, production composition, validation-matrix coverage, and adjacent Git readers. Ran targeted race tests, 100 repetitions of coordination regressions, go vet ./internal/pose, context resolution, artifact-check with the exact supplied range, surface-check, and suggest review. Consulted sealed full-validation evidence. No repository changes or attestation were made.\\\",\\n  \\\"criteria\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assumption-integrity\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/federated-proof-reads-each-input-once-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Verified content-based keys, fresh ref resolution, raw-history Git reads, failure non-retention and copy isolation. The spec records the performance measurement; its external benchmark was not independently reproduced. Per-scope check recomputation remains explicitly outside scope.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-concurrency\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/federated-proof-reads-each-input-once-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Inspected mutex and channel publication, coordinated retries and pending-entry preservation. Targeted race tests and 100 repetitions of coordination regressions passed. The helper introduces no background worker lifecycle.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-contracts\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/federated-proof-reads-each-input-once-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Standalone and listed tag resolution retain equivalent outcomes; snapshot and material callers retain their existing result contracts.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-input-errors\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/federated-proof-reads-each-input-once-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Unreadable material, failed peels and incomplete snapshots are retried. Missing snapshots preserve typed errors, and invalid bundle content preserves its loss classification.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-integration-impact\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/federated-proof-reads-each-input-once-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Inspected CLI hook registration, graph material recomputation, archived-fragment loading and review-header consumers. Surface-check reported one target and zero findings.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-observability\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/typed-diagnostics-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Existing returned diagnostics remain intact; cached header losses receive the current file's artifact path. No new logging or sensitive diagnostic payload was introduced.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"compatibility\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/federated-proof-reads-each-input-once-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Examined CLI registration, file results, tag errors and snapshot serialization. Changes are internal memoization with no public schema or command migration.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"correctness\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/federated-proof-reads-each-input-once-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Reviewed positive and negative cache paths and independently ran the targeted tests under the race detector.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"design-causality\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-45ebef919f284a6d\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"D1 identifies repeated material, snapshot, tag-peel and JSON work. The four caches address those measured sources directly; fresh ref reads preserve currency, and the shared helper supplies R5 bounds and R6 coordination. No structural delta facts were listed in the brief.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"documentation\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-45ebef919f284a6d\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The spec's requirements, implementation plan, review remediation history and permanent validation command match runtime behavior. No operational command or public contract changed.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"operability\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/federated-proof-reads-each-input-once-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Failed reads remain recoverable rather than poisoning process caches; existing actionable errors remain available. Retained values are bounded and incomplete computations remain coordinated.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"requirements\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/federated-proof-reads-each-input-once-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Mapped R1-R4 to their material, snapshot, tag and header regressions; R5 to completion-time eviction and burst coverage; R6 to concurrent-miss, recovery and failing-read regressions. The external performance result is recorded in the spec.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"scope\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-45ebef919f284a6d\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The implementation stays within the four planned caches and their shared coordination helper. Exact-range artifact-check passed with no non-warning findings. The documented per-scope recomputation follow-up was not expanded into this change.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"security\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/federated-proof-reads-each-input-once-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Examined input-derived keys, Git argument construction, raw-history policy, fresh refs, snapshot isolation and loss attribution. No new authority source, dependency, secret handling or persistent storage was introduced.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"solution-proportionality\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-45ebef919f284a6d\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"A small shared memoization helper is sufficient for the four repeated operations and avoids persistent invalidation machinery. D1 explains why fewer caches did not meet the measured target. The design would need reconsideration if results gained mutable inputs not represented in their keys.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"tools\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"artifact-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-federated-proof-reads-each-input-once --from bf2ff02c31752a3343b0200fa62b27c220ce2453 --to 0bc412bc507b2c91f2bf98ad51494ecb2bed0313 --strict --json\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Exit 0; all 958 reported findings were warnings. Repeated with the exact supplied range after the default selector included a later sealing commit.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-design\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-45ebef919f284a6d\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Consulted sealed design evidence and inspected D1 and the implementation directly; did not regenerate assessment artifacts.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-discover\\\",\\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Preserved the read-only review boundary; inspected the mapped component and sealed build, unit and integration evidence.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-integrate\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/federated-proof-reads-each-input-once-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Reviewed production callers and sealed integration evidence directly. No public inter-module contract changed; assessment files were not regenerated.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-tech-debt\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Did not regenerate assessment artifacts. Searched affected production files for TODO, FIXME, stub and panic markers and inspected the spec's existing follow-up.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"closeout-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Requires the completed review attestation; this review returns a draft and does not record one.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"review-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Requires the completed review attestation; POSE must record and verify the conclusion first.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"suggest-review\\\",\\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Selected the review workflow and security, documentation-style and backend-go rules.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"surface-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/federated-proof-reads-each-input-once-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Ran pose surface-check --spec pose-federated-proof-reads-each-input-once --strict; reported one target, 225 results and zero findings.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"validate\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Reused the sealed successful strict-validation run rather than rewriting repository validation artifacts. Independently supplemented it with targeted race tests and go vet.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"validate\\\",\\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/federated-proof-reads-each-input-once-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Reused the sealed module validation evidence, including the permanent cache integration check and sealed build and unit results. Independent targeted race tests and go vet passed.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\\n```\",\n.pose/review-runs/rrn-cd0ac9394ca5892b.json:39:      \"scope\": \"spec:pose-assess-leaves-sealed-checkouts-alone\",\n.pose/review-runs/rrn-cd0ac9394ca5892b.json:86:  \"brief_notes\": \"Implementer notes (Claude Opus 5.5, the lead). Use them as context only; the judgment is yours.\\n\\nScope: spec `pose-assess-leaves-sealed-checkouts-alone` (R1–R4, decisions D1–D2, residual limit L1 in the Final Report). Reviewer runs used to fail with \\\"the run changed files in the sealed worktree\\\" after a planned `pose assess` persisted `.pose/assessments/*` and `.pose/state/*` into the sealed checkout.\\n- R1: `pose assess discover|integrate|tech-debt --no-persist` prints the result without writing (`internal/cli/assess.go`, `assessPersists`).\\n- R2: in the sealed checkout of a delegated review (`POSE_SEALED_CHECKOUT`, already set by the dispatch) those commands never persist and say so on standard error; `init`, `snapshot` and `request` refuse. The Store's assessment writers (`SaveComponentState`, `GenerateConsolidatedAssessment`, `SaveIntegrationMatrix`, `SaveTechDebtReport`) also refuse there (`internal/pose/assessment_sealed.go`).\\n- R3: the review plan's assessment tools carry `--no-persist` (`reviewToolArgs`).\\n- R4: `TestAssessLeavesTheSealedCheckoutUnchanged` hashes the whole tree before and after every command.\\nEach guard has a test that failed with it mutated out. The full `go test ./...` of `pose-mcp` passed.\\n\\nPlease check in particular that no assess path still writes in a sealed checkout, that `--update-state` cannot bypass the guard, and that persisting runs outside a sealed checkout behave as before.\\n\\nThe planned assessment tools of this bundle now carry `--no-persist`, so you may run them in the sealed checkout: that is also a live test of R2 and R3.\\n\\nBefore you finish, run `\\\"$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\\\" review draft-check --draft -` on your final message (pipe it on standard input) and fix every reason it reports.\\n\\nDraft format rules, enforced by the conclusion preflight:\\n- New findings use short unprefixed IDs (N1, N2, …). Round-prefixed IDs go only in `prior_findings`, and only for the findings the brief lists under \\\"Findings to account for\\\", with exactly id, status and evidence.\\n- Structural-delta mappings go inside the criterion that answers them, with `basis` set to a requirement or a decision of this spec (R1–R4, D1, D2).\\n- A criterion scoped to a component cites evidence from that component only.\\n\\nSandbox limits: the checkout is sealed and read-only. Never `cd`; keep the checkout root as the working directory. Keep test runs focused (`go -C pose-mcp test ./internal/cli ./internal/pose -run 'Assess|ReviewPlanRunsAssessments'`, `go -C pose-mcp vet ./internal/cli ./internal/pose`), and let every command you start finish before you end: a process still running when you end makes the run unconcludable. A tool you cannot rerun in the sandbox is a limit of the run, not a defect of the subject: cite the sealed evidence that covers it, then decide on the code itself.\\n\",\n.pose/review-runs/rrn-cd0ac9394ca5892b.json:92:  \"scope\": \"spec:pose-assess-leaves-sealed-checkouts-alone\",\n.pose/review-runs/rrn-cd0ac9394ca5892b.json:108:  \"output\": \"decision: changes-requested\\n\\n**Finding N1 — medium, blocker:** [discovery.go](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-1460578027/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/discovery.go:658) exports `GenerateComponentAssessmentMarkdown`, which creates and writes an assessment file without the sealed-checkout guard. A caller can therefore mutate the sealed checkout directly, bypassing the guards on the other Store writers. This leaves the Store-level guarantee in D1 incomplete.\\n\\nThe focused Go tests and vet passed: `go -C pose-mcp test ./internal/cli ./internal/pose -run 'Assess|ReviewPlanRunsAssessments'` and `go -C pose-mcp vet ./internal/cli ./internal/pose`. The design assessment reported no structural deltas. The final draft preflight **accepted** the conclusion draft below. I did not record an attestation.\\n\\n**Execution issue:** I ran assessment commands with the installed `pose` executable, which predates the reviewed `--no-persist` change. It printed that it wrote artifacts and changed these tracked files:\\n\\n- [.pose/assessments/README.md](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-1460578027/worktree/.pose/assessments/README.md)\\n- [.pose/assessments/consolidated.md](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-1460578027/worktree/.pose/assessments/consolidated.md)\\n- [.pose/assessments/integrations.md](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-1460578027/worktree/.pose/assessments/integrations.md)\\n- [.pose/assessments/pose-mcp.md](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-1460578027/worktree/.pose/assessments/pose-mcp.md)\\n- [.pose/assessments/technical-debt.md](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-1460578027/worktree/.pose/assessments/technical-debt.md)\\n- [.pose/state/components/pose-mcp.json](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-1460578027/worktree/.pose/state/components/pose-mcp.json)\\n- [.pose/state/integrations.json](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-1460578027/worktree/.pose/state/integrations.json)\\n- [.pose/state/technical-debt.json](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-1460578027/worktree/.pose/state/technical-debt.json)\\n\\nI left them untouched under the no-edit boundary. The artifact-check and surface-check attempts did not return a captured completion status, so the draft records them as failed; this is a review-run limitation, not an additional subject-code finding.\\n\\n```pose-draft\\n{\\n  \\\"schema\\\": \\\"pose.review.draft/v1\\\",\\n  \\\"decision\\\": \\\"changes-requested\\\",\\n  \\\"findings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"N1\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"medium\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"blocker\\\",\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/discovery.go\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": 658,\\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"GenerateComponentAssessmentMarkdown writes .pose/assessments/\\u003cslug\\u003e.md without refuseSealedAssessmentWrite, so a Store caller can still mutate the sealed checkout despite the guards on SaveComponentState and the other assessment writers.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"criteria\\\": [\\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"assumption-integrity\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/sealed-checkout-child-evidence-integration\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Verified review_dispatch.go appends POSE_SEALED_CHECKOUT for the checkout and IsSealedCheckout resolves and compares the paths. L1 remains an accepted limitation: a reviewer process that clears the variable can write, with the dispatch tree comparison detecting the mutation.\\\"},\\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"backend-concurrency\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The change adds no shared mutable state or asynchronous lifecycle. The no-persist paths skip publication; the focused Assess and ReviewPlanRunsAssessments Go tests passed.\\\"},\\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"backend-contracts\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"N1\\\"},\\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"backend-input-errors\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Sealed CLI write commands return a refusal, while Store assessment writes use the typed ErrSealedAssessmentWrite error. Focused CLI and pose package tests passed.\\\"},\\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"backend-integration-impact\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/sealed-checkout-child-evidence-integration\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The change stays within the pose-mcp assessment CLI and Store boundary; sealed integration evidence covers delegated review checkout handling.\\\"},\\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"backend-observability\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/typed-diagnostics-integration\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The CLI emits a persistence hint on stderr and direct Store callers receive a typed error with a remediation hint.\\\"},\\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"compatibility\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The three flags are additive; persisting paths remain the default outside a sealed checkout, JSON output keeps the same result shape, and no stored record schema changes.\\\"},\\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"correctness\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"N1\\\"},\\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"design-causality\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"structure:design-f5a95f8918bdd747\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"R1/R2 address persisted assessment files as the cause of sealed-run failures; D1's CLI skip plus Store guard is the smallest direct backstop, and D2 makes planned commands safe when copied. The design assessment observed no structural deltas, so there are no delta mappings.\\\",\\\"mappings\\\":[]},\\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"documentation\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/distributed-instructions-parity-integration\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Compared the English and pt-BR manuals and embedded scaffold copies with the CLI behavior and help entries; they describe --no-persist, sealed checkout behavior, refusal commands, and planned flags consistently.\\\"},\\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"operability\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The refusal paths explain why writes are blocked and the Store error names --no-persist. The focused tests passed.\\\"},\\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"requirements\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"N1\\\"},\\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"scope\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"structure:design-f5a95f8918bdd747\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Changes are confined to the assessment CLI and Store writers, review plan, help, and the specified manuals/scaffold copies. The one omitted writer guard is recorded as N1.\\\"},\\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"security\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"No new external input or credential handling was added. The sealed root comparison is path-normalized; L1 is disclosed under assumption-integrity. N1 is a sealed-worktree integrity gap, not an input-validation or secret-exposure issue.\\\"},\\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"solution-proportionality\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"structure:design-f5a95f8918bdd747\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The two-layer CLI and Store guard is proportionate to the failure cause; a CLI-only flag would leave other Store callers able to publish. It avoids a broader filesystem policy. The choice would be incomplete unless every exported assessment writer, including the markdown writer in N1, is guarded.\\\"}\\n  ],\\n  \\\"tools\\\": [\\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"artifact-check\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"failed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-assess-leaves-sealed-checkouts-alone --strict\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The installed pose executable did not return a captured completion status; the checkout was subsequently changed by that older executable, so no pass can be claimed.\\\"},\\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"assess-design\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"structure:design-f5a95f8918bdd747\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The design assessment returned observed with no structural deltas.\\\"},\\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"assess-discover\\\",\\\"component\\\":\\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"not-used\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"command:pose assess discover --no-persist --component pose-mcp\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The installed pose executable predates the reviewed --no-persist change and wrote assessment artifacts; its output is not valid evidence for the reviewed implementation.\\\"},\\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"assess-integrate\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"not-used\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"command:pose assess integrate --no-persist\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The installed pose executable predates the reviewed --no-persist change and wrote assessment artifacts; its output is not valid evidence for the reviewed implementation.\\\"},\\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"assess-tech-debt\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"not-used\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"command:pose assess tech-debt --no-persist\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The installed pose executable predates the reviewed --no-persist change and wrote assessment artifacts; its output is not valid evidence for the reviewed implementation.\\\"},\\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"closeout-check\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"deferred\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"command:pose closeout-check spec:pose-assess-leaves-sealed-checkouts-alone\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The closeout check requires completion of this review and must remain deferred because no attestation was recorded.\\\"},\\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"review-check\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"deferred\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"command:pose review-check spec:pose-assess-leaves-sealed-checkouts-alone\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The review check requires completion of this review and must remain deferred because no attestation was recorded.\\\"},\\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"suggest-review\\\",\\\"component\\\":\\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Rule selection returned backend-go, security, and documentation-style for pose-mcp.\\\"},\\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"surface-check\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"failed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/sealed-checkout-child-evidence-integration\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The attempted installed-CLI check did not return a captured completion status; the stale executable makes the result untrustworthy.\\\"},\\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"validate\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"build:pose-mcp/go/build\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Cited the bundle's sealed validation evidence because a fresh strict run could not be safely trusted after the installed CLI changed the checkout.\\\"},\\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"validate\\\",\\\"component\\\":\\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Cited the bundle's sealed module validation evidence; the focused current-source Go tests and vet passed separately.\\\"}\\n  ]\\n}\\n```\",\n.pose/review-runs/rrn-5194c12d6de2fcf7.json:106:  \"output\": \"**decision: changes-requested**\\n\\nThe code change is sound, but the plan's required `artifact-check` fails in strict mode on one error. That error alone blocks approval. The other three findings are low severity and proposed as follow-ups.\\n\\n## How I reviewed it\\n\\n- I read the full diff for the range `50768fbb..7d5f0193`, the new `VerifyReviewRunProofForReading` (`pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_run_provenance.go:668`), both verifiers, the closeout's own verifier (`verifyRunReviewReference`, line 687), and every caller of the new function and of `VerifyReviewRunProof`.\\n- I ran `pose artifact-check --spec … --strict` twice: once with its default range and once pinned to the sealed range. Both exit 1.\\n- I could not run `go test` or `pose assess design`: this profile denied both. Test results below therefore come from the sealed evidence, mainly `integration:pose-mcp/go/verdict-readers-sealed-integration` (the two new tests) and `unit:pose-mcp/go/test`.\\n\\n## The implementer's soundness questions\\n\\n- **No reader's answer backs a new attestation (the falsifier of D1).** Confirmed. There are three callers:\\n  - `cmdReviewRunProof` only prints the result.\\n  - `verifiedVerdictOf` (`delegated_verdicts.go:345`) only fills an `Issuer` field.\\n  - `recoveredReviewConclusion` (`review_conclusions.go:510`) also only fills `Issuer`, and only after `runBackedReviewBlockers` has already passed the existing attestation.\\n  - The paths that create a verdict still ask the live question: `concludeReviewRun` (`review_conclusions.go:568`), `verifiedVerdictRun` (`delegated_verdicts.go:428`) and fulfilment (`delegated_review_request.go:300`).\\n- **Fail closed.** Confirmed. If the run can't be loaded, the function returns the error. If the bundle can't be read or the scope's done-ness can't be decided, it falls back to the live verifier, which fails on the same bundle read.\\n- **The reader asks the same question as the closeout.** Confirmed. `runApprovalAsSealed` dispatches between the same two verifiers that `verifyRunReviewReference` uses.\\n- **The stated gap.** The adjudication/smoke gap is real. It also means the change at `delegated_verdicts.go:345` has no visible effect when a done scope has drifted: `verifiedVerdictProof` refuses first, through the live check. The spec admits this, but the manual does not (F3).\\n- **The two new tests discriminate.** A reader that always asked the live question would fail the done-scope test. One that always asked the sealed question would fail the open-scope test.\\n\\n## Defects\\n\\n| id | severity | file:line | summary |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| F1 | medium (blocker) | `.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-verdict-readers-ask-the-sealed-question.md:50` | The spec declares itself `created`, but it was added in `af36fc0b`, outside the range. This range only modifies it. Strict `artifact-check` reports `[err] error action-mismatch`, so the required tool fails. Every other finding in that output (938) is a repo-wide orphan warning. |\\n| F2 | low | `pose-mcp/internal/pose/retained_run_approval_test.go:144` | R2 says expiry is not checked on the sealed path, and the trace cites the drift test for it. That test never uses a proof with a TTL or a clock past expiry, so R2 has no behavioural test. |\\n| F3 | low | `POSE.md:1063` (also `pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/POSE.md:1050` and both pt-BR copies) | The manual says \\\"the other readers of a run's verdict\\\" ask the sealed question. The adjudication/smoke readers (`verifiedVerdictProof`) still ask the live one, and the manual does not mention this gap. |\\n| F4 | low | `pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_run_provenance.go:589` | The sealed verifier, now reached by `pose review run-proof`, skips the directory symlink refusal (`ensureReviewArtifactDirIn`) that the live verifier does at line 367. Only the final file is checked with `Lstat`. The signature and run-digest binding still prevent forgery, so this is a hardening gap that predates this change. |\\n\\n## Required tools\\n\\n- **`artifact-check`: failed** (F1).\\n- **`validate`: passed**, from the sealed `unit:pose-mcp/go/test`.\\n- **`review-check` and `closeout-check`: deferred** until after the attestation.\\n- **Recommended assess/suggest tools: not used.** Running them was denied.\\n\\nThe fix for F1 is a one-word edit to line 50 of the spec (`created:` → `modified:`), after which strict `artifact-check` should be re-run.\\n\\n```pose-draft\\n{\\n  \\\"schema\\\": \\\"pose.review.draft/v1\\\",\\n  \\\"decision\\\": \\\"changes-requested\\\",\\n  \\\"findings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"F1\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"medium\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"blocker\\\",\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\".pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-verdict-readers-ask-the-sealed-question.md\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": 50,\\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"The spec's own artifact is declared 'created' but was added in af36fc0b, before the range; the range only modifies it. 'pose artifact-check --spec pose-verdict-readers-ask-the-sealed-question --strict' exits 1 with '[err] error action-mismatch' on this path (the other 938 findings are repo-wide orphan warnings), so the required artifact-check does not pass. Declare it 'modified:'.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"F2\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"low\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"follow-up\\\",\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/retained_run_approval_test.go\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": 144,\\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"R2 (expiry not checked on the sealed path) is traced to TestTheProofReaderAndTheCloseoutAgreeOnADoneScopeWithDrift, which never uses a proof with a TTL or a clock past expiry; R2 is backed only by code reading and the manual, not by a behavioural test.\\\",\\n      \\\"action\\\": \\\"Add a test: a done scope whose run proof has a TTL, read at a time past expiry; VerifyReviewRunProofForReading succeeds and VerifyReviewRunProof refuses.\\\",\\n      \\\"owner\\\": \\\"@pose-maintainers\\\",\\n      \\\"review_by\\\": \\\"2027-02-08\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"F3\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"low\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"follow-up\\\",\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"POSE.md\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": 1063,\\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"The manual (also scaffold/dist/POSE.md:1050 and both pt-BR copies) says 'pose review run-proof and the other readers of a run's verdict' ask the sealed question, but the adjudication/smoke readers (verifiedVerdictProof via SpecAdjudications/SmokeResults -\\u003e verifiedVerdictRun) still ask the live question. As a result, the change at delegated_verdicts.go:345 has no visible effect for a drifted done scope. The gap is in the spec but not in the manual.\\\",\\n      \\\"action\\\": \\\"Narrow the manual sentence to the readers actually changed, or close the follow-up that makes verifiedVerdictProof ask the sealed question for done scopes.\\\",\\n      \\\"owner\\\": \\\"@pose-maintainers\\\",\\n      \\\"review_by\\\": \\\"2027-02-08\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"F4\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"low\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"follow-up\\\",\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_run_provenance.go\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": 589,\\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"VerifyReviewRunProofAsSealed, now reached by 'pose review run-proof' for done scopes, does not call ensureReviewArtifactDirIn(..., false) like VerifyReviewRunProof does at line 367, so a symlinked proof directory is not refused (readBoundedRegularIn Lstats only the final file). Signature and run-digest binding still prevent forgery; this is an inconsistency in hardening that predates this change.\\\",\\n      \\\"action\\\": \\\"Apply the same proof-directory symlink refusal on the sealed path (and in VerifyReviewRunProofRecord).\\\",\\n      \\\"owner\\\": \\\"@pose-maintainers\\\",\\n      \\\"review_by\\\": \\\"2027-02-08\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"criteria\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assumption-integrity\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/verdict-readers-sealed-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Examined the assumptions. Verified: no caller of VerifyReviewRunProofForReading uses its result to back a new attestation (three callers only print or fill Issuer metadata; conclude/adjudication/smoke/fulfilment stay on VerifyReviewRunProof at review_conclusions.go:568, delegated_verdicts.go:428, delegated_review_request.go:300); an unreadable bundle falls back to the live verifier, which fails closed. Unresolved but stated: the adjudication/smoke gap (spec Known gaps). Accepted risk: low follow-ups F2-F4.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-concurrency\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/verdict-readers-sealed-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The new function is a read-only dispatcher with no shared state, locks or goroutines. A scope that turns done between the dispatch check and the verification only changes which read-only question is answered; no write depends on it.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-contracts\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/verdict-readers-sealed-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The output shape of the 'pose review run-proof' CLI is unchanged (same ReviewRunAssurance rendering). Its meaning for done scopes changes on purpose and is disclosed in the changelog (category fixed) and the manual. The new exported Go function is additive.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-input-errors\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/verdict-readers-sealed-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Errors from LoadProvenanceReviewRun, runProofPath and the verifiers propagate unchanged; when the bundle cannot be read or lifecycle detection fails, the function falls back to the live verifier, which is fail-closed (review_run_provenance.go:674-677).\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-integration-impact\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-approval-survives-routine-drift-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The CLI, delegated verdict and conclusion-recovery consumers now share the closeout's dispatch (runApprovalAsSealed). Retained-approval and conclusion integration checks remain sealed as passing.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-observability\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Failures still return the verifier's bounded 'run provenance: ...' reasons; no new logging, and no secrets are exposed.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"compatibility\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/verdict-readers-sealed-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Examined the CLI and MCP surfaces: no flag, file format or tool schema changed; open scopes keep the live answer (TestTheProofReaderKeepsTheLiveQuestionForAnOpenScope). The more permissive reading for done scopes is documented in the manual (EN/pt-BR, root and scaffold) and in the changelog.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"correctness\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/verdict-readers-sealed-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The done-scope test shows the closeout approves, the live verifier refuses and the reader agrees with the closeout; the open-scope test shows the reader refuses after drift. Together they rule out an always-live or always-sealed reader.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"design-causality\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/verdict-readers-sealed-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Cause: the readers called VerifyReviewRunProof while the closeout used runApprovalAsSealed to choose between sealed and live. Design: one function that reuses the closeout's exact predicate and verifiers, so the two cannot diverge (R1); D1 drops expiry on the sealed path because the sealed verifier never checked it (R2). No structural fact ids were listed for mapping; the sealed design assessment is structure:design-d354476c9c16ae8a.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"documentation\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"F3\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"operability\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/verdict-readers-sealed-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Examined the CLI error path (cli/review_run_provenance.go:76-80): failures still render 'pose review run proof: \\u003creason\\u003e' with exit 1; the manual explains when the sealed versus live answer applies.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"requirements\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"F2\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"scope\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"F1\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"security\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"F4\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"solution-proportionality\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/verdict-readers-sealed-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"An 18-line dispatcher reusing existing verifiers, plus three one-line call-site swaps, is the smallest sufficient change; the alternative of inlining the predicate at each caller would duplicate it. No speculative extension. The choice would be invalidated if any caller used the reading answer to back a new attestation (D1 falsifier); none does today.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"tools\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"artifact-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"failed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-verdict-readers-ask-the-sealed-question --strict\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Exit 1. The same error appears when pinned to the sealed range (--from 50768fbb --to 7d5f0193): '[err] error action-mismatch .pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-verdict-readers-ask-the-sealed-question.md: declared artifact action is absent from the attributed Git change sets'. See F1.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-design\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Recommended; running it was denied in this profile. The sealed structure evidence structure:design-d354476c9c16ae8a exists.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-discover\\\",\\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Recommended; not run. The review relied on reading the code directly.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-integrate\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Recommended; not run. Integration was judged from sealed integration evidence.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-tech-debt\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Recommended; not run. The change is small and was read in full.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"closeout-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Its precondition is a completed review; it cannot pass before the attestation.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"review-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Its precondition is a completed review; it cannot pass before the attestation.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"suggest-review\\\",\\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Recommended; not run. The review scope was taken from the sealed change list.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"validate\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Strict validation is sealed as passing in the bundle.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"validate\\\",\\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Strict pose-mcp validation is sealed as passing, including integration:pose-mcp/go/verdict-readers-sealed-integration.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\\n```\",\n.pose/review-runs/rrn-41cc27dbae7fdd47.json:118:  \"output\": \"decision: changes-requested\\n\\nI'm requesting changes. The code works and the focused tests pass. But the main promise of R1, that the review profile blocks writes outside the run directory, doesn't hold in a real review run: test code run by the reviewer can write to the main repository's Git data.\\n\\n## What I ran (this run is the R3 evidence)\\n\\nAll commands ran inside the mandatory sandbox. Go's cache and temp files were in the run's private scratch directory.\\n\\n| Command | Result |\\n|---|---|\\n| `go test ./internal/pose -run TestSandboxedReview -count=1 -v` (in pose-mcp) | All 8 `TestSandboxedReview*` tests pass (0.091s) |\\n| `go vet ./internal/pose` | exit 0 |\\n| `touch ../SANDBOX_PROBE` | `Read-only file system`: writes to the sealed source are blocked by the OS. Writing to scratch works. |\\n| `pose artifact-check --spec … --strict` | exit 0. Only warnings for files that already had no spec claim. It took the change-set head as `4a4077c4`, a later commit holding only sealing chores. |\\n| `pose surface-check --spec … --strict` | exit 0, 209 results, 0 findings |\\n| `pose assess design --spec … --json` | input digest `b05eed146f58614e` matches the sealed `structure:design-b05eed146f58614e` |\\n| `pose suggest review --path pose-mcp` | exit 0 |\\n| `pose assess integrate` | Refused: it can't save `.pose/state/integrations.json` because the checkout is read-only |\\n| `pose validate --strict --module pose-mcp --jobs 4` | **exit 1**: 197 pass, 10 fail, 2 time out at 600s (`test`, `optional-worktree-runtime-integration`) |\\n| `pose validate --strict --jobs 4` | **exit 1**: 200 pass, the same 10 fail and 2 time-outs. All five other modules pass. |\\n| `go clean -cache` (last command, inside the sandbox) | exit 0; 8.0K left in the cache |\\n\\n**The validation failures come from this sandbox, not from the change.** None of the failing tests touch the changed code:\\n- Inside the sandbox, `/tmp` and `/home` show up as owned by `nobody(65534)`, which makes POSE refuse \\\"belongs to another user\\\".\\n- The proxy returned 403 when the install journey tried to list published releases.\\n- The runtime host couldn't start, and the full suite ran past 600s.\\n\\nStill, the validate tools did not pass in this run, so I report them as `failed`. The sealed evidence shows they passed on the implementer's machine.\\n\\n## Defects\\n\\n**F1 (high): the sandbox can write to the main repository's Git data.**\\n- Where: `.pose/policy/delegation.json:287` and `:317`, the `review_profile` wrappers.\\n- When the review runs in a Git worktree, Claude Code automatically adds the main repo's `.git` to the sandbox's write allow-list. This session's sandbox config lists `/home/go/IdeaProjects/harne8/pose-dist/.git`.\\n- I checked without writing anything (`test -w`, which reports read-only mounts):\\n  - **writable:** `.git/HEAD`, `.git/refs/heads`, `.git/refs/tags`, `.git/objects/pack`, `.git/info`, `.git/worktrees/worktree/HEAD`\\n  - **protected:** `.git/config`, `.git/hooks`\\n- So a test inside the reviewed change could move branches or release tags, or add objects, in your real repository.\\n- This breaks R1 (\\\"nega gravação fora do diretório do run\\\") and triggers D1's own falsifier (\\\"escrever fora do scratch autorizado\\\").\\n- The after-run checks don't catch it. `checkDispatchOrigin` only checks that the main repo's HEAD still resolves (`review_dispatch.go:1186`, result thrown away). Refs, tags and objects are never compared.\\n- A fix to consider: have the wrapper add `git rev-parse --git-common-dir` to `denyWrite`, then qualify that in a real worktree dispatch.\\n\\n**F2 (medium): the qualification claims a check it didn't really make.**\\n- Where: `.pose/reports/claude-review-sandbox-qualification.md:13` and `:35`; `.pose/adr/2026-11-12-sandboxed-claude-review-commands.md:16`.\\n- The ADR requires a real execution to show that writes to shared Git metadata are denied.\\n- The qualification used a made-up `/tmp/pose-sandbox-shared-git` sentinel. That doesn't match how a real review runs (see F1).\\n- The report then names \\\"existing dispatch integrity checks\\\" as the safeguard, but those checks don't look at refs, tags or objects.\\n\\n**F3 (low): one test can skip silently.**\\n- Where: `pose-mcp/internal/pose/claude_sandboxed_review_test.go:187`.\\n- `TestSandboxedReviewWrapperKeepsScratchPrivateAndPropagatesStartupFailure` skips when `jq` is missing, even though `jq` is now required.\\n- On a CI machine without `jq`, the tests for passing on startup failures and keeping scratch private quietly stop running.\\n\\n## Checks that hold\\n- **Only governed review uses the profile:** `delegation_policy.go:788-795` applies it to review only and copies Resume before replacing its command. Review resume reads `plan.Config.Resume.Command` (`review_dispatch.go:868`), so a resumed run is held to the same limits as a fresh one.\\n- **Invalid profiles are refused before anything runs:** `delegation_policy.go:601-622`.\\n- **Leaving the profile out changes nothing:** existing adapters stay byte-identical (tested).\\n- **Fresh and resume commands are identical** apart from `--resume {session}`. Both set `failIfUnavailable:true` and `allowUnsandboxedCommands:false`.\\n- **Missing tools stop the run with install advice:** without bwrap, socat or jq the wrapper exits 127 with install hints.\\n- **Startup failures pass through:** a failing Claude start is reported as is (exit 78 in the test), with no fallback to another command.\\n- **Capture-failure messages are safe:** they now name the stage where capture failed and withhold the raw output.\\n- **Docs match:** the new paragraphs are identical in the root and scaffold copies. The only other difference (contributor mode) is older than this change.\\n\\n## Structural facts\\n- **SD-2147e11f** (ADR added) → D1: it is the decision record for choosing a review-specific profile.\\n- **SD-29d21675** (`delegation.json` changed) → R1: it adopts the sandboxed Claude review profile and its dependency gate.\\n\\n```pose-draft\\n{\\n  \\\"schema\\\": \\\"pose.review.draft/v1\\\",\\n  \\\"decision\\\": \\\"changes-requested\\\",\\n  \\\"findings\\\": [\\n    {\\\"id\\\": \\\"F1\\\", \\\"severity\\\": \\\"high\\\", \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"blocker\\\", \\\"file\\\": \\\".pose/policy/delegation.json\\\", \\\"line\\\": 287, \\\"summary\\\": \\\"In real worktree dispatch Claude Code auto-allows writes to the primary repository's Git common dir; from inside the review sandbox .git/HEAD, refs/heads, refs/tags, objects/pack and info are writable (verified with non-mutating test -w; config/hooks are protected). The fresh and resumed review_profile wrappers (lines 287, 317) set allowWrite=[scratch] and denyWrite=[cwd] but do not deny the git common dir, so untrusted tests can move branches/tags or add objects in the user's repo. Violates R1 and triggers D1's falsifier; checkDispatchOrigin (review_dispatch.go:1186) only checks that origin HEAD resolves and does not detect ref/tag/object tampering.\\\"},\\n    {\\\"id\\\": \\\"F2\\\", \\\"severity\\\": \\\"medium\\\", \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"blocker\\\", \\\"file\\\": \\\".pose/reports/claude-review-sandbox-qualification.md\\\", \\\"line\\\": 13, \\\"summary\\\": \\\"Qualification claims shared Git metadata writes are denied using a synthetic /tmp/pose-sandbox-shared-git sentinel that does not match real worktree dispatch, where the git common dir is auto-allowed; the ADR (2026-11-12-sandboxed-claude-review-commands.md:16) requires a real demonstration, and line 35 names dispatch integrity checks as the safeguard even though they do not compare refs, tags or objects.\\\"},\\n    {\\\"id\\\": \\\"F3\\\", \\\"severity\\\": \\\"low\\\", \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"follow-up\\\", \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/claude_sandboxed_review_test.go\\\", \\\"line\\\": 187, \\\"summary\\\": \\\"The startup-failure-propagation and private-scratch regression skips when jq is absent although jq is now a mandatory dependency, so CI without jq silently loses that coverage; it should fail rather than skip.\\\"}\\n  ],\\n  \\\"criteria\\\": [\\n    {\\\"id\\\": \\\"assumption-integrity\\\", \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\", \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"F2\\\"},\\n    {\\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-concurrency\\\", \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\", \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/claude-sandboxed-review-integration\\\", \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The projection copies Command and Resume before replacing them, so shared policy is not mutated; TestSandboxedReviewSelectsOnlyReviewAndKeepsResumeConfiguration passes (reproduced). No new concurrency surface.\\\"},\\n    {\\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-contracts\\\", \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\", \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/claude-sandboxed-review-integration\\\", \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Optional review_profile is opt-in; omission keeps legacy adapters byte-identical (TestSandboxedReviewOmissionPreservesLegacyAdapter, reproduced); task/adjudicate/smoke keep their commands.\\\"},\\n    {\\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-input-errors\\\", \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\", \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/claude-sandboxed-review-integration\\\", \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Empty, incomplete, interpolated, task-fragment and executable-session profiles are refused at parse time (delegation_policy.go:601-622; TestSandboxedReviewRefusesIncompleteOrUnsafeCommands reproduced).\\\"},\\n    {\\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-integration-impact\\\", \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\", \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/claude-sandboxed-profile-integration\\\", \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Review resume and provenance consume plan.Config.Resume.Command (review_dispatch.go:868, review_run_provenance.go:531) and the origin check uses the same kind-to-purpose projection; claude-sandboxed-profile-integration passed in my sandboxed run.\\\"},\\n    {\\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-observability\\\", \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\", \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-output-redaction-diagnostics-integration\\\", \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Capture failure now names a closed-vocabulary stage/reason and withholds raw output (review_dispatch.go:1055); reproduced pass, and TestSandboxedReviewCaptureFailureNamesTheSafeStage... confirms no leak.\\\"},\\n    {\\\"id\\\": \\\"compatibility\\\", \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\", \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/claude-sandboxed-review-integration\\\", \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Examined the DelegationAgent schema change, the omission test and the docs: the field is optional, existing adapters and digests are unchanged, and the docs/changelog state that older strict parsers reject the key. Compatible, with the migration explicitly documented.\\\"},\\n    {\\\"id\\\": \\\"correctness\\\", \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\", \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/claude-sandboxed-review-integration\\\", \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Selection, refusal, dependency gating (exit 127 with hints, Claude never launched) and startup-failure propagation (exit 78) behave as specified; 8/8 TestSandboxedReview and go vet pass in this run. The boundary gap is tracked under security/requirements as F1.\\\"},\\n    {\\\"id\\\": \\\"design-causality\\\", \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\", \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-b05eed146f58614e\\\", \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Examined the ADR, D1 and the projection code: a review-only profile running under the OS sandbox addresses the stated cause (Go flags that execute code can't be blocked by a prefix allow-list) without widening task/read. The design is causally sound; how the boundary is configured is a separate defect (F1).\\\", \\\"mappings\\\": [\\n      {\\\"delta\\\": \\\"SD-2147e11f\\\", \\\"basis\\\": \\\"D1\\\", \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"mapped\\\", \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The ADR is D1's decision record for choosing a review-specific sandboxed profile.\\\"},\\n      {\\\"delta\\\": \\\"SD-29d21675\\\", \\\"basis\\\": \\\"R1\\\", \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"mapped\\\", \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"delegation.json adopts the sandboxed Claude review_profile that R1 requires, including the dependency gate.\\\"}\\n    ]},\\n    {\\\"id\\\": \\\"documentation\\\", \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\", \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"F2\\\"},\\n    {\\\"id\\\": \\\"operability\\\", \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\", \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/claude-sandboxed-review-integration\\\", \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Examined the wrapper refusals and capture diagnostics: missing bwrap/socat/jq names the tool and gives apt/dnf/pacman advice; capture failure names a safe stage and reason. Remediation is actionable.\\\"},\\n    {\\\"id\\\": \\\"requirements\\\", \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\", \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"F1\\\"},\\n    {\\\"id\\\": \\\"scope\\\", \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\", \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/claude-sandboxed-review-integration\\\", \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Compared the diff with the spec's artifact list and non-goals: the files changed match the declared artifacts; no change to adjudication/smoke/tasks and no engine containment upgrade.\\\"},\\n    {\\\"id\\\": \\\"security\\\", \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\", \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"F1\\\"},\\n    {\\\"id\\\": \\\"solution-proportionality\\\", \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\", \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-b05eed146f58614e\\\", \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Compared with the smallest alternative (widening the read allow-list), which can't contain executable Go flags; the opt-in field plus a policy wrapper is minimal with no speculative extension. The choice is invalidated if the sandbox cannot be configured to deny shared Git metadata (see F1).\\\"}\\n  ],\\n  \\\"tools\\\": [\\n    {\\\"id\\\": \\\"artifact-check\\\", \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\", \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-claude-reviewer-runs-tests-in-sandbox --strict\\\", \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"exit 0; only pre-existing orphan warnings; change-set head resolved to descendant 4a4077c4 (sealing chores only).\\\"},\\n    {\\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-design\\\", \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\", \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-b05eed146f58614e\\\", \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Ran pose assess design --json; input digest matches the sealed ref; two governance-contract deltas.\\\"},\\n    {\\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-discover\\\", \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\", \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\", \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Not run: it persists assessment state under .pose, which is read-only in the sealed checkout; design and surface evidence covered the structural questions.\\\"},\\n    {\\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-integrate\\\", \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\", \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Ran pose assess integrate; it refused to save .pose/state/integrations.json on the read-only sealed checkout (exit 1), so it produced no assessment. Integration is covered by the module integration checks.\\\"},\\n    {\\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-tech-debt\\\", \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\", \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Not run: it persists .pose/state/technical-debt.json, which is read-only here; the change adds no TODO markers.\\\"},\\n    {\\\"id\\\": \\\"closeout-check\\\", \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\", \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Requires the review to be complete and attested first.\\\"},\\n    {\\\"id\\\": \\\"review-check\\\", \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\", \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Requires the review attestation this draft precedes.\\\"},\\n    {\\\"id\\\": \\\"suggest-review\\\", \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\", \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\", \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\\\", \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"exit 0; it pointed to the security, documentation-style and backend-go rules, which were applied.\\\"},\\n    {\\\"id\\\": \\\"surface-check\\\", \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\", \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/spec-surface-integration\\\", \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Ran pose surface-check --spec pose-claude-reviewer-runs-tests-in-sandbox --strict: exit 0, 209 results, 0 findings.\\\"},\\n    {\\\"id\\\": \\\"validate\\\", \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"failed\\\", \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\", \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Ran pose validate --strict --jobs 4 inside the review sandbox: exit 1, 200 pass, 10 fail, 2 timeouts, all in pose-mcp checks with environmental signatures (/tmp and /home seen as uid 65534, proxy 403, runtime host start failure, 600s timeout); none touch the changed code. The sealed ref passed on the host, but the tool did not pass in this run.\\\"},\\n    {\\\"id\\\": \\\"validate\\\", \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\", \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"failed\\\", \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/claude-sandboxed-review-integration\\\", \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Ran pose validate --strict --module pose-mcp --jobs 4 inside the review sandbox: exit 1, 197 pass, 10 fail, 2 timeouts, all environmental as above; claude-sandboxed-review, claude-sandboxed-profile, redaction-diagnostics, build and vet passed.\\\"}\\n  ]\\n}\\n```\",\n.pose/review-runs/rrn-6feb82c74a471cb5.json:106:  \"output\": \"decision: approved\\n\\nNo new defects found. R1-F1 is fixed: the tests separately exercise command and stream replay, and detect a changed HEAD after the deadline.\\n\\nReviewed under the Go, security, documentation and delivery-evidence rules. Tests were assessed from sealed evidence and source inspection; no local builds were attempted. The worktree remains unchanged. Review and closeout completion checks remain deferred.\\n\\n```pose-draft\\n{\\n  \\\"schema\\\": \\\"pose.review.draft/v1\\\",\\n  \\\"decision\\\": \\\"approved\\\",\\n  \\\"findings\\\": [],\\n  \\\"prior_findings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R1-F1\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"governance_read_view_audit_timeout_test.go:35-74 uses ls-tree against HEAD, separates command and stream regressions, and requires detection after HEAD moves. governance_git_pure.go:59-60 confirms HEAD listings require replay. Sealed integration:pose-mcp/go/read-view-audit-repeats-a-read-under-its-own-time-integration passed.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"sweep\\\": \\\"Swept R1-R3 and D1 against both production capture/replay paths, timeout calculation and lock ordering, all deadline-field uses, pure-read exemptions, caller cancellation, observation copying and synchronization, command and stream audit budgets, negative/change-detection tests, CLI index composition, validation-matrix registration, declared artifacts, start metadata, supplied gate outputs, and sealed validation provenance. No new defects established.\\\",\\n  \\\"criteria\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assumption-integrity\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/read-view-audit-repeats-a-read-under-its-own-time-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Verified timeout measurement precedes state.mu.Lock in both capture paths. Verified existing WithoutCancel semantics rather than assuming caller cancellation bounds the final audit. The spec explicitly acknowledges cumulative replay latency. The reported 135-second index run was not independently reproduced; approval rests on source inspection and sealed regression evidence.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-concurrency\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/governance-read-view-integration\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-contracts\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/cli-mcp-operation-results-integration\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-input-errors\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/read-view-audit-repeats-a-read-under-its-own-time-integration\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-integration-impact\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/check-index-generation-integration\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-observability\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/governance-read-view-integration\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"compatibility\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/cli-mcp-operation-results-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Examined the diff and production callers. No exported signatures, CLI/MCP schemas, stored formats, or output contracts change. Reads without deadlines retain their existing behavior; deadline-bound audit replays receive a fresh duration.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"correctness\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/read-view-audit-repeats-a-read-under-its-own-time-integration\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"design-causality\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-3d544b355dce57c3\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"D1 addresses R1-R3 directly: auditTimeout computes deadline minus capture start with a positive fallback, and both replay sites use WithTimeout. This removes dependence on an expired absolute instant while retaining per-read bounds. Timeout capture occurs before state-lock queuing; existing synchronization and comparison logic remain intact. No individual structural delta facts were enumerated in the brief.\\\",\\n      \\\"mappings\\\": []\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"documentation\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/read-view-audit-repeats-a-read-under-its-own-time-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Compared the scope spec, D1, requirement trace, code comments and registered test command against runtime behavior. They describe fresh per-read audit timeouts, the positive expired-deadline fallback and cumulative audit latency consistently. No public operational interface requires migration.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"operability\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/governance-read-view-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Examined replay failures and budget-exhaustion handling. Existing changed/unknown producer reporting, bounded diagnostic summaries and hashed Git identifiers remain intact. Unchanged successful reads no longer produce false changes solely because their original deadline passed.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"requirements\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/read-view-audit-repeats-a-read-under-its-own-time-integration\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"scope\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-3d544b355dce57c3\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Compared the declared implementation artifacts with the scoped diff. Changes are confined to recording and replaying timeout durations, focused regression coverage and its required validation registration. Generated governance material is distinguished from implementation changes.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"security\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/governance-read-view-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Inspected context construction, command arguments, root routing, retained observations and audit budgets. Every previously deadline-bound replay remains deadline-bound. The change adds no command interpolation, dependency, authority expansion, sensitive diagnostic content or budget bypass.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"solution-proportionality\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-3d544b355dce57c3\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The shared duration helper plus one duration field per observation and two replay substitutions are sufficient for D1. Increasing original deadlines merely postpones recurrence; removing deadlines loses the bound. No scheduler, global timeout policy or speculative abstraction is added. A future requirement that caller cancellation or one absolute deadline bound the entire audit would require reconsidering this design; the existing detached audit contract does not impose that requirement.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"tools\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"artifact-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-read-view-audit-repeats-a-read-under-its-own-time --strict\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Disposed from the supplied sealed-commit output /var/tmp/closeout/ac-at.out and command implementation. It names cs-4bd6fb70856f and the requested base/head, with four claims and warning-only findings. The local rerun was interrupted and is not used as passing evidence.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-design\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-3d544b355dce57c3\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Consumed the sealed design result and inspected the implementation against D1 directly. Did not rerun assessment commands that may write governance artifacts.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-discover\\\",\\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Read-only review; no assessment refresh was performed. Reviewed the affected component directly.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-integrate\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/check-index-generation-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"No REST, Protobuf, Kafka or MCP contract changes. Inspected CLI composition and consumed sealed integration evidence without running a writing assessment.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-tech-debt\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"No assessment writes permitted. Searched the three implementation/test files for TODO, FIXME, stub and panic markers; none were present.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"closeout-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Completion requires the review conclusion to be recorded and verified by POSE; this review does not record an attestation.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"review-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Completion requires the review conclusion to be recorded and verified by POSE; this review does not record an attestation.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"suggest-review\\\",\\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Ran successfully and applied the selected Go, security and documentation rules.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"surface-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/read-view-audit-repeats-a-read-under-its-own-time-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Consumed /var/tmp/closeout/sc-at.out: one target, 233 results, zero findings. Independently traced the CLI index stream producer through the read view to final replay. The interrupted local rerun is not used as passing evidence.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"validate\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/read-view-audit-repeats-a-read-under-its-own-time-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Consumed sealed strict-validation evidence and delivery-validation.json: 233 executed checks, all passed. Its recorded commit is 87360eda; verified no subsequent changes to the reviewed implementation, regression tests or validation matrix through f72cf7e3. No local build or test run attempted.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"validate\\\",\\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Consumed sealed pose-mcp validation evidence, including unit, integration and build results. Read the focused regressions and verified their registered command. No local build or test run attempted.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\\n```\",\n.pose/review-bundles/rvb-7f6c2f6adbb4ee37.json:424:          \"description\": \"Explain how the selected design addresses the stated requirement and material cause, citing the relevant decision basis and structural observations where available.\",\n.pose/review-bundles/rvb-7f6c2f6adbb4ee37.json:533:          \"rationale\": \"observe bounded structural deltas on the canonical review subject\",\n.pose/review-bundles/rvb-7f6c2f6adbb4ee37.json:3199:      \"structural-causality\"\n.pose/review-runs/rrn-bef40df473391d0c.json:85:  \"brief_notes\": \"Implementer notes — factual context, not a review decision\\n\\nThe generated sealed brief is authoritative. Review independently and report every blocking finding; do not infer approval from passing checks.\\n\\nUser selected Claude Code Opus 5.5 for independent review and retains Sol medium for implementation tasks. The implementing session is OpenAI; its exact model is unknown and must not be invented. The local executor signer is an executor declaration, not an Anthropic receipt or human authority.\\n\\nB34 was recovered after loss of a temporary clone. The spec preserves failed historical rounds and the prospective start b2eb2d34; unrecovered historical receipts were not reconstructed. The normal binary built from b7b5680f passed the current canonical 189/189 strict checks (four workers, native wall 430.0s), including the uncached full Go suite and the expanded B34 race integration. The normal final index, artifact-check and surface-check passed. The final real global structural gate passed with 35 historical warnings and no errors. All native stages completed successfully before sealing. Historical checkpoint prose in the source reports describes the evidence available when committed; use the sealed current evidence rather than those earlier pending checkpoints.\\n\\nD7 separates the global audited selection/catalogue coordinator from bounded per-scope evaluation with at most 16 live workers and exact root/Files/authority bindings. The first real run after D7 took about three hours and failed with 19 errors. b7b5680f corrects two independently reproduced defects: final DirEntry.Info audit re-listed a directory once per entry (a 200-entry probe observed 199 listings), and roadmap child evaluation cleared the active authorized Store context despite already disabling recursive federated acceptance through its existing argument. The new probes fail under an overlay of the previous source and pass after correction; budgets were not increased. Index material builds now use a fresh existing spec snapshot per build. D8 excludes only instance-owned delegation.json from the scaffold using its established policy exclusion path.\\n\\nThe complete go test -race ./... attempt passed every other package, including CLI (508.703s) and MCP (13.919s); the domain package hit the default ten-minute timeout while starting TestR2PoliciesOfTheCutAreValidated. The domain-only -timeout=30m attempt also timed out without a race diagnostic. Neither timeout is a pass. All 1,425 domain tests subsequently passed with race in four disjoint complete groups (357/356/356/356): 214.656/136.488/168.012/191.100s. There are no Fuzz or Example functions in this package. The validation matrix's independent commands were not coalesced; this was an additional full-domain race run.\\n\\nThe first native review of bundle rvb-b93ae9162907b66a never invoked the vendor. Its immutable record rrn-accfce117640c7af has execution_state=not-started, empty transcript, and a sealed-checkout setup failure: the committed delivery index at b7 did not yet hold B34 attribution. Checkpoint 42c8891f commits the actual generated index/evidence and derived report updates; it contains no Go change. The canonical matrix was regenerated on 42c8891f and passed 189/189 checks (352.1s). The new bundle includes the current native provenance and a sealed checkout with the required indexed attribution. Preserve the failed setup run; it is not an approval and consumed no vendor tokens.\\n\\n\\nReview bounded Files/Git capture and audit, directory and handle replay/errors, byte/metadata/record budgets, root-vector authority, retries, closure localization, stale review retention, production writer guard/CAS/receipt paths, and outputs/bindings from a single audited index build. External uncooperative ABA is explicitly outside the guarantee; no universal filesystem transaction or persistent authorization is claimed. No watcher/daemon/runtime/cache adoption was included.\\n\\nD5 preserves 64 local edges / 256 unique nodes / 256 entries while applying eight to composed cross-project paths, including redirects; tests cover shared DAG suffixes and deduplication. D6 is measured 25,000 aggregate records and 512 MiB input with 8 MiB metadata retained; versioned reports explain why the full corpus exceeded initial limits. Index generation must use the normal build, never calibration overlays.\\n\\nAssessment integrate is static inventory, not functional proof. Tech-debt scan remains INCOMPLETE because two historical specs are invalid (pose-instance-engine-version-tracking and pose-knowledge-durable-reference-type); no uncovered marker was found in the scanned content. Knowledge check passed with 21 artifacts. Recurrence check has no flagged unresolved keys, and discloses an existing validate-native flapping cluster. Remote CI was waived by the user; Harne8 engine adoption/gitlink is outside this change.\\n\\nPlease evaluate all generated criteria and tool dispositions, including structural mappings. A component validation tool with producer_coverage none must not be described as executed; use a supported not-used disposition with rationale if appropriate. Final approval is your independent judgment. Do not invoke contributors/issue submission or edit project files.\\n\",\n.pose/review-runs/rrn-da6e5287b19f2087.json:86:  \"brief_notes\": \"Review of spec pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit, implemented by Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic). The ADR `.pose/adr/2026-11-12-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-and-benefit.md` is Accepted; judge the implementation against it and the spec, not the decision itself.\\n\\nMechanism. Review policy schema 5 adds `milestone_review_required` / `roadmap_review_required` (`never|when-justified|always`), validated in `parseReviewPolicy` via `validateCloseoutReviewPolicyKeys` (closeout_review_policy.go). One evaluator `evaluateCloseoutReview` (closeout-review@1): canonical members `xref:\\u003cproject\\u003e/spec:\\u003cslug\\u003e` (aliases, verified redirects, federated resolver, unknown = diagnostic, never zero) and ADR associations (closeout_adr_associations.go: roadmap `adrs:`, ADR `roadmaps:`, local Markdown links both ways; malformed/missing/unreadable = unknown). `closeoutReviewGate` is the single entry for readers: receipt first, roadmap done before adoption = legacy (nil decision), else evaluate + `protectCloseoutDecision` (baseline policy at the change set base when the scope changes the review contract); exemption only when not required AND no review recorded on the scope (`scopeReviewRecorded`, unreadable counts as recorded). Consumers: `reviewCheck` (review_closeout.go, Required=false + ApprovalOrigin), `proportionalReviewVerification` (review_bundle.go; under adoption the legacy singleton inheritance and `unreviewed_milestones` are skipped), `getCloseoutState` (CloseRequired, receipt, terminal only with receipt, new diagnostics), `ReachedMilestones`/`RoadmapsReachedBy`/`roadmapReachedApartFrom` (roadmaps.go), `milestoneReachedObligations`, `ReviewPlan.CloseoutReview` (out of the digest), doctor (`CloseoutReviewsOwed`), setup and `pose adopt` (capability_catalog.go `closeoutReviewPolicyCatalogEntry`, `SetCloseoutReviewPolicy`; refs/transfer adopt/retire no longer lower schema 5). CLI close (cli/review_closeout.go `closeoutReceiptPreflight`, `publishCloseoutReceipt`): milestone and roadmap close publish an immutable receipt (closeout_receipt.go, ExpectAbsent publish, strict parse); a done roadmap without receipt is completed by a new close. `milestoneMember` now maps `spec:\\u003cslug\\u003e` to its slug (was `spec:spec:\\u003cslug\\u003e` in closeout state). Existing tests changed on purpose: catalog lists, schema after adopt (fresh install is now schema 5), progressive_review fixtures that force schema 2, and the previous-release compatibility test (a fresh install is refused by v7.4.0 by its schema, by ADR design; an updated legacy instance stays readable).\\n\\nPlease do an exhaustive sweep in this round and report ALL findings together, classified blocker vs follow-up. Inventory every entry point that answers \\\"is this aggregate scope approved / closed / reached\\\" (CLI close, closeout-check, review-check, review verify, review-plan, attention/obligations, reached, nextCloses, roadmap check, MCP closeout state, federated acceptance, doctor) and check each one reads the same gate, cannot launder a recorded rejection under `never`, cannot let `always` be weakened by inheritance or `unreviewed_milestones`, and never treats an unknown member/association as an exemption. Also check: receipts are never overwritten nor fabricated for history; `pose update` never adopts; no schema-5 downgrade path; the recovery path for a roadmap done without receipt cannot close a scope whose review is required and unapproved.\\n\\nKnown pre-existing state: `pose check --strict` reports 19 delivery-contract errors of other specs (runtime worktree, common-domain handoff, governance performance, bounded graph caches), identical line by line on the base commit 956153f1; they are follow-up F4, not this spec.\\n\\nRequired tools: run `pose artifact-check --spec pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit --strict` and `pose surface-check --spec pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit --strict`; declare each `passed` only after running it (evidence `command:\\u003cthe command\\u003e`, rationale quoting its result). The surface-check disposition must cite both an `integration:` and a `reachability:` sealed evidence id. Cite sealed `unit:`/`integration:` ids for criteria, never `SD-…` structural facts or requirement ids. Send each shell command alone in its own call (no pipes, `;`, `\\u0026\\u0026`, redirects). `validate` of a component with registered checks is `passed` with the sealed run's evidence; `review-check` and `closeout-check` are `deferred`. New findings have bare ids (F1, F2 …); follow-ups carry `action`, `owner`, `review_by`; only low-severity risks may be accepted.\\n\\nRound 12. Your round-11 run rrn-3e1184879382ed6c approved the scope with one low follow-up (N37), but the engine refused to record it: a draft finding has no `rationale` field. A finding object accepts exactly `id`, `severity`, `disposition`, `file`, `line`, `summary`, and for an accepted follow-up `action`, `owner`, `review_by`; put any rationale inside `summary`. Criteria and tools keep their own `rationale`. Since round 11, N37 was fixed (doctor's closeout diagnostic uses the bound store, cliGovernedStore, as `pose close` does), and one engine bound changed: during this closeout the repository's attributed history crossed the governance read view's 512 MiB captured-input budget (measured: `git show --binary` of 2,451 trailer commits, 492 MB, plus the generation's file inputs), so every `pose index` of pose-dist was refused; the budget is recalibrated to 1 GiB by amendment D10 of ADR governance-reads-use-bounded-operation-scoped-views, the same measured-recalibration procedure D6 used, with follow-up F5 for the structural fix (retain only a digest for pure reads of immutable objects a producer only hashes). Judge D10 like any other change. Account in `prior_findings` for every finding the brief lists as open for this scope (round-10 run rrn-8b1997980713c10a: R9-N34 … R9-N36, plus any earlier partial), each with whether it stands, and report N37 as fixed or standing. Do NOT run `pose assess`, `pose state`, `pose index` or anything else that writes under `.pose/`; dispose assess-* tools from the sealed evidence and the code. Leave the worktree as you found it. Sweep the whole surface again and report every remaining finding in one pass, classified blocker vs follow-up; a remote variant of a threat the ADR does not promise to defend is a follow-up, and so is a pre-existing gap of the federation or transfer engine that this spec did not introduce and does not claim to close.\\n\",\n.pose/review-runs/rrn-da6e5287b19f2087.json:106:  \"output\": \"decision: changes-requested\\n\\nTwo medium blockers remain:\\n\\n- **N38:** An adopted policy with bundles disabled can report a receipt-closed milestone terminal after a member’s rejection, through the legacy `unreviewed_milestones` exception.\\n- **N39:** Empty or duplicate ADR association metadata can become a known absence and grant a `when-justified` exemption.\\n\\nThe five prior findings are fixed in their reviewed paths. Artifact-check, surface-check, focused policy tests, round-ten regressions, and `go vet` passed. Custom probes could not run because the sandbox denied temporary-file creation. No repository changes or attestation were made.\\n\\nApplied the review workflow and Go, security, documentation, delivery-evidence, and knowledge-governance rules. The JSON below contains every criterion, tool disposition, structural mapping, and finding.\\n\\n```pose-draft\\n{\\n  \\\"schema\\\": \\\"pose.review.draft/v1\\\",\\n  \\\"decision\\\": \\\"changes-requested\\\",\\n  \\\"findings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"N38\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"medium\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"blocker\\\",\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_closeout.go\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": 2742,\\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"Restrict the legacy declaredUnreviewed child exception to legacy closeout semantics. Schema 5 supports review_bundles=false. In that configuration, an aggregate's approved legacy attempt remains fresh when a child's review is subsequently rejected: ScopeDigest binds the child's content, not its verdict, and the legacy-attempt verification branch does not verify children. This condition then suppresses child-scope-open whenever unreviewed_milestones is present, even under adopted always. With an existing valid receipt, getCloseoutState can therefore return Terminal=true while its child is nonterminal. closedByReceipt propagates that result to reached, obligations, readiness and doctor. CLI repeated close independently checks the member gate and refuses, creating a disagreement between authoritative projections. Preserve child terminal failures under every adopted mode and cover an approved legacy-attempt milestone before and after member rejection, with bundles disabled and unreviewed_milestones present.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"N39\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"medium\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"blocker\\\",\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_adr_associations.go\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": 89,\\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"Preserve association-field presence and reject ambiguous or malformed declarations before proving absence. An explicit empty adrs: value is indistinguishable here from an absent field. parseInlineList also discards empty items, accepting adrs: [,] as an empty list. Duplicate adrs fields are overwritten by parseRoadmapFile, while duplicate ADR roadmaps fields are overwritten by SplitFrontmatter; for example adrs: [adr:decision.md] followed by adrs: [] silently removes the association. A roadmap with two canonical members and no other association consequently receives Known=true, Required=false under when-justified. This contradicts R3's technical contract that malformed or ambiguous association inputs cannot produce an exemption. Validate presence, list syntax and duplicate association keys in both directions, with negative regression fixtures.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"N40\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"low\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"follow-up\\\",\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_adr_associations.go\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": 55,\\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"The Markdown link extractor scans raw bodies, including fenced code, inline code and comments. An ADR containing a documented example such as a fenced [example](../roadmaps/example.md) is treated as a real reverse association input. If the illustrative roadmap does not exist, the inventory makes unrelated when-justified roadmap decisions unknown; if it exists, the example can spuriously require review. This over-enforces the gate rather than bypassing it, so it is accepted as a low residual risk.\\\",\\n      \\\"action\\\": \\\"Exclude non-link Markdown contexts before extracting associations and add code-example and comment fixtures.\\\",\\n      \\\"owner\\\": \\\"@pose-maintainers\\\",\\n      \\\"review_by\\\": \\\"2026-12-13\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"N41\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"low\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"follow-up\\\",\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\".pose/adr/2026-11-03-governance-reads-use-bounded-operation-scoped-views.md\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": 253,\\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"git diff --check for the reviewed range exits 2 because the D10 amendment adds a blank line at EOF. This is a nonfunctional hygiene defect and is accepted as a low residual risk.\\\",\\n      \\\"action\\\": \\\"Remove the extra blank line at EOF when addressing the review findings.\\\",\\n      \\\"owner\\\": \\\"@pose-maintainers\\\",\\n      \\\"review_by\\\": \\\"2026-11-20\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"prior_findings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R8-N32\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go:3556 now verifies exemption children and clears approval on a non-closed, unapproved or stale child; closeout_review_policy_test.go:1316 covers an exempt receipt-bearing milestone falling with its member. The focused TestCloseoutReviewPolicy run passed.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R9-N34\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go:3518 evaluates adopted exemptions before the !policy.ReviewBundles return at 3576. TestCloseoutReviewPolicyRoundTen/an_exempt_milestone_without_review_bundles_closes_by_its_receipt passed without skipping.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R9-N35\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/roadmaps.go:401 uses closedByReceipt for adopted predecessor warnings. TestCloseoutReviewPolicyRoundTen/start_warnings_name_an_approved_but_unclosed_predecessor passed.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R9-N36\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go:1823 propagates a failed inherited child's blockers instead of silently skipping it. TestCloseoutReviewPolicyRoundTen/a_roadmap's_own_approval_does_not_stand_over_a_fallen_exempt_milestone passed. N38 concerns the separate supported legacy-attempt and declaredUnreviewed closeout path.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R11-N37\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/doctor.go:1587 constructs cliGovernedStore(root), preserving the environment-bound resolver used by close. The CLI TestCloseoutReviewPolicy tests passed.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"sweep\\\": \\\"Reviewed R1-R7, the accepted cost-benefit ADR, D10 and its spec amendment, the specified implementation and governance paths, schemas, templates and distribution docs. Swept policy parsing/adoption/setup/update preservation; canonical and transferred members; forward/reverse ADR associations; protected baseline and mandatory-human handling; optional-review vetoes; receipt parsing, immutable publication, interrupted-close recovery and historical closure; CLI close, closeout-check, review-check, review verification and review-plan; reached/nextCloses; obligations, readiness and portfolio; roadmap gates; MCP closeout projection; federation; doctor; and the adversarial corpus. Ran context resolution, suggest-review, artifact-check, surface-check, focused domain/CLI/MCP policy tests, verbose round-ten regressions, go vet and diff hygiene. Artifact-check and surface-check exited 0; policy tests and vet passed. The attempted additional overlay probes failed before execution because no temporary directory was writable, so N38-N40 are established by the cited control flow rather than claimed custom runtime reproductions. Final git status was clean. No assessment, state refresh, index, repository edit or attestation was performed.\\\",\\n  \\\"criteria\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assumption-integrity\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Distinguished executed checks and inspected control flow from implementer claims. Historical approvals require positive legacy evidence; unknown members fail exemption. D10's 492 MB measurement was not independently repeated because index/assessment writes are prohibited; it is documented decision evidence, while the 1 GiB constant and unchanged remaining bounds were verified in code. F5 remains explicitly documented scaling debt.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-concurrency\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/writer-coordination-and-atomic-publication-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Inspected guarded reevaluation, receipt ExpectAbsent publication, intent-before-status ordering and conflict handling. The change uses existing writer coordination and introduces no background lifecycle.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-contracts\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N38\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The supported bundles-disabled policy can produce conflicting terminal answers across closeout projections and CLI close.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-input-errors\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N39\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Malformed and ambiguous association metadata is not consistently diagnosed before granting an exemption.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-integration-impact\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N38\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The remaining terminal-state exception propagates through consumers of closedByReceipt.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-observability\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/typed-diagnostics-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Inspected decision reasons, canonical refs, unknown-input diagnostics, receipt corruption errors, doctor remediation and publication-conflict context. Diagnostics are bounded by the existing read and inventory limits.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"compatibility\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/install-and-upgrade-journeys-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Schema 5 deliberately rejects older engines, requires both enums and keeps references/transfer optional. Existing instances retain legacy semantics until explicit adoption; capability retirement preserves schema 5; historical plans retain their reading. Inspected the updated previous-release compatibility assertions and catalog/install paths.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"correctness\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N38\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"A receipt-bearing aggregate can remain terminal over a rejected member in the supported legacy-attempt configuration.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"design-causality\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-9d28f40675908bcf\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The shared deterministic evaluator addresses review cost without removing explicit close. Receipts separate review exemption from lifecycle completion; schema 5 makes adoption explicit. D10 is a bounded capacity recalibration tied to observed corpus growth, with the structural scaling correction retained as F5.\\\",\\n      \\\"mappings\\\": [\\n        {\\n          \\\"delta\\\": \\\"SD-607ff681\\\",\\n          \\\"basis\\\": \\\"R3\\\",\\n          \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"mapped\\\",\\n          \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The roadmap template exposes explicit adrs association metadata used by the deterministic roadmap predicate.\\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"delta\\\": \\\"SD-7e629ade\\\",\\n          \\\"basis\\\": \\\"R7\\\",\\n          \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"mapped\\\",\\n          \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The spec's artifact reconciliation explicitly includes D10 to restore operation on the current attributed-history corpus while retaining bounded reads.\\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"delta\\\": \\\"SD-ec2d86f4\\\",\\n          \\\"basis\\\": \\\"R1\\\",\\n          \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"mapped\\\",\\n          \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The new accepted ADR records policy location, thresholds, defaults, historical compatibility and explicit close semantics.\\\"\\n        }\\n      ]\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"documentation\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/distributed-instructions-parity-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Compared English, Portuguese and scaffold descriptions with runtime policy modes, receipt paths, adoption and exit-gate behavior. Templates expose adrs. N38 and N39 identify runtime departures from the documented contract; N41 records the nonfunctional amendment whitespace.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"operability\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N40\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Literal Markdown examples can create spurious association failures; the bounded over-enforcement is retained as an owned low follow-up.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"requirements\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N39\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"R3's malformed/ambiguous-input requirement is incomplete; N38 also violates the requirement to preserve member review standing.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"scope\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-9d28f40675908bcf\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The changes implement the policy, evaluator, receipts and required consumers within the amended spec. D10 and its tests/docs are explicitly reconciled artifacts. No new configuration command, MCP write tool or global ADR-reference grammar was added.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"security\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N38\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The local approval boundary must not suppress a member rejection under adopted semantics. Separately inspected receipt confinement, ADR regular-file checks, transfer resolution and immutable publication.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"solution-proportionality\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-9d28f40675908bcf\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"A paired policy, one evaluator and an immutable terminal receipt are sufficient to separate review cost from closeout. Reusing adopt and existing writer guards avoids another settings service or lifecycle mechanism. Remote backlink inventory and broader ArtifactRef grammar remain excluded. D10 buys finite headroom; another budget refusal or unacceptable retained-memory cost invalidates that temporary choice and triggers F5's digest-only retention work. Inspected the adversarial corpus's parent-outlives-a-rejected-child case; N38 records its uncovered legacy-attempt variant.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"tools\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"artifact-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit --strict\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Executed and exited 0. Output included artifact.claims=46, artifact.observed=157 and artifact.findings=920. The emitted broad orphan warnings did not fail the strict gate; the printed first recorded change set predates the current HEAD, and the implementation also collects the current attributed set.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-design\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-9d28f40675908bcf\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Did not run a state-writing assessment in the sealed checkout. Used sealed structure evidence and independently mapped all three supplied deltas.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-discover\\\",\\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Discovery writes assessment state and is prohibited by this review boundary. Component scope and applicable rules were checked from the brief, spec, matrix and suggest output.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-integrate\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Did not run the state-writing assessment. Inspected CLI/domain/MCP/federation boundaries and used sealed integration evidence plus the independently executed focused tests.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-tech-debt\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Did not run the state-writing assessment. Inspected changed code and the spec's explicit F1-F5 follow-ups; D10's retained-byte scaling debt remains documented as F5.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"closeout-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:pose context --task spec:pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit --json\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Completion-only check requires the recorded review conclusion. This independent run must not record an attestation.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"review-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:pose context --task spec:pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit --json\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Completion-only check is deferred until POSE records the verified run's conclusion.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"suggest-review\\\",\\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Executed successfully; selected security, documentation-style and backend-go rules and the review workflow.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"surface-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Executed pose surface-check --spec pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit --strict; exited 0 with surface.targets=1, surface.results=213 and surface.findings=0. Integration evidence: integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration. Production reachability evidence: reachability:pose-mcp/go/closeout-plan-reachability.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"validate\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Disposed from the sealed validation run as permitted for registered checks; did not rerun the state-writing validate producer. The bundle also seals build:pose-mcp/go/build and e2e:pose-mcp/go/multi-repo-agent-installed-journey. Independently ran the focused policy tests and go vet.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"validate\\\",\\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Used the sealed component validation evidence. Independently executed go test ./internal/pose ./internal/cli ./internal/mcpserver -run '^TestCloseoutReviewPolicy' -count=1, the verbose round-ten regression test and go vet ./...; all passed. Passing registered checks do not cover N38-N40.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\\n```\",\n.pose/review-runs/rrn-207a81f2e9c7aed0.json:106:  \"output\": \"**Approved. No defects found.**\\n\\nVerified that Go code, tests and ADRs are unchanged since the previous reviewed commit. The completed spec’s Final Report matches the implementation and its documented limitations.\\n\\nThe focused race-enabled tests, `go vet`, strict artifact-check and strict surface-check passed. Artifact-check reported warnings only. Full validation relies on the supplied sealed evidence. Review-check and closeout-check did not pass: they report no current-plan approval and an unknown governance read view. Terminal closeout remains unverified.\\n\\nApplied backend-go, security, documentation-style and delivery-evidence rules. No repository changes or attestations were made. `SD-5c6c5a14` maps to D1, whose basis is R1–R8.\\n\\n```pose-draft\\n{\\n  \\\"schema\\\": \\\"pose.review.draft/v1\\\",\\n  \\\"decision\\\": \\\"approved\\\",\\n  \\\"findings\\\": [],\\n  \\\"prior_findings\\\": [],\\n  \\\"sweep\\\": \\\"Swept all declared cursor implementation paths, five MCP handlers, argument validation, token integrity and bindings, ordering and mutation handling, generation verification/cache invalidation, bounds and expiry, compatibility, tests, validation registration, ADR, changelog, operational/scaffold documentation and completed-spec Final Report. Compared the previous reviewed commit with the current head: no pose-mcp or ADR changes; the spec changes only status and completed_at. Independently ran the focused race-enabled regression selection, go vet, artifact-check, surface-check and diagnostic review/closeout checks. No prior findings were listed and no new defects were established.\\\",\\n  \\\"criteria\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assumption-integrity\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-484c6eb6d942f499\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Verified unchanged implementation and ADR, full-scan collection reads, process-local signing and explicit restart semantics. Accepted limits include restart invalidation and weaker metadata detection outside Linux. Cross-platform execution was not independently tested. Current governance read-view freshness remains unknown and is not claimed as verified.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-concurrency\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/generation-bound-query-cursors-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Independent focused tests passed with -race in internal/pose and internal/mcpserver. Signing-key initialization and generation-cache access are synchronized; no retained query lifecycle is introduced.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-contracts\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/generation-bound-query-cursors-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The five tools share pagination validation and generation-bound continuation. Legacy unpaginated calls remain supported; version-1 tokens are explicitly refused. HTTP/stdio compatibility tests are included in the passing regression selection.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-input-errors\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/generation-bound-query-cursors-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Passing negative tests cover malformed, truncated, oversized and altered tokens, unsupported versions, expiry, invalid positions, mismatched bindings, null cursors, aliases and invalid explicit limits.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-integration-impact\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/generation-bound-query-cursors-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Inspected every changed handler and its domain-helper integration. Generation-reader status, reason and diverged files propagate to pages. Strict surface-check passed with one delivery target and zero findings.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-observability\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/generation-bound-query-cursors-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Pages disclose generation status, reason, divergence, collection, position, total and scan cost. Refusals provide bounded cursor codes and actionable restart guidance without exposing signing material.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"compatibility\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/generation-bound-query-cursors-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Token migration is deliberate and documented. Calls without pagination remain unpaginated, while continuations remain bounded. The CLI has no cursor-paginated surface requiring migration.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"correctness\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/generation-bound-query-cursors-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Independent focused race-enabled tests and go vet passed. Reviewed mutation, query binding, position, expiry, generation status and cache invalidation paths. The current source is identical to the previous reviewed source.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"design-causality\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-484c6eb6d942f499\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Signing the query binding and ordered-collection digest prevents a continuation from silently applying its offset to another sequence. Recomputing and refusing changed collections implements the selected restart strategy.\\\",\\n      \\\"mappings\\\": [\\n        {\\n          \\\"delta\\\": \\\"SD-5c6c5a14\\\",\\n          \\\"basis\\\": \\\"D1\\\",\\n          \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"mapped\\\",\\n          \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"D1 derives from R1-R8. The ADR records generation/query bindings, token integrity, restart behavior, resource bounds, scan costs and compatibility.\\\"\\n        }\\n      ]\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"documentation\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/distributed-instructions-parity-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The Final Report, ADR, changelog, tool descriptions and English/Portuguese scaffold documentation agree with runtime behavior. The owned indexing follow-up and full-scan cost remain explicit; completion does not claim indexed optimization.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"operability\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/generation-bound-query-cursors-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Cursor errors identify malformed, unsupported, signature, binding, expired, stale and position failures. Generation movement requests retry, while page disclosure explains coverage and cost.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"requirements\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/generation-bound-query-cursors-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Checked R1-R8 against the unchanged implementation, requirement trace, ADR and passing focused tests. Indexed-read optimization remains an explicitly owned follow-up because these collections are not indexed.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"scope\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-484c6eb6d942f499\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The implementation covers the declared five list tools and shared helper. Artifact-check passed. The completion delta changes lifecycle and derived/review records without expanding implementation scope.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"security\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/generation-bound-query-cursors-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"HMAC protects token integrity; tool/query/project/root bindings restrict replay; token size and expiry are bounded. Pagination introduces no gate or write authority and does not replace current request authorization.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"solution-proportionality\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-484c6eb6d942f499\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"A shared signed cursor with collection comparison is sufficient for explicit restart semantics. Retained snapshots and durable keys would add unnecessary lifecycle obligations. Revisit the design if cross-process continuation or indexed selective reads become requirements.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"tools\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"artifact-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"check:pose artifact-check --spec pose-generation-bound-query-cursors --strict --json\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Executed successfully: exit 0, 889 warnings, no nonwarning findings.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-design\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-484c6eb6d942f499\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Executed the read-only assessment successfully. Its input digest matches the sealed structural evidence.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-discover\\\",\\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The command persists assessment artifacts, conflicting with the no-repository-changes boundary. Inspected component structure and the unchanged source directly.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-integrate\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/generation-bound-query-cursors-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The assessment persists repository artifacts. Used direct inspection of all five handlers and passing integration evidence instead.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-tech-debt\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The assessment persists repository artifacts. Direct inspection found no TODO, FIXME, stub or panic markers in the cursor implementation; the indexing follow-up already has an owner and review date.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"closeout-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Executed diagnostically: lifecycle_done=true, review_approved=false and terminal=false. It reports no current-plan review attempt and an unknown governance read view. Final verification remains deferred until the conclusion is recorded and governance inputs verify.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"review-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Executed diagnostically: fresh=false and approved=false, with no current-plan review attempt and an unknown governance read view. This is not a passing gate; recheck after POSE records the conclusion and verifies current inputs.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"suggest-review\\\",\\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"check:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Executed and applied the selected workflow and backend-go, security and documentation-style rules.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"surface-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/generation-bound-query-cursors-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Executed strict surface-check: exit 0, one target, 190 results and zero findings. Additional sealed evidence: integration:pose-mcp/go/delivery-integration and reachability:pose-mcp/go/delivery-reachability.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"validate\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"build:pose-mcp/go/build\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Reused supplied sealed validation rather than rerunning repository-writing checks. Supporting classes: e2e:pose-mcp/go/multi-repo-agent-installed-journey; integration:pose-mcp/go/generation-bound-query-cursors-integration; unit:pose-mcp/go/test. Independently ran focused tests with -race and go vet; both passed.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"validate\\\",\\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/generation-bound-query-cursors-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Reused sealed module validation over unchanged source. Supporting classes: build:pose-mcp/go/build; e2e:pose-mcp/go/multi-repo-agent-installed-journey; unit:pose-mcp/go/test. The focused race-enabled regression selection and go vet passed independently.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\\n```\",\n.pose/review-bundles/rvb-3b6f52e24b22f0d3.json:352:          \"rationale\": \"observe bounded structural deltas on the canonical review subject\",\n.pose/review-bundles/rvb-3b6f52e24b22f0d3.json:1157:      \"structural-causality\"\n.pose/review-runs/rrn-55303f94e0410c2f.json:106:  \"output\": \"decision: approved\\n\\nR1-F1 is fixed. No new defects found. Both locale tests passed, including the pt_BR regression without skipping. Focused audit, budget, cancellation, and concurrency tests passed. The subject engine built; artifact-check and surface-check passed. The worktree remains unchanged.\\n\\nRules applied: bugfix review under `.pose/workflows/review.md`, with backend-go, security, documentation-style, and delivery-evidence rules. Full validation uses the sealed producer evidence.\\n\\n```pose-draft\\n{\\n  \\\"schema\\\": \\\"pose.review.draft/v1\\\",\\n  \\\"decision\\\": \\\"approved\\\",\\n  \\\"findings\\\": [],\\n  \\\"prior_findings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R1-F1\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"governance_read_view_git.go:637 defines LC_ALL=C and LANGUAGE=C; captured runner line 649 and streaming runner governance_read_view_stream.go:230 append that shared environment. Independently ran TestEveryGovernanceGitRunnerIsUntranslated and TestGovernanceGitIsReadUntranslated: both passed, neither skipped.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"sweep\\\": \\\"Reviewed the complete implementation diff, validation-matrix addition, start record, spec R1/D1, both captured and streaming runners including observation and final-audit routing, gitCommandContext environment construction, production consumers, module-discovery stderr classification, and adjacent snapshotGit, previewGit, gitCheckIgnore and gitOutputUntranslated paths. Inspected bounds, typed errors, cancellation, concurrency, raw-history protections and locale-sensitive output assumptions. Built the subject engine and ran focused regression and lifecycle tests; artifact-check and surface-check passed. No new defects established.\\\",\\n  \\\"criteria\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assumption-integrity\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/governance-git-reads-untranslated-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Verified that appended environment values override inherited values through the two-runner regression and local Go os/exec implementation. Inspected consumers using object data, explicit formats and porcelain output; found no locale-dependent parsed stdout. The translated regression can skip where pt_BR is unavailable, but it ran here and the environment regression does not require translation. No unresolved material assumption or accepted risk.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-concurrency\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/governance-read-view-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The shared environment is read-only after initialization and appended to each command independently. Existing locking, cancellation and process joining remain intact. Independently passed concurrent streamed-read comparison, audit, budget and caller-cancellation tests.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-contracts\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/cli-mcp-operation-results-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"No public signatures, schemas, tool definitions or file formats changed; the change normalizes subprocess diagnostics.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-input-errors\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/governance-git-reads-untranslated-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Verified non-repository classification under pt_BR. Bounded stderr, output admission and GitSnapshotError propagation remain intact; focused budget and warning tests passed.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-integration-impact\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/governance-git-reads-untranslated-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Traced module discovery and production artifact-integrity consumers through both runners; the coordinator regression and strict surface-check passed.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-observability\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/typed-diagnostics-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Failures retain operation context and bounded stderr through existing typed errors. Locale normalization improves classification without adding logging or sensitive output.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"compatibility\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/cli-mcp-operation-results-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Examined CLI/MCP consumers and error wrapping. Public contracts remain unchanged; C-locale sessions retain existing behavior, and translated sessions receive deterministic internal Git diagnostics.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"correctness\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/governance-git-reads-untranslated-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Both runners append the required overrides. Independently built the subject and passed locale, coordinator, captured-read and streamed-read regression tests.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"design-causality\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-2cb3bb3a223a46ad\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"R1 requires untranslated diagnostics for every governance Git command. D1 selects subprocess locale normalization because matching translated phrases would require maintaining Git translations. The shared environment reaches both execution paths and their audits, addressing the original cause and the previous round's omission. No individual structural delta facts were listed in the brief.\\\",\\n      \\\"mappings\\\": []\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"documentation\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/governance-git-reads-untranslated-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Compared the spec, shared-environment comment, regression tests and required validation-matrix command. They describe and exercise both runners; no operational command or template contract changes.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"operability\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/governance-git-reads-untranslated-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Non-repository directories are classified correctly under pt_BR, while other failures retain bounded forensic stderr and operation context. No new configuration or remediation step is required.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"requirements\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/governance-git-reads-untranslated-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"R1 is covered by direct environment assertions for both runners and the translated coordinator regression. Independently executed both successfully.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"scope\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-2cb3bb3a223a46ad\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Implementation changes are limited to the environment of the two governance Git runners, regression coverage and its validation registration. Adjacent non-governance runners remain outside the spec's explicit scope.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"security\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/git-and-dispatch-snapshot-integrity-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Inspected subprocess construction, environment filtering, raw-history restrictions, argument handling and output bounds. The change adds fixed locale values and preserves path, authority, cancellation and diagnostic boundaries; no secret material or dependency was introduced.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"solution-proportionality\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-2cb3bb3a223a46ad\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"One shared environment value applied at the two execution points is the smallest cohesive correction covering R1. It avoids translation tables, new abstractions and changes to unrelated runners. Reconsider if future governance commands require localized semantic stdout or another execution path bypasses these runners.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"tools\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"artifact-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:/tmp/pose-review-8704a030 artifact-check --spec pose-governance-git-reads-untranslated --strict\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Ran the engine built from the subject commit; exited 0. Reported repository-wide orphan warnings but no blocking findings; a JSON inspection confirmed no non-warning findings.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-design\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-2cb3bb3a223a46ad\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Used sealed design evidence and independently inspected R1/D1 and both execution paths; did not regenerate assessment artifacts in this read-only review.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-discover\\\",\\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/governance-read-view-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"No component discovery refresh was needed for the bounded environment change; avoided assessment writes.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-integrate\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/governance-git-reads-untranslated-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"No inter-module public contract changed. Independently traced production consumers and ran coordinator integration coverage without generating assessment artifacts.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-tech-debt\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:rg -n 'TODO|FIXME|stub|panic' pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_git_untranslated_test.go pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view_git.go pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view_stream.go\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Performed a read-only marker sweep of the affected implementation and tests; no markers found. Did not generate assessment artifacts.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"closeout-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:/tmp/pose-review-8704a030 context --task spec:pose-governance-git-reads-untranslated --json\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Requires completion and recording of this independent review; no attestation was recorded.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"review-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:/tmp/pose-review-8704a030 context --task spec:pose-governance-git-reads-untranslated --json\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Requires POSE to record this review conclusion first.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"suggest-review\\\",\\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:/tmp/pose-review-8704a030 suggest review --path pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Resolved backend-go, security and documentation-style rules and applied them.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"surface-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/governance-git-reads-untranslated-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Ran /tmp/pose-review-8704a030 surface-check --spec pose-governance-git-reads-untranslated --strict using the subject engine: exited 0, one target, zero findings.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"validate\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Uses the sealed strict-validation producer results listed in the brief, including build, integration and e2e results. Did not rerun the repository-writing validation command during this read-only review.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"validate\\\",\\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/governance-git-reads-untranslated-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Uses sealed component validation results. Independently built the subject and reran locale, coordinator, captured-read, streaming, audit, budget, cancellation and concurrency tests successfully.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\\n```\",\n.pose/review-runs/rrn-9b810c44750e6d93.json:106:  \"output\": \"decision: changes-requested\\n\\nR1-F4 is fixed for runs and attestations. Three medium-severity blockers remain:\\n\\n- **N1 — Transcript verification fails open** after finalization: the memo error becomes an empty success string.\\n- **N2 — Bundle-header reads lose failure coverage** after finalization: the memo error becomes an observation with no loss.\\n- **N3 — Memo hits lose producer attribution**, so final audits can omit affected consumers.\\n\\nReviewed the spec, selected implementation, callers, tests, ADR and validation matrix. Applied backend-Go, security, documentation-style and delivery-evidence rules. Used sealed test evidence; no builds or tests were executed in this read-only sandbox. Artifact and surface checks exited successfully. The worktree remains unchanged.\\n\\n```pose-draft\\n{\\n  \\\"schema\\\": \\\"pose.review.draft/v1\\\",\\n  \\\"decision\\\": \\\"changes-requested\\\",\\n  \\\"findings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"N1\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"medium\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"blocker\\\",\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": 1661,\\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"Propagate memo lifecycle failures as transcript verification problems. After view.audit(), memoizedLedgerRead returns the zero string and errGovernanceReadViewFinalized without invoking the computation, but reviewRunTranscriptIntact discards the error and returns an empty string, which its callers interpret as an intact transcript. This affects both warmed and cold keys. Previously checkReviewRunTranscript reached Files.Lstat and returned a nonempty inspection failure. R4 error compatibility and the fail-closed integrity contract are therefore violated. Preserve the failure in the returned problem string and cover transcript checks after finalization.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"N2\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"medium\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"blocker\\\",\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_operation_view.go\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": 30,\\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"Preserve SourceLoss when the memo refuses a header read. A finalized view makes memoizedLedgerRead return an error and a zero reviewHeaderObservation; this wrapper discards the error and returns owner empty, loss nil and readError empty. Previously observeReviewBundleHeader returned LossReadError and the underlying diagnostic. Consumers such as ReadReviewBundles skip an observation whose owner differs from the requested scope, so a lifecycle refusal can become an unreported omission instead of coverage loss. Convert memo errors into the existing read-error observation and cover finalized-view header reads.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"N3\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"medium\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"blocker\\\",\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_ledger_memo.go\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": 49,\\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"Preserve dependency attribution for every producer consuming a memo cell. The operation-wide key excludes the Files producer, governanceReadViewFromFiles discards its wrapper, and a hit only calls begin/end before returning the first producer's result. Thus producer A can read a ledger, producer B can consume the same cached result, and a subsequent mutation or unreadable-input audit is attributed only to A. governance_read_view.go:2180 marks changed producers from the recorded file attribution, while obligation_projection.go:259-285 uses those names to downgrade individual producer coverage. B can consequently retain current coverage despite consuming the affected ledger. This violates R4 and the ADR's explicit producer-attribution contract. Retain and replay the derived value's input dependencies for each consumer, with a two-producer audit regression test.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"prior_findings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R1-F4\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"review_ledger_memo.go:44 checks view.begin before serving or computing a cell; review_dispatch.go:256 and review_bundle.go:3343 propagate its error. TestReviewLedgerMemoIsNotServedAfterTheOperationEnds in review_ledger_memo_test.go warms runs and attestations, audits the view, and requires errGovernanceReadViewFinalized from both readers. Its execution is sealed as integration:pose-mcp/go/review-ledger-is-read-once-per-operation-integration. N1 and N2 identify separate wrappers that discard the newly returned error.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"sweep\\\": \\\"Reviewed R1-R4, the performance requirement and D1; all six changed implementation/test files; synchronization, lifecycle, deep-copy isolation, filtering, memo keys, native-read fallback, transcript integrity and bundle-header coverage; downstream review-round, conclusion, provenance and obligation-audit consumers; ADR D14, validation-matrix registration and artifact/surface evidence. Accounted for R1-F4 before examining additional defects. Read the registered regression tests and delivery-validation results without building or writing. Ran context resolution, suggest review, artifact-check, surface-check and recurrence-check; recurrence reported zero flagged keys. Confirmed an unchanged worktree. The deployment-specific CPU measurement was inspected as recorded evidence, not independently reproduced.\\\",\\n  \\\"criteria\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assumption-integrity\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N3\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Immutable captured bytes justify value reuse, but do not justify dropping each consumer's dependency attribution. The deployment-specific timing remains an implementer measurement.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-concurrency\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N1\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"sync.Once serializes concurrent misses, but lifecycle refusal is converted into transcript success.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-contracts\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N2\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The existing SourceLoss contract is not preserved for memo lifecycle errors.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-input-errors\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N1\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-integration-impact\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N3\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Operation-wide reuse is not integrated with per-producer final-audit attribution.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-observability\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N2\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"compatibility\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N1\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Public signatures and serialized formats remain unchanged, but finalized-view error behavior changes.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"correctness\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N1\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"design-causality\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-c0693406841990a9\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"D1 addresses repeated parsing and hashing directly by retaining derived ledger values inside the existing operation. The implementation uses one sync.Once cell per key, preserves native recomputation without an operation, and copies returned records. Its lifecycle and attribution defects are reported separately.\\\",\\n      \\\"mappings\\\": [\\n        {\\n          \\\"delta\\\": \\\"SD-16da51ec\\\",\\n          \\\"basis\\\": \\\"R1\\\",\\n          \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"mapped\\\",\\n          \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The validation matrix registers the permanent integration check for read-once behavior, fallback, equivalence, concurrent misses, copy isolation and finalization. The adjacent doctor check belongs to the separately governed companion scope.\\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"delta\\\": \\\"SD-55df3a37\\\",\\n          \\\"basis\\\": \\\"D1\\\",\\n          \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"mapped\\\",\\n          \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"ADR amendment D14 records operation-scoped derived-value reuse, first-read closure coverage, copies and no cross-operation retention.\\\"\\n        }\\n      ]\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"documentation\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-c0693406841990a9\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The spec, ADR D14 and registered validation command describe the selected optimization and its boundaries consistently. Git latency is explicitly separated into follow-ups; no public format migration is claimed.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"operability\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N2\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Discarding the lifecycle error removes the existing actionable read-error diagnostic.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"requirements\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N1\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Sealed tests cover the principal R1-R3 behavior, but R4 is violated by the discarded error.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"scope\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-c0693406841990a9\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The selected artifacts implement the approved operation-local ledger optimization and its governance evidence. No cross-operation cache, ledger-format change or new authorization mechanism is introduced.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"security\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N1\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"A refused integrity check must not return the success sentinel. Root authorization and existing size bounds otherwise remain in the underlying readers.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"solution-proportionality\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-c0693406841990a9\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"An operation-owned map with per-key sync.Once is a small sufficient mechanism for the measured repeated work. It avoids persistent invalidation machinery, background workers and speculative cross-operation reuse. D1 would need reconsideration if inputs ceased to be immutable within an operation or memory retention exceeded the existing operation budgets.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"tools\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"artifact-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-review-ledger-is-read-once-per-operation --strict\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Executed and exited zero. For the exact sealed subject, also inspected /var/tmp/closeout/ac-rl.out, which names cs-653e8a9bf9e7 and head e37b673ef02fa7b0b7c6789712dd1ce570613983. The rerun resolved a different head, so its scope identity was not substituted for the sealed report.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-design\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-c0693406841990a9\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Used the sealed structural assessment and independently inspected its mapped changes; did not rerun assessments that write repository state.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-discover\\\",\\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-c0693406841990a9\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Did not run the state-writing discovery assessment in this read-only review; inspected the component implementation and sealed evidence directly.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-integrate\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-ledger-is-read-once-per-operation-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Did not run the state-writing assessment. Inspected sealed integration results and downstream consumers; N3 records the uncovered attribution integration defect.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-tech-debt\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:git diff 319bfd9c99ae17e6db4945ab348b5a4cf4f51551..e37b673ef02fa7b0b7c6789712dd1ce570613983 -- pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view.go pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_ledger_memo.go pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_operation_view.go\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Did not run the state-writing assessment. Inspected the implementation diff, searched the new memo files for debt markers, and reviewed the spec's explicit Git-performance follow-ups.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"closeout-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:pose context --task spec:pose-review-ledger-is-read-once-per-operation --json\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Completion check depends on the recorded review conclusion and is deferred to POSE; this review requests changes.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"review-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:pose context --task spec:pose-review-ledger-is-read-once-per-operation --json\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Cannot verify this attestation before POSE records it. No attestation was written.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"suggest-review\\\",\\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Executed; selected backend-Go, security and documentation rules and the review workflow.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"surface-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-ledger-is-read-once-per-operation-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Executed strict surface-check: exited zero with one target, 231 results and zero findings. Also inspected the supplied sealed-subject report /var/tmp/closeout/sc-rl.out. This establishes composition coverage, not absence of the reported defects.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"validate\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Used the sealed pipeline execution of pose validate --strict and inspected delivery-validation.json, including the passing ledger integration result. Did not rerun build-producing validation in the read-only sandbox.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"validate\\\",\\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-ledger-is-read-once-per-operation-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Used sealed component validation, including the registered seven-test ledger suite. Read those tests independently; they do not cover N1-N3. No local test execution is claimed.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\\n```\",\n.pose/review-runs/rrn-5e598ead031d2345.json:106:  \"output\": \"decision: changes-requested\\n\\n**F24 — low, blocker:** [doctor_commit_graph.go:167](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-732430253/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/cli/doctor_commit_graph.go:167) treats every nonzero configured Bloom-filter version as usable. With `commitGraph.changedPathsVersion=3`, Git 2.56 consults no filters, but doctor recommends a rewrite that retains the unsupported setting. Report an actionable configuration warning and add regression coverage.\\n\\nAll eight listed prior findings are fixed. Sealed validation reports 233 passing checks; I inspected the tests and reproduced F24 using read-only Git commands. No repository changes or attestations were made.\\n\\nRules applied during review: feature review workflow, backend-go, security, documentation-style and delivery-evidence. Knowledge was consulted; no residual risk was accepted.\\n\\n```pose-draft\\n{\\n  \\\"schema\\\": \\\"pose.review.draft/v1\\\",\\n  \\\"decision\\\": \\\"changes-requested\\\",\\n  \\\"findings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"F24\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"low\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"blocker\\\",\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/doctor_commit_graph.go\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": 167,\\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"commitGraphReadsDisabledBy treats every nonzero changedPathsVersion as usable. Read-only reproduction on Git 2.56 with commitGraph.changedPathsVersion=3: git config --type=int --get returns 3 successfully, while git log -1 --format=%H -- AGENTS.md exits zero and emits Bloom statistics with filter_not_present=1583, maybe=0 and definitely_not=0. Lines 167-172 return no configuration diagnosis, so doctor.go recommends a fixable rewrite. The installed git-config manual supports only -1, 0, 1 and 2; the Git binary also contains the diagnostic rejecting writes of unsupported versions. The advertised repair preserves this setting. Under R3, report a bounded actionable warning naming the unsupported configuration instead of recommending a rewrite, and add regression coverage.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"prior_findings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R1-F5\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"doctor_commit_graph.go:47-95 distinguishes expected exclusions from repository, HEAD, tree and history failures; lines 89-90 preserve successful history warnings before the threshold. doctor.go:369-370 emits warn. Regression tests cover broken history and malformed graphs at both history sizes.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R3-F11\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"doctor_commit_graph.go:74-80 excludes an empty HEAD tree before counting history or returning for the threshold. TestDoctorCommitGraphSkipsAnEmptyTree and TestDoctorCommitGraphSkipsAShortEmptyTree cover both branches.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R3-F14\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"doctor_commit_graph.go:82-90 checks successful rev-list stderr, and lines 109-116 check successful lookup stderr. TestDoctorCommitGraphReportsAnUnreadableGraph and TestDoctorCommitGraphWarnsBelowTheThreshold cover malformed graphs.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R4-F17\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"doctor_commit_graph.go:74-80 returns not-applicable for empty HEAD trees independently of history size; doctor_commit_graph_test.go:278-286 and 377-383 cover the exclusion.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R4-F20\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"doctor_commit_graph.go:89-90 and 115-116 preserve successful Git diagnostics as errors rendered at warn; doctor_commit_graph_test.go:334-343 and 363-372 exercise malformed graphs.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R5-F21\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"doctor_commit_graph.go:89-90 checks rev-list stderr before the threshold return at lines 97-98. TestDoctorCommitGraphWarnsBelowTheThreshold, lines 363-372, covers the reported short-history failure.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R5-F22\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"doctor_commit_graph.go:74-80 performs empty-tree exclusion before the short-history return. TestDoctorCommitGraphSkipsAShortEmptyTree, lines 377-383, exercises a short history without lowering the threshold.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R5-F23\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"doctor.go:94 and 375-379 display --max-new-filters=-1; doctor_commit_graph.go:181-187 runs that effective command. TestDoctorCommitGraphShowsTheEffectiveCommand, lines 388-401, checks the displayed command and its result under maxNewFilters=0.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"sweep\\\": \\\"Reviewed the complete changed doctor implementation, fix registry and execution/recheck path, all new regression tests, both full-history CI jobs, validation-matrix deltas, spec R1-R4 and D1, structural metadata facts, sealed validation report, artifact and surface outputs, applicable rules and related knowledge. Checked exclusions, thresholds, malformed history and graphs, alternate and split graphs, literal paths, configuration precedence and unsupported versions, partial-clone fetch prevention, diagnostic redaction, temporary trace lifecycle and CLI compatibility. Reproduced the unsupported-version behavior using read-only Git commands. No builds, repairs, edits or attestations were performed.\\\",\\n  \\\"criteria\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assumption-integrity\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-41b046075b716869\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Examined the 500-commit threshold, reliance on Git trace2 Bloom statistics, Git configuration semantics and sealed test evidence. The threshold is D1's explicit design choice; trace2 stability is a documented technical risk. Real Git 2.56 confirms the probe mechanism. Unsupported configuration behavior is separately reported as F24; fresh package execution was unavailable under the read-only boundary.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-concurrency\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The feature adds synchronous CLI subprocess calls rather than shared concurrent runtime state. Each trace uses a unique temporary file with deferred removal; tests restore their threshold override and do not run these fixtures in parallel.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-contracts\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/doctor-recommends-the-commit-graph-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The finding and fix use the existing doctor report and registry contracts. No public API, event or MCP schema is changed.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-input-errors\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"F24\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-integration-impact\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/doctor-recommends-the-commit-graph-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Inspected production diagnostic composition, fix registration and post-fix recheck, plus real-repository integration fixtures and CI placement.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-observability\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"F24\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"compatibility\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/doctor-recommends-the-commit-graph-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Examined doctor JSON and text rendering, remediation classification and fix execution. The new checks are additive and preserve the existing report format and public CLI/MCP contracts.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"correctness\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"F24\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"design-causality\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-41b046075b716869\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"D1 puts repository maintenance behind doctor advice and explicit repair, addressing repeated expensive path-history lookups without mutating governance reads. Asking Git which filters it actually consults avoids duplicating alternate-object and graph-format selection logic. The three structural deltas expand permanent regression coverage for that behavior.\\\",\\n      \\\"mappings\\\": [\\n        {\\n          \\\"delta\\\": \\\"SD-28db7861\\\",\\n          \\\"basis\\\": \\\"R3\\\",\\n          \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"mapped\\\",\\n          \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Broadens the doctor integration selector to include the complete TestDoctorCommitGraph regression family, covering exclusions, read failures and configuration behavior.\\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"delta\\\": \\\"SD-9fc0fe4e\\\",\\n          \\\"basis\\\": \\\"R3\\\",\\n          \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"mapped\\\",\\n          \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Adds unreadable-history regression coverage to the permanent doctor integration command.\\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"delta\\\": \\\"SD-d29398e6\\\",\\n          \\\"basis\\\": \\\"R3\\\",\\n          \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"mapped\\\",\\n          \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Adds broken-versus-unborn, literal-path and disabled-read configuration regressions to the permanent integration command.\\\"\\n        }\\n      ]\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"documentation\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-41b046075b716869\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Inspected spec requirements, D1, requirement trace, runtime remediation messages and CI comments. The displayed manual repair now matches the effective fixed-argument repair, and the operational workflow remains the existing doctor advice/preview/apply flow.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"operability\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"F24\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"requirements\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"F24\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"scope\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-41b046075b716869\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The doctor check, explicit repair, CI preparation and permanent regression registration match R1-R4 and the declared artifacts. Adjacent validation entries in the cumulative range belong to separately identified work; no unrelated runtime feature was introduced by this delivery.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"security\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/doctor-recommends-the-commit-graph-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Examined fixed Git arguments, literal pathspec handling, RawHistoryGit environment isolation, disabled lazy fetching, private temporary trace creation and existing secret-shaped-content redaction. No new dependency, authority boundary or credential handling was introduced.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"solution-proportionality\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-41b046075b716869\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Compared the implementation with documentation alone, implicit writes during governance reads and a custom graph parser. The existing doctor registry plus a Git-owned probe is a proportionate implementation of D1, without a background maintenance service or new persistence layer. Loss of compatible trace2 Bloom statistics would invalidate the probe choice and requires revisiting it.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"tools\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"artifact-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-doctor-recommends-the-commit-graph --strict --json\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Ran the read-only strict check successfully. Also inspected /var/tmp/closeout/ac-dc.out, which identifies the requested change set and exact sealed range. Its provenance diagnostics are warning-level.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-design\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-41b046075b716869\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Did not rerun the assessment producer under the no-write boundary. Used the supplied sealed structural evidence and independently inspected D1 and the metadata changes.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-discover\\\",\\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Discovery can write assessment artifacts. Resolved the component read-only and inspected its implementation and sealed validation evidence.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-integrate\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/doctor-recommends-the-commit-graph-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Did not invoke the assessment producer under the no-write boundary. Inspected production composition and real-Git integration tests; no public inter-module schema changed.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-tech-debt\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Did not run the writing assessment producer. Independently searched the new implementation and tests for TODO, FIXME, stub and panic markers and inspected the spec's existing doctor-performance follow-up.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"closeout-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:pose context --task spec:pose-doctor-recommends-the-commit-graph --json\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Completion-only gate is deferred until POSE records and verifies the review conclusion; this review does not record an attestation.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"review-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:pose context --task spec:pose-doctor-recommends-the-commit-graph --json\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Cannot establish approval before the review conclusion has been recorded.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"suggest-review\\\",\\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Executed successfully and applied its backend-go, security and documentation-style rule selection.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"surface-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/doctor-recommends-the-commit-graph-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Ran the strict read-only surface check successfully. The supplied sealed output at /var/tmp/closeout/sc-dc.out records one delivery target, 233 results and zero surface findings.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"validate\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/doctor-recommends-the-commit-graph-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Used the sealed strict pipeline validation as directed by the read-only boundary. Inspected delivery-validation.json: 233 executed checks passed with zero failures or errors. Did not attempt a fresh build or test run.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"validate\\\",\\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Inspected sealed module build, unit and doctor integration results and read the regression tests. They pass but do not cover the unsupported changedPathsVersion configuration reported in F24.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\\n```\",\n.pose/review-runs/rrn-4a37964df583131c.json:86:  \"brief_notes\": \"Review of spec pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit, implemented by Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic). The ADR `.pose/adr/2026-11-12-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-and-benefit.md` is Accepted; judge the implementation against it and the spec, not the decision itself.\\n\\nMechanism. Review policy schema 5 adds `milestone_review_required` / `roadmap_review_required` (`never|when-justified|always`), validated in `parseReviewPolicy` via `validateCloseoutReviewPolicyKeys` (closeout_review_policy.go). One evaluator `evaluateCloseoutReview` (closeout-review@1): canonical members `xref:\\u003cproject\\u003e/spec:\\u003cslug\\u003e` (aliases, verified redirects, federated resolver, unknown = diagnostic, never zero) and ADR associations (closeout_adr_associations.go: roadmap `adrs:`, ADR `roadmaps:`, local Markdown links both ways; malformed/missing/unreadable = unknown). `closeoutReviewGate` is the single entry for readers: receipt first, roadmap done before adoption = legacy (nil decision), else evaluate + `protectCloseoutDecision` (baseline policy at the change set base when the scope changes the review contract); exemption only when not required AND no review recorded on the scope (`scopeReviewRecorded`, unreadable counts as recorded). Consumers: `reviewCheck` (review_closeout.go, Required=false + ApprovalOrigin), `proportionalReviewVerification` (review_bundle.go; under adoption the legacy singleton inheritance and `unreviewed_milestones` are skipped), `getCloseoutState` (CloseRequired, receipt, terminal only with receipt, new diagnostics), `ReachedMilestones`/`RoadmapsReachedBy`/`roadmapReachedApartFrom` (roadmaps.go), `milestoneReachedObligations`, `ReviewPlan.CloseoutReview` (out of the digest), doctor (`CloseoutReviewsOwed`), setup and `pose adopt` (capability_catalog.go `closeoutReviewPolicyCatalogEntry`, `SetCloseoutReviewPolicy`; refs/transfer adopt/retire no longer lower schema 5). CLI close (cli/review_closeout.go `closeoutReceiptPreflight`, `publishCloseoutReceipt`): milestone and roadmap close publish an immutable receipt (closeout_receipt.go, ExpectAbsent publish, strict parse); a done roadmap without receipt is completed by a new close. `milestoneMember` now maps `spec:\\u003cslug\\u003e` to its slug (was `spec:spec:\\u003cslug\\u003e` in closeout state). Existing tests changed on purpose: catalog lists, schema after adopt (fresh install is now schema 5), progressive_review fixtures that force schema 2, and the previous-release compatibility test (a fresh install is refused by v7.4.0 by its schema, by ADR design; an updated legacy instance stays readable).\\n\\nPlease do an exhaustive sweep in this round and report ALL findings together, classified blocker vs follow-up. Inventory every entry point that answers \\\"is this aggregate scope approved / closed / reached\\\" (CLI close, closeout-check, review-check, review verify, review-plan, attention/obligations, reached, nextCloses, roadmap check, MCP closeout state, federated acceptance, doctor) and check each one reads the same gate, cannot launder a recorded rejection under `never`, cannot let `always` be weakened by inheritance or `unreviewed_milestones`, and never treats an unknown member/association as an exemption. Also check: receipts are never overwritten nor fabricated for history; `pose update` never adopts; no schema-5 downgrade path; the recovery path for a roadmap done without receipt cannot close a scope whose review is required and unapproved.\\n\\nKnown pre-existing state: `pose check --strict` reports 19 delivery-contract errors of other specs (runtime worktree, common-domain handoff, governance performance, bounded graph caches), identical line by line on the base commit 956153f1; they are follow-up F4, not this spec.\\n\\nRequired tools: run `pose artifact-check --spec pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit --strict` and `pose surface-check --spec pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit --strict`; declare each `passed` only after running it (evidence `command:\\u003cthe command\\u003e`, rationale quoting its result). The surface-check disposition must cite both an `integration:` and a `reachability:` sealed evidence id. Cite sealed `unit:`/`integration:` ids for criteria, never `SD-…` structural facts or requirement ids. Send each shell command alone in its own call (no pipes, `;`, `\\u0026\\u0026`, redirects). `validate` of a component with registered checks is `passed` with the sealed run's evidence; `review-check` and `closeout-check` are `deferred`. New findings have bare ids (F1, F2 …); follow-ups carry `action`, `owner`, `review_by`; only low-severity risks may be accepted.\\n\\nRound 15. Account in `prior_findings` exactly for the findings the brief lists as open for this scope (your round-14 run rrn-348663b5b871bc42: R13-N46 and R13-N47, plus any earlier partial the brief shows), each with whether it stands. Since round 14 the association reader is fail-closed by design: the code/comment filter added for N40 is gone, so code and comments are read like prose and a link shown as an example still counts (over-enforcement: the answer may become unknown or require review; accepted residual risk, follow-up F6), and a destination with parentheses, which the extractor may cut short, leaves the answer unknown in both directions (N47). Classify accordingly: a Markdown form in which a real association is silently dropped and an exemption follows is a blocker; a form that makes the reader require review or report unknown where a perfect parser would not is a follow-up under F6. Dispose the `validate` tools from the sealed evidence: the pipeline ran `pose validate --strict` on a clean clone of the sealed commit with a GitHub token (`.pose/results/delivery-validation.json`); a rerun in your sandbox fails for environment reasons and is not evidence about the code. A finding object accepts exactly `id`, `severity`, `disposition`, `file`, `line`, `summary`, and for an accepted follow-up `action`, `owner`, `review_by`; put any rationale inside `summary`. Do NOT run `pose assess`, `pose state`, `pose index` or anything else that writes under `.pose/`; dispose assess-* tools from the sealed evidence and the code. Leave the worktree as you found it. Sweep the whole surface again and report every remaining finding in one pass, classified blocker vs follow-up; a remote variant of a threat the ADR does not promise to defend is a follow-up, and so is a pre-existing gap of the federation or transfer engine that this spec did not introduce and does not claim to close.\\n\",\n.pose/review-runs/rrn-4a37964df583131c.json:106:  \"output\": \"decision: changes-requested\\n\\n- **N48 — medium blocker:** [closeout_adr_associations.go:50](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-3967574839/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_adr_associations.go:50) silently drops encoded Markdown associations. For example, `../adr/decision%2Emd` and `../adr/decision\\u0026#46;md` name `decision.md`, but produce neither an association nor a diagnostic. Equivalent backlinks fail too. A two-member roadmap can consequently receive an incorrect exemption.\\n- **N49 — low follow-up:** Code/comment examples and parentheses can require extra review or return unknown. This remains the accepted F6 over-enforcement risk.\\n\\nBoth prior findings are fixed. Targeted tests across domain, CLI and MCP passed; `go vet ./...` passed. Required artifact and surface commands exited 0. The repository remains unchanged.\\n\\nRules applied: mixed Go/governance feature; review workflow, backend-go, security, documentation-style, delivery-evidence and knowledge-governance.\\n\\n```pose-draft\\n{\\n  \\\"schema\\\": \\\"pose.review.draft/v1\\\",\\n  \\\"decision\\\": \\\"changes-requested\\\",\\n  \\\"findings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"N48\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"medium\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"blocker\\\",\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_adr_associations.go\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": 50,\\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"Decode Markdown destinations before testing the association namespace and extension, or report unsupported forms as unknown. The reader does not decode URL escapes or Markdown character references; it also truncates numeric character references at '#'. Thus '[decision](../adr/decision%2Emd)', '[decision](../adr/decision\\u0026#46;md)' and '[decision](../%61dr/decision.md)' all name the canonical decision.md but are silently skipped at lines 174-175. Equivalent backlinks to pair.md are skipped at lines 245-246. A read-only reproduction using the extracted production regex and namespace predicates confirmed associations=[] and diagnostics=[] for all six forward/backward cases. With two resolved members and no other association, evaluateCloseoutReview therefore returns Known=true and Required=false, violating R3. Normalize supported destination escapes before containment checks, or fail closed, and cover both association directions.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"N49\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"low\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"follow-up\\\",\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_adr_associations.go\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": 43,\\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"Existing spec follow-up F6 remains applicable: links shown in code or comments count as associations, and destinations containing parentheses return unknown even when a complete Markdown parser could resolve them. This can demand unnecessary review, but does not grant an exemption. Inspection and the passing TestCloseoutReviewPolicyRoundTwelve/RoundFourteen regressions confirm the conservative behavior; accept this limited over-enforcement risk.\\\",\\n      \\\"action\\\": \\\"Complete existing spec follow-up F6 with context-aware Markdown parsing while retaining fail-closed behavior for unsupported or unresolved local associations.\\\",\\n      \\\"owner\\\": \\\"@pose-maintainers\\\",\\n      \\\"review_by\\\": \\\"2026-12-13\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"prior_findings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R13-N46\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"closeout_adr_associations.go:42-64 no longer filters code or comments. TestCloseoutReviewPolicyRoundFourteen at closeout_review_policy_test.go:1604 covers both reported bodies in both association directions. Ran go test ./internal/pose ./internal/cli ./internal/mcpserver -run 'Test.*CloseoutReview|Test.*CloseoutReceipt|Test.*ADRAssociation' -count=1; all three packages passed.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R13-N47\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"closeout_adr_associations.go:170-172 and 241-243 now diagnose destinations containing parentheses before extension filtering. TestCloseoutReviewPolicyRoundFourteen at closeout_review_policy_test.go:1630 covers forward and backward destinations and requires unknown rather than exemption. The targeted three-package test command passed.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"sweep\\\": \\\"Reviewed the spec R1-R7, D1/D2, accepted ADR, changed production files, schemas, manuals, templates and regression tests. Traced policy adoption and schema preservation; canonical member and transfer resolution; forward/reverse ADR metadata and Markdown parsing; protected baselines and mandatory-human requirements; voluntary-review vetoes; immutable receipt publication, interrupted roadmap recovery and historical verification. Inventoried CLI close, closeout-check, review-check, review verify, review-plan, attention/obligations, reached, nextCloses, roadmap-check, MCP closeout state, readiness/portfolio dependencies, federated acceptance and doctor. Checked their shared review/terminal paths and supporting member/cut-criteria gates. Ran required artifact-check and surface-check, suggest review, targeted three-package tests, go vet ./..., git diff --check and git status. Examined adversarial-corpus coverage and identified the uncovered encoded-destination exemption in N48. Used sealed full-validation evidence; did not run assessment/index/state writers or record an attestation. Final worktree status was clean.\\\",\\n  \\\"criteria\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assumption-integrity\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Verified schema/default/legacy behavior and prior-finding fixes against code and independently rerun tests. Full validation is sealed producer evidence, not a claimed local rerun. Distinguished the unresolved R3 defect N48 from the conservative, owned F6 risk N49. Remote backlink discovery and protection against nonparticipating external writers remain outside the accepted design.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-concurrency\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/writer-coordination-and-atomic-publication-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Inspected guarded close, repeated authorization checks, ExpectAbsent receipt publication and intent/status/receipt sequencing. Existing coordination bounds remain in use; failures leave an incomplete close rather than overwriting a receipt.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-contracts\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Schema 5 explicitly migrates the aggregate policy contract while schemas 1-4 retain legacy semantics. CLI configuration requires the pair, MCP additions are projections, and receipt schema/path contracts are covered.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-input-errors\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N48\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-integration-impact\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Traced CLI/MCP domain reuse, receipt-backed producer proof, canonical transfer destinations and aggregate dependency closure. The association defect is shared domain behavior, not transport divergence.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-observability\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N48\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"compatibility\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-policy-adoption-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Reviewed explicit adoption, legacy cutoffs and sealed-plan handling, schema-5 preservation in reference/transfer toggles, and previous-release compatibility tests. Older engines intentionally refuse fresh schema-5 instances; update does not adopt the pair.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"correctness\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N48\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"design-causality\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-846b41e9a5123ab5\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"D1 separates explicit aggregate closure from independent review using deterministic thresholds. D2 reuses the resolver, capability catalog and setup/adopt paths, adding receipts because milestone close previously had no persisted transition. Shared evaluation and receipt-backed terminal projection address inconsistent exemptions and closure claims; N48 identifies an implementation failure in association recognition.\\\",\\n      \\\"mappings\\\": [\\n        {\\n          \\\"delta\\\": \\\"SD-3ce6ee69\\\",\\n          \\\"basis\\\": \\\"R4\\\",\\n          \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"mapped\\\",\\n          \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The explicit close delivery exposed the measured governance read-budget refusal. The spec's artifact reconciliation links the bounded 1-GiB amendment to completing close without truncating historical inputs.\\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"delta\\\": \\\"SD-c74440ab\\\",\\n          \\\"basis\\\": \\\"R3\\\",\\n          \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"mapped\\\",\\n          \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The roadmap template exposes adrs: [] for the explicit ADR associations used by when-justified.\\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"delta\\\": \\\"SD-ec2d86f4\\\",\\n          \\\"basis\\\": \\\"R1\\\",\\n          \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"mapped\\\",\\n          \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The accepted ADR records policy location, deterministic modes, defaults, historical compatibility and authority protections before implementation.\\\"\\n        }\\n      ]\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"documentation\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/distributed-instructions-parity-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Compared English/Portuguese manuals, scaffold copies and roadmap templates with runtime policy names, thresholds, adoption, explicit close and receipt behavior. The supported contract is documented consistently; N48 is its implementation defect, and F6 records conservative parser limitations.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"operability\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N48\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"requirements\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N48\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"scope\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Compared the declared artifacts and production changes with R1-R7 and D1/D2. Policy, receipt, reader, setup/doctor, schema and documentation changes support the approved aggregate closeout scope. No new MCP write tool or global ADR identity framework was introduced.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"security\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N48\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"solution-proportionality\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-846b41e9a5123ab5\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"A shared evaluator plus a write-once terminal receipt is sufficient for distinct review/close semantics; reusing adopt/setup/resolver avoids another configuration framework or global ADR type. Metadata alone would lose existing explicit Markdown associations. A narrow parser is sufficient only if unsupported local forms return unknown; N48 shows that condition is currently violated and needs correction. Remote backlink inventory remains deliberately excluded.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"tools\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"artifact-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit --strict\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Ran the exact command; exit 0. Output included artifact.claims=46, artifact.observed=185 and artifact.findings=920 with provenance warnings. This is a successful gate exit, not a claim of warning-free global provenance.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-design\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Did not rerun an assessment writer under the no-repository-changes boundary. Examined the design and structural mappings using sealed structure:design-846b41e9a5123ab5 and the current spec/ADR/code.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-discover\\\",\\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Did not regenerate component assessments. Inspected current component sources, validation registration and sealed pose-mcp evidence directly.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-integrate\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Did not run the assessment writer. Traced CLI/MCP/federation integration in code and examined sealed integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration plus independently rerun three-package tests.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-tech-debt\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Did not write assessment artifacts. Inspected changed production markers and the spec's explicit follow-ups, including the bounded-read capacity debt and F6 parser limitations.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"closeout-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Completion gate requires the recorded review conclusion; no attestation was recorded during this independent review.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"review-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Completion gate must follow POSE recording and verifying this review conclusion.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"suggest-review\\\",\\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Exit 0; selected backend-go, security and documentation-style under the review workflow. Also applied delivery-evidence and consulted knowledge governance for residual-risk handling.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"surface-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Ran pose surface-check --spec pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit --strict; exit 0 with surface.targets=1, surface.results=213 and surface.findings=0. Composition evidence: integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration. Reachability evidence: reachability:pose-mcp/go/closeout-plan-reachability. A passing surface gate does not cover the missing encoded-destination negative case N48.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"validate\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Disposed from the sealed strict producer run, not rerun locally because validate writes repository results. Inspected delivery-validation.json: 213 checks, all pass. Independently reran the closeout-policy tests across pose, cli and mcpserver; all passed. go vet ./... also passed.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"validate\\\",\\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"build:pose-mcp/go/build\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The sealed strict run includes the component's registered build, unit, integration and e2e checks. Current targeted domain/CLI/MCP tests and go vet passed independently; the uncovered R3 parser case remains N48.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\\n```\",\n.pose/review-runs/rrn-a5f810837f976a64.json:117:  \"output\": \"decision: approved\\n\\nNo defects found. The targeted tests and strict artifact/surface checks passed. Both broad local validation runs failed, including a 600-second unit-test timeout; approval relies on the supplied sealed validation evidence, not those reruns. The worktree remains unchanged.\\n\\nRules applied: pose-review workflow, backend-go, security, documentation-style, and delivery-evidence. Knowledge governance was consulted; no knowledge artifacts were changed.\\n\\n```pose-draft\\n{\\n  \\\"schema\\\": \\\"pose.review.draft/v1\\\",\\n  \\\"decision\\\": \\\"approved\\\",\\n  \\\"findings\\\": [],\\n  \\\"criteria\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assumption-integrity\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-444c1b1b0cc8d340\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Compared R1-R3 with the diff and existing apply path. Verified that catalog adoption mutates freshly loaded in-memory policy maps. The spec explicitly acknowledges that adopt.values lacks a direct assertion; its behavior was inspected in code. Broad local validation failed, so full-suite assurance rests on the supplied sealed evidence.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-concurrency\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/writer-coordination-and-atomic-publication-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The added preview performs synchronous reads and local map mutations; it adds no goroutines, lifecycle ownership or publication changes.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-contracts\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/adopt-request-shows-what-it-sets-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The change adds the specified preview fields while preserving request arguments, pair-flag refusal and apply behavior.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-input-errors\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/configuration-review-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Existing request validation remains intact. Policy-load failures return contextual errors and stop processing.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-integration-impact\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/adopt-request-shows-what-it-sets-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Reviewed the configuration-review request, adoption CLI and setup composition. Targeted tests passed independently.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-observability\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/adopt-request-shows-what-it-sets-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The preview now exposes catalog changes through adopt.change and provides actionable closeout-value guidance without adding sensitive output.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"compatibility\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/configuration-review-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Inspected CLI parsing and application. Existing arguments, persisted policy formats and MCP contracts remain unchanged; additional human-readable preview fields are declared by the spec.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"correctness\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/adopt-request-shows-what-it-sets-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The preview invokes the same catalog adoption function as apply, using the selected date. The focused regression, configuration-review and pair-refusal tests passed independently.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"design-causality\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-444c1b1b0cc8d340\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"R1's cause was omission of catalog mutations from the request preview. Reusing entry.Adopt on freshly loaded maps exposes those mutations without changing persistence. The closeout-specific message addresses R2, and the four attribution edits address R3. No individual structural delta facts were listed in the supplied brief.\\\",\\n      \\\"mappings\\\": []\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"documentation\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/distributed-instructions-parity-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Inspected all four manual diffs. English and Portuguese source and scaffold copies consistently attribute the sandboxed profile to pose-dist.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"operability\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/adopt-request-shows-what-it-sets-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Inspected adopt.go: policy changes are printed before adopt.apply, and the closeout guidance names both value flags and their accepted alternatives.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"requirements\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/adopt-request-shows-what-it-sets-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"R1 is covered by the focused regression and apply-path comparison. R2 was verified against the closeout catalog defaults and emitted guidance; its direct-test gap is disclosed in the spec. R3 was verified across all four manual changes.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"scope\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-444c1b1b0cc8d340\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Compared the requested range with the spec's artifacts and non-goals. The change is limited to preview reporting, its regression/check registration, manual attribution and governance records. It does not change what an answer applies.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"security\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/configuration-review-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Inspected the added reads, catalog lookup, output and existing answer validation. The change adds no command execution, caller-controlled path, credential handling or authority bypass.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"solution-proportionality\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-444c1b1b0cc8d340\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Reusing the existing catalog mutator is a small sufficient fix and avoids duplicating policy-key descriptions. The capability-specific guidance is bounded to the present requirement. This choice would need reconsideration if catalog adoption gained external side effects or stopped being safe on isolated in-memory maps.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"tools\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"artifact-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-adopt-request-shows-what-it-sets --strict --from 43099880d96a55d195811bf1f5269a9a3d14073d --to 5c3c804541a1e5020bb41be2b284c61fe65227af --json\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Ran verification bound to the requested range; exit 0, with no error or critical findings.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-design\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-444c1b1b0cc8d340\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Used the supplied sealed structure evidence and independently inspected the spec, diff and catalog/apply relationship. Did not regenerate assessment artifacts.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-discover\\\",\\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"A component-wide assessment refresh was unnecessary for this bounded review and could write repository assessment state.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-integrate\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/adopt-request-shows-what-it-sets-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Inspected the existing CLI/domain boundary and supplied integration evidence. No REST, event, Protobuf or MCP contract changed; did not regenerate assessment state.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-tech-debt\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Inspected the changed code directly. It adds no TODO, FIXME, stub or panic marker; did not regenerate assessment state.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"closeout-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Requires the completed review conclusion to be recorded and verified by POSE.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"review-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Requires the completed review conclusion to be recorded and verified by POSE.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"suggest-review\\\",\\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Resolved the backend-go, security and documentation-style review trail.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"surface-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/adopt-request-shows-what-it-sets-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Ran pose surface-check --spec pose-adopt-request-shows-what-it-sets --strict; exit 0, one target and zero findings.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"validate\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Disposition refers to the supplied sealed producer's passing validation evidence. Independently ran pose validate --strict; that local rerun exited 1, including a 600-second unit-test timeout, and is not represented as passing.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"validate\\\",\\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/adopt-request-shows-what-it-sets-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Disposition refers to the supplied sealed producer's passing validation evidence. Independently ran pose validate --strict --module pose-mcp; that local rerun exited 1, including a 600-second unit-test timeout. The focused adoption/configuration-review tests passed independently.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\\n```\",\n.pose/review-runs/rrn-93914466c27974f9.json:86:  \"brief_notes\": \"Review of spec pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit, implemented by Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic). The ADR `.pose/adr/2026-11-12-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-and-benefit.md` is Accepted; judge the implementation against it and the spec, not the decision itself.\\n\\nMechanism. Review policy schema 5 adds `milestone_review_required` / `roadmap_review_required` (`never|when-justified|always`), validated in `parseReviewPolicy` via `validateCloseoutReviewPolicyKeys` (closeout_review_policy.go). One evaluator `evaluateCloseoutReview` (closeout-review@1): canonical members `xref:\\u003cproject\\u003e/spec:\\u003cslug\\u003e` (aliases, verified redirects, federated resolver, unknown = diagnostic, never zero) and ADR associations (closeout_adr_associations.go: roadmap `adrs:`, ADR `roadmaps:`, local Markdown links both ways; malformed/missing/unreadable = unknown). `closeoutReviewGate` is the single entry for readers: receipt first, roadmap done before adoption = legacy (nil decision), else evaluate + `protectCloseoutDecision` (baseline policy at the change set base when the scope changes the review contract); exemption only when not required AND no review recorded on the scope (`scopeReviewRecorded`, unreadable counts as recorded). Consumers: `reviewCheck` (review_closeout.go, Required=false + ApprovalOrigin), `proportionalReviewVerification` (review_bundle.go; under adoption the legacy singleton inheritance and `unreviewed_milestones` are skipped), `getCloseoutState` (CloseRequired, receipt, terminal only with receipt, new diagnostics), `ReachedMilestones`/`RoadmapsReachedBy`/`roadmapReachedApartFrom` (roadmaps.go), `milestoneReachedObligations`, `ReviewPlan.CloseoutReview` (out of the digest), doctor (`CloseoutReviewsOwed`), setup and `pose adopt` (capability_catalog.go `closeoutReviewPolicyCatalogEntry`, `SetCloseoutReviewPolicy`; refs/transfer adopt/retire no longer lower schema 5). CLI close (cli/review_closeout.go `closeoutReceiptPreflight`, `publishCloseoutReceipt`): milestone and roadmap close publish an immutable receipt (closeout_receipt.go, ExpectAbsent publish, strict parse); a done roadmap without receipt is completed by a new close. `milestoneMember` now maps `spec:\\u003cslug\\u003e` to its slug (was `spec:spec:\\u003cslug\\u003e` in closeout state). Existing tests changed on purpose: catalog lists, schema after adopt (fresh install is now schema 5), progressive_review fixtures that force schema 2, and the previous-release compatibility test (a fresh install is refused by v7.4.0 by its schema, by ADR design; an updated legacy instance stays readable).\\n\\nPlease do an exhaustive sweep in this round and report ALL findings together, classified blocker vs follow-up. Inventory every entry point that answers \\\"is this aggregate scope approved / closed / reached\\\" (CLI close, closeout-check, review-check, review verify, review-plan, attention/obligations, reached, nextCloses, roadmap check, MCP closeout state, federated acceptance, doctor) and check each one reads the same gate, cannot launder a recorded rejection under `never`, cannot let `always` be weakened by inheritance or `unreviewed_milestones`, and never treats an unknown member/association as an exemption. Also check: receipts are never overwritten nor fabricated for history; `pose update` never adopts; no schema-5 downgrade path; the recovery path for a roadmap done without receipt cannot close a scope whose review is required and unapproved.\\n\\nKnown pre-existing state: `pose check --strict` reports 19 delivery-contract errors of other specs (runtime worktree, common-domain handoff, governance performance, bounded graph caches), identical line by line on the base commit 956153f1; they are follow-up F4, not this spec.\\n\\nRequired tools: run `pose artifact-check --spec pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit --strict` and `pose surface-check --spec pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit --strict`; declare each `passed` only after running it (evidence `command:\\u003cthe command\\u003e`, rationale quoting its result). The surface-check disposition must cite both an `integration:` and a `reachability:` sealed evidence id. Cite sealed `unit:`/`integration:` ids for criteria, never `SD-…` structural facts or requirement ids. Send each shell command alone in its own call (no pipes, `;`, `\\u0026\\u0026`, redirects). `validate` of a component with registered checks is `passed` with the sealed run's evidence; `review-check` and `closeout-check` are `deferred`. New findings have bare ids (F1, F2 …); follow-ups carry `action`, `owner`, `review_by`; only low-severity risks may be accepted.\\n\\nRound 17. Account in `prior_findings` exactly for the findings the brief lists as open for this scope (your round-16 run rrn-9f528bb5bec8a10b: R15-N50 … R15-N53, plus any earlier partial the brief shows), each with whether it stands. Since round 16 the association reader is no longer a hand-written extractor: by decision D3 and ADR governance-association-links-are-read-with-a-commonmark-parser it takes link and image destinations from the syntax tree of the CommonMark parser goldmark v1.8.4 (references, block quotes, multi-line and escaped labels, angle-bracket destinations, code and comments as CommonMark reads them), decodes each destination in POSE in one CommonMark-precedence pass (backslash escapes and character references, then fragment and query, then percent escapes), and leaves the answer unknown for raw HTML carrying `href`/`src` and for an undecodable escape. Judge the dependency choice with the ADR (licence, transitive dependencies, `govulncheck`). A link inside code or a comment is no longer an association, so F6 is done. Classify accordingly: a Markdown form in which a real association is silently dropped and an exemption follows is a blocker; a divergence from CommonMark that only makes the reader require review or report unknown is a follow-up. Dispose the `validate` tools from the sealed evidence: the pipeline ran `pose validate --strict` on a clean clone of the sealed commit with a GitHub token (`.pose/results/delivery-validation.json`); a rerun in your sandbox fails for environment reasons and is not evidence about the code. A finding object accepts exactly `id`, `severity`, `disposition`, `file`, `line`, `summary`, and for an accepted follow-up `action`, `owner`, `review_by`; put any rationale inside `summary`. Do NOT run `pose assess`, `pose state`, `pose index` or anything else that writes under `.pose/`; dispose assess-* tools from the sealed evidence and the code. Leave the worktree as you found it. Sweep the whole surface again and report every remaining finding in one pass, classified blocker vs follow-up; a remote variant of a threat the ADR does not promise to defend is a follow-up, and so is a pre-existing gap of the federation or transfer engine that this spec did not introduce and does not claim to close.\\n\",\n.pose/review-runs/rrn-93914466c27974f9.json:106:  \"output\": \"decision: approved\\n\\nNo blockers found. All six previous findings are addressed. One low-severity follow-up remains: HTML comments containing `href=` or `src=` can unnecessarily block an exemption.\\n\\nFocused tests, the CLI publication race test, `go vet`, artifact-check, and surface-check passed. Artifact-check reported 920 warnings and zero errors; surface-check reported zero findings. Full validation uses the sealed 213/213 passing run. `govulncheck` was unavailable locally, so I did not independently repeat its recorded scan.\\n\\nApplied the review workflow and Go, security, documentation, delivery-evidence, and knowledge-governance rules. The worktree remains unchanged; no attestation was recorded.\\n\\n```pose-draft\\n{\\n  \\\"schema\\\": \\\"pose.review.draft/v1\\\",\\n  \\\"decision\\\": \\\"approved\\\",\\n  \\\"findings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"N54\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"low\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"follow-up\\\",\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_adr_associations.go\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": 87,\\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"The HTML fallback also examines CommonMark comments. For example, \\u003c!-- example: \\u003ca href=\\\\\\\"../adr/decision.md\\\\\\\"\\u003ex\\u003c/a\\u003e --\\u003e becomes a goldmark HTMLBlockType2, whose complete text reaches htmlLink at line 96; href= therefore produces an unknown association. Inline comments take the analogous RawHTML path. A comment in any inventoried ADR can consequently block an otherwise valid when-justified exemption. This is conservative over-enforcement, not an exemption bypass. Source evidence: the AST dispatch at lines 80-96, the attribute expression at line 109, and goldmark parser/html_block.go's comment classification.\\\",\\n      \\\"action\\\": \\\"Exclude CommonMark comment nodes from the HTML attribute fallback and add inline/block comment regressions in both association directions while retaining unknown for actual raw HTML links.\\\",\\n      \\\"owner\\\": \\\"@pose-maintainers\\\",\\n      \\\"review_by\\\": \\\"2026-12-13\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"prior_findings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R14-N48\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"closeout_adr_associations.go:51-60 decodes Markdown destinations before namespace/extension checks; lines 115-136 implement one-pass escape/entity precedence. Independently ran go test ./internal/pose ./internal/cli ./internal/mcpserver -run TestCloseoutReviewPolicy -count=1 successfully, including RoundFifteen and RoundSixteen.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R14-N49\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"closeout_adr_associations.go:49 and 75-79 use parsed Link/Image destinations rather than extracting examples from code; balanced parentheses are parsed whole. The independently passing policy suite includes RoundTwelve and RoundFourteen regressions. The narrower HTML-comment fallback residual is reported separately as N54.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R15-N50\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"closeout_adr_associations.go:49 and 75-79 consume goldmark's resolved AST links. TestCloseoutReviewPolicyRoundSixteen covers forward/backward multiline labels, reference definitions in blockquotes and escaped-bracket labels; it passed in the independently executed policy suite.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R15-N51\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"closeout_adr_associations.go:49 and 77 obtain the complete parsed destination before decoding. RoundSixteen's forward/backward escaped-angle-bracket cases passed in the independently executed policy suite.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R15-N52\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"closeout_adr_associations.go:119-129 consumes an escaped ampersand before considering character references and never decodes it a second time. RoundSixteen's escaped-ampersand regression passed in the independently executed policy suite.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R15-N53\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"AST Link/Image collection at closeout_adr_associations.go:75-79 replaces the old code/comment extractor and truncated-parenthesis behavior. RoundTwelve, RoundFourteen and RoundSixteen passed in the independently executed policy suite. N54 records the narrower remaining HTML-comment over-enforcement.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"sweep\\\": \\\"Reviewed the sealed range and R1-R7/D1-D3; policy parsing, adoption/setup/install/update and schema preservation; canonical members and transfer handling; metadata and CommonMark associations in both directions; required/optional review, veto, mandatory-human and protected baseline precedence; immutable receipts, publication locking, interrupted-close recovery and historical closure; CLI close, closeout-check/state, review-check, review verify, review-plan, attention/obligations, reached, nextCloses, roadmap-check member/cut acceptance, MCP projections, federated acceptance, dependency readiness, portfolio and doctor. Examined schemas, templates, English/Portuguese scaffold parity, dependency licence/module metadata and bounded-read capacity decision. Independently executed the complete TestCloseoutReviewPolicy prefix across domain/CLI/MCP, the CLI publication race regression, go vet, diff hygiene, required artifact/surface commands and final clean-worktree check. The race invocation reported no matching domain test, so race evidence is limited to the CLI publication test. Full validation relies on the sealed 213/213 run. No edits or attestation were made.\\\",\\n  \\\"criteria\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assumption-integrity\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Distinguished verified thresholds, canonical resolution and fail-closed diagnostics from recorded historical validation claims. Prior-policy comparison remains explicitly unknown without a snapshot. N54 accepts only conservative over-enforcement. Local govulncheck was unavailable; no fresh vulnerability-scan claim is made.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-concurrency\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/writer-coordination-and-atomic-publication-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Inspected writer guards, protected publication rechecks, ExpectAbsent receipts and intent-before-status ordering. Independently reran the CLI publication regression under the race detector successfully.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-contracts\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Schema 5 explicitly fences older engines; schemas 1-4 retain legacy behavior. Reviewed additive projections, receipt/plan schemas and CLI/MCP parity.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-input-errors\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Checked invalid policy pairs, duplicates, unsupported enums, member/association failures, containment and inventory limits. Unknown inputs and corrupt receipts refuse closure.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-integration-impact\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Traced CLI/MCP consumers, dependency readiness, portfolio, doctor and federation to the shared decision or terminal projection; producer authority governs federated exemptions.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-observability\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/typed-diagnostics-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Decisions expose policy, reason, counts and resolution diagnostics. Incomplete publication and invalid receipts provide remediation; doctor discloses unknown historical comparisons.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"compatibility\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/install-and-upgrade-journeys-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Reviewed explicit adoption, update preservation, schema-5 retention by other capability toggles, old-engine refusal and verification of pre-adoption sealed scopes without fabricated receipts.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"correctness\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N54\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"design-causality\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-7ae84774f012464a\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The shared deterministic evaluator implements the selected cost/benefit thresholds; receipts separate review eligibility from explicit closure. Goldmark addresses repeated grammar-driven silent drops. The bounded-read capacity amendment supports the existing governance operations without changing their fail-closed limits.\\\",\\n      \\\"mappings\\\": [\\n        {\\n          \\\"delta\\\": \\\"SD-04999039\\\",\\n          \\\"basis\\\": \\\"D3\\\",\\n          \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"mapped\\\",\\n          \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Goldmark replaces the hand-written CommonMark approximation that repeatedly lost real associations. Cached module metadata confirms MIT licensing and no transitive module requirements.\\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"delta\\\": \\\"SD-3ce6ee69\\\",\\n          \\\"basis\\\": \\\"D2\\\",\\n          \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"mapped\\\",\\n          \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The existing read-view ADR records the measured capacity adjustment needed by governance operations supporting the receipt/evaluator design; capture and audit retain a common bounded budget. Its memory cost and later optimization are documented.\\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"delta\\\": \\\"SD-c74440ab\\\",\\n          \\\"basis\\\": \\\"D2\\\",\\n          \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"mapped\\\",\\n          \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The roadmap template exposes the selected flat adrs association contract with an explicit empty list.\\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"delta\\\": \\\"SD-e01b22c0\\\",\\n          \\\"basis\\\": \\\"D3\\\",\\n          \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"mapped\\\",\\n          \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The parser ADR records grammar coverage, decoding precedence, conservative HTML handling and dependency trade-offs.\\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"delta\\\": \\\"SD-ec2d86f4\\\",\\n          \\\"basis\\\": \\\"D1\\\",\\n          \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"mapped\\\",\\n          \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The policy ADR defines the three modes, thresholds, explicit close, prospective adoption, historical compatibility and veto protections required by R1-R7.\\\"\\n        }\\n      ]\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"documentation\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N54\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"operability\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Reviewed preview/setup settings, doctor explanations, explicit-close next actions and recovery instructions. Receipt corruption is actionable and cannot be cleared by overwriting; N54 is a bounded conservative residual.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"requirements\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N54\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"scope\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The implementation covers R1-R7 and the approved D1-D3 choices. It reuses adopt/setup and existing authority machinery, introduces no MCP configuration writer, and does not adopt policy in this instance.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"security\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Inspected path containment, regular-file checks, bounded association inventory, canonical authority, recorded-review veto, baseline protection and immutable publication. The cheapest attempted bypass is a never exemption despite negative or unknown evidence; the policy Protection/Veto/Unavailable and round regressions exercise those refusals. The generic adversarial corpus is supplemental, not claimed as a dedicated case for this gate. Confirmed goldmark licence and dependency metadata locally; its recorded vulnerability scan was not independently repeated because govulncheck is unavailable.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"solution-proportionality\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-7ae84774f012464a\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Compared the selected design with two booleans, agent judgment and continued regex repair. Three enums and one shared evaluator are sufficient for the approved middle mode; receipts are necessary because milestone close previously persisted no transition. A pure-Go CommonMark parser addresses the demonstrated repeated failures without adding rendering or global backlink search. Reconsider if remote backlink discovery or a different Markdown dialect becomes a requirement; N54 remains conservative follow-up work.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"tools\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"artifact-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit --strict\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Executed successfully, exit 0: artifact.claims=49, artifact.observed=208, artifact.findings=920. A second JSON invocation confirmed zero error findings and 920 warnings. The default output includes recorded historical change sets, so these counts are not the sealed range's file count. An additional explicit-range diagnostic failed with git diff signal: broken pipe; it is not counted as passing evidence.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-design\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-7ae84774f012464a\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Did not rerun a writing assessment in the sealed checkout. Examined the sealed structural result, implementation, D1-D3 and their ADRs directly.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-discover\\\",\\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:pose context --task spec:pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit --json\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Discovery writes assessment artifacts and was excluded by the review boundary. Confirmed local authority and sealed revision through the read-only context command and inspected the component directly.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-integrate\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Avoided assessment writes. Used sealed integration evidence, independently reran the policy integration prefix across domain/CLI/MCP and traced provider/consumer paths.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-tech-debt\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Avoided assessment writes. Inspected changed code and spec follow-ups and searched the new closeout files for TODO, FIXME, stub and panic markers; no new unresolved implementation marker was established.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"closeout-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:pose context --task spec:pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit --json\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Completion check depends on the review conclusion being recorded by POSE; this independent run must not record an attestation.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"review-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:pose context --task spec:pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit --json\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The review's own completion check cannot pass before POSE records its conclusion.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"suggest-review\\\",\\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Executed successfully; selected the review workflow and security, documentation-style and backend-go rules.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"surface-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Executed pose surface-check --spec pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit --strict, exit 0: surface.targets=1, surface.results=213, surface.findings=0. Composition is supported by integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration and reachability:pose-mcp/go/closeout-plan-reachability.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"validate\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Disposed from the sealed strict pipeline run as directed. delivery-validation.json records 213 executed, 213 passed, zero failed/errored/skipped; the sealed evidence includes build, unit, integration and e2e results. Did not rerun the writing full-validation workflow.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"validate\\\",\\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Used the component's sealed passing validation results, including build:pose-mcp/go/build and unit:pose-mcp/go/test. Independently reran all TestCloseoutReviewPolicy tests across domain/CLI/MCP, the CLI publication race regression and go vet successfully.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\\n```\",\n.pose/review-bundles/rvb-6600abdbead9518a.json:452:          \"rationale\": \"observe bounded structural deltas on the canonical review subject\",\n.pose/review-bundles/rvb-6600abdbead9518a.json:982:      \"structural-causality\"\n.pose/review-runs/rrn-fa6a6e8e1df0a0ba.json:86:  \"brief_notes\": \"Implementer notes (Claude Opus 5.5, the lead). Use them as context only; the judgment is yours.\\n\\nScope: spec `pose-review-readiness-before-seal` (R1–R6, decisions D1–D2, ADR `2026-11-23-review-readiness-before-seal` with residual limits L1–L2). It moves refusals that used to arrive after a full review round to the earliest point that has their inputs:\\n- R1/R2: a new seal of a spec bundle refuses the `undeclared-delivery` finding at error severity in the delivery index, and, when the plan has structural facts, a decision or assumption that reaches no requirement or constraint (`pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_seal_readiness.go`, called from `sealReviewBundle`).\\n- R3: `pose review draft-check` (`internal/cli/review_draft_check.go`, `internal/pose/review_draft_check.go`). The content part of the bundle-attestation validation was extracted unchanged into `attestationContentBlockers`, which both the conclusion preflight and the draft check call. The dispatch writes the bundle and the round's open findings to the run's private temporary directory and names it in `POSE_REVIEW_DRAFT_CONTEXT`.\\n- R4: brief template `review-brief/8` (the `/7` text and its golden digest are unchanged).\\n- R5/R6: `pose delegate` names an oversized note; a completed run nothing concluded prints its `pose review conclude` command.\\nEach requirement has a regression test that failed with its fix mutated out. The full `go test ./...` of `pose-mcp` passed.\\n\\nPlease check in particular that the extraction of `attestationContentBlockers` changed no behaviour of `validateBundleAttestationWith`, that the draft check cannot accept a draft the conclusion refuses for content, and that the seal refusal cannot block a bundle already sealed.\\n\\nThis brief is review-brief/8, so its last step asks you to run `pose review draft-check --draft -` on your own draft. Please do: it is also a live test of R3.\\n\\nDraft format rules, enforced by the conclusion preflight:\\n- New findings use short unprefixed IDs (N1, N2, …). Round-prefixed IDs go only in `prior_findings`, and only for the findings the brief lists under \\\"Findings to account for\\\" (none in round 1), with exactly id, status and evidence.\\n- Structural-delta mappings go inside the criterion that answers them, with `basis` set to a requirement or a decision of this spec (R1–R6, D1, D2).\\n- A criterion scoped to a component cites evidence from that component only.\\n\\nSandbox limits: the checkout is sealed and read-only. Never run `pose assess` or any other command that writes inside it: a run that changes the sealed checkout fails. Never `cd`; keep the checkout root as the working directory. If building or a scratch copy is not possible, run the focused Go tests (`go test ./internal/pose ./internal/cli -run 'DraftCheck|SealReadiness|SealRefuses|DelegateNamesTheNoteLimit|Brief|SealedGate|OnlyTheSigning'`, `go vet`) and cite the sealed canonical result for the rest, stating the limit. A tool you cannot rerun in the sandbox is a limit of the run, not a defect of the subject: cite the sealed evidence that covers it, then decide on the code itself.\\n\",\n.pose/review-runs/rrn-fa6a6e8e1df0a0ba.json:106:  \"output\": \"decision: changes-requested\\n\\nThree medium-severity blockers: R2’s seal gate applies beyond its specified scope, R3’s run-ID input is missing, and an undeclared artifact blocks delivery verification.\\n\\nApplied the review workflow and security, backend-go, and documentation-style rules. Focused regression tests and vet passed. The broader Go test attempt exited 1; no full-suite pass is claimed.\\n\\nFinal draft validation remains unavailable: the installed binary lacks `draft-check`, the temporary source-built binary was cleaned up, and rebuilding was refused by the read-only filesystem. No repository changes or attestation were made.\\n\\nBundle: `rvb-0268e39f3711f7f3`. Plan: `sha256:3cfbd69688cfec3b0d559efebb47a313e9d6911bc210eafbbfc4f10ad7960edb`.\\n\\n```pose-draft\\n{\\n  \\\"schema\\\": \\\"pose.review.draft/v1\\\",\\n  \\\"decision\\\": \\\"changes-requested\\\",\\n  \\\"findings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"N1\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"medium\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"blocker\\\",\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_seal_readiness.go\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": 35,\\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"R2 applies only when the plan asks for structural mappings, but this condition checks only for material structural facts. Review-plan resolution observes structure before selecting overlays, so a nonmatching structural selector can leave material facts without a required mapping criterion. Such scopes are now refused for unbased decisions although reviewStructuralCausalityBlockers returns immediately without mapping owners. Gate readiness on a required RequiresStructuralMapping criterion. TestSealReadinessRefusesADecisionWithoutBasis demonstrates the overreach by expecting blockers from a bundle with no criteria.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"N2\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"medium\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"blocker\\\",\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_draft_check.go\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": 64,\\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"R3 requires draft-check \\u003crun|bundle\\u003e, but every positional argument is passed as a bundle ID to LoadReviewBundle, which accepts only rvb-* IDs. Run IDs therefore always fail before draft validation and cannot select their recorded bundle and round. Resolve run references explicitly and test that invocation. The source-built binary reproduced the bundle-ID rejection for draft-check run-fixture --draft -.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"N3\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"medium\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"blocker\\\",\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\".pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-readiness-before-seal.md\\\",\\n      \\\"line\\\": 67,\\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"The artifact declarations omit modified pose-mcp/internal/pose/live_policy_reads_test.go. The independent strict surface check reports error undeclared for that path, and the committed delivery-integrity index contains the same scope-specific error. Declare its modified action and reconcile the attributed changes before closeout.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"criteria\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assumption-integrity\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-179046b00fd968e0\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Examined D1/D2 and ADR limits L1/L2. Dispatch context is advisory; conclusion revalidates authority. A stale delivery index remains a documented detection limitation. Focused tests and vet were independently rerun; canonical validation remains sealed evidence.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-concurrency\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/writer-coordination-and-atomic-publication-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Inspected context publication before process start and the existing temporary-directory lifecycle. No new shared mutable state or goroutines were introduced.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-contracts\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N2\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-input-errors\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Focused DraftCheck, SealReadiness, SealRefuses and note-limit tests passed. Inspected parser errors, context schema checks and actionable readiness diagnostics.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-integration-impact\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-review-capability-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Inspected CLI routing, dispatch context and shared attestation-content extraction. Focused context and conclusion-comparison regressions passed.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-observability\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-output-redaction-diagnostics-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Returned errors retain rule, path and remediation. Note errors name size and limit; conclusion hints identify the run. Existing output containment remains intact.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"compatibility\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N1\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"correctness\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N1\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"design-causality\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N1\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"D1 shares parsing, round accounting and content validation. D2 separates pre-review readiness from final authority checks, but N1 violates its conditional scope.\\\",\\n      \\\"mappings\\\": [\\n        {\\n          \\\"delta\\\": \\\"SD-0bfbfab6\\\",\\n          \\\"basis\\\": \\\"D1\\\",\\n          \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"mapped\\\",\\n          \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The ADR records R3/R4's shared validation and private dispatch context, together with D2's seal timing and residual limits.\\\"\\n        }\\n      ]\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"documentation\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-brief-templates-are-immutable-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Reviewed manual and scaffold changes in both locales, /8 rendering and preservation of /7 text and digest. Documentation describes the implemented bundle/context command; N2 separately identifies the missing spec-required run form.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"operability\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N3\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"requirements\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N2\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"R1 and R4-R6 have exercised regressions. R2 is overbroad under N1, R3 omits run-ID input under N2, and artifact reconciliation remains blocked under N3.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"scope\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N3\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Implementation stays within the planned component, but artifact declarations omit a changed test and readiness enforcement exceeds R2's stated precondition.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"security\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-adapter-containment-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Examined private 0600 context publication, adapter confinement and final authority checks. Editing advisory context cannot authorize an attestation. No new credential exposure or authority bypass was found.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"solution-proportionality\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-179046b00fd968e0\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Extracting existing validation and passing a private snapshot is a small sufficient solution for a sealed checkout. Signature and identity checks remain deferred. Mutable authoritative context would invalidate this choice. Editing advisory context or supplying an arbitrary valid Basis are cheap formal shortcuts: conclusion revalidation protects authority, while substantive causality remains reviewer judgment. No dedicated readiness case exists in the adversarial corpus; focused refusal tests provide narrower coverage.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"tools\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"artifact-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"failed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-review-readiness-before-seal --strict\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Executed. Reconciliation identifies undeclared live_policy_reads_test.go, independently corroborated by the committed delivery-integrity finding N3.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-design\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Assessment writers were excluded from the sealed checkout. Inspected sealed structure evidence and mapped the governance delta.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-discover\\\",\\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Avoided assessment publication into the sealed checkout; inspected component source and regressions directly.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-integrate\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Assessment writers were excluded. Inspected CLI, dispatch and conclusion boundaries and sealed integration evidence.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-tech-debt\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Assessment writers were excluded. Direct searches of the new readiness and draft-check files found no TODO, FIXME, stub or panic markers.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"closeout-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Requires completion and recording of this review; the reviewer recorded no attestation.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"review-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Requires completion and recording of this review; the reviewer recorded no attestation.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"suggest-review\\\",\\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Executed; applied security, documentation-style and backend-go rules.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"surface-check\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"failed\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/spec-surface-integration\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Inspected sealed evidence. Independently executed pose surface-check --spec pose-review-readiness-before-seal --strict, which reported the undeclared artifact in N3.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"validate\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Full pose validate was not rerun because registered checks can write in the sealed checkout. Used sealed canonical evidence and independently reran focused tests and vet. The broader go test ./... attempt exited 1; CLI tests passed in 203.813s, but no full-suite pass is claimed.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"validate\\\",\\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"not-used\\\",\\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Read-only validation limitation. Focused go -C pose-mcp test ./internal/pose ./internal/cli -run 'DraftCheck|SealReadiness|SealRefuses|DelegateNamesTheNoteLimit|Brief|SealedGate|OnlyTheSigning' and go -C pose-mcp vet ./internal/pose ./internal/cli passed. unit:pose-mcp/go/test remains sealed canonical evidence.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\\n```\",\n.pose/review-runs/rrn-5ed84b0f66cce29b.json:86:  \"brief_notes\": \"Implementer notes (Claude Opus 5.5, the lead in this session). Use them as context only; the judgment is yours.\\n\\n- The feature was motivated by the Harne8 batch of 2026-11-22. There, every review round re-ran a 72-check matrix of about 35 minutes, and intermittent suites failed roughly one run in three.\\n- In this repository `pose-mcp` holds 233 of the 236 checks and is high criticality, so `--carry` saves little here. The dogfood record at c4182727 carried five of six modules with zero changed files.\\n- Please challenge the soundness argument of D1 in particular. A carried result is bound to the material computed at HEAD, and that is only safe when the selection guarantees the carried module's inputs did not change.\\n- Please also check the derived-record exclusion (`carryExclusions` with `posemodel.IsAdministrativePath`) and the engine identity, which is the version plus the VCS revision.\\n- Report every finding you see in this round, each classified as blocker or follow-up.\\n\\nRound 2 notes:\\n- F1 from round 1 (rrn-0dd98c4aab8b5918) is addressed in d601fbe1. The record now has `material_clean`, set when the working copy matched HEAD at the start and at the end of the run. `planCarry` refuses a base without it, or with any unavailable material binding. `TestCarryRefusesABaseThatValidatedADirtyWorkingCopy` reproduces your sequence: a pass over an uncommitted fix, a commit of the record alone, the restored failing file, then `--carry`. The test failed with the check mutated out. Account for F1 in prior_findings.\\n- Round 1 also changed files in the sealed worktree because `pose assess integrate` and `pose assess tech-debt` persist their outputs: `.pose/assessments/*`, `.pose/state/*`. Run every `assess` command on a copy in the operation's scratch, never in the sealed checkout, and keep the Bash working directory at the checkout root. Example: `scratch=$(mktemp -d \\\"$TMPDIR/pose-assess.XXXXXX\\\")`, `git archive HEAD | tar -x -C \\\"$scratch\\\"`, `sh -c 'cd \\\"$1\\\" \\u0026\\u0026 exec \\\"$2\\\" assess integrate --json' sh \\\"$scratch\\\" \\\"$(command -v pose)\\\"`.\\n- The `artifact-check` head differs from the bundle subject because the index commits also carry this spec's trailer. `artifact-check` resolves the change set range to the last trailer commit, which is an index-only commit. The bundle subject skips commits that only touch derived records, whose material digest is unchanged. That is existing engine behaviour, which the lead will take up separately. Judge it as you see fit.\\n- The full matrix takes about 13 minutes. If you cannot complete it in the sandbox, cite the sealed canonical result for the `validate` tool and state your own run's limits.\\n\\nRound 3 notes: round 2 (rrn-1c033e4c349d7794) found N1–N4. 2077731b fixes them:\\n- The changed set uses `git diff -z --no-renames` and `ls-files -z`, so a rename names both sides and a quoted name keeps its owner.\\n- The root module `.` is never exempt from root files.\\n- A build with `vcs.modified=true` is not a verifiable identity: it never carries, and a base with a `.dirty` identity is refused.\\n\\nThe regression tests are `TestCarrySelectsBothSidesOfARename`, `TestCarryKeepsTheOwnerOfAQuotedName`, `TestCarryRootModuleOwnsRootFiles` and `TestEngineIdentityRefusesModifiedBuilds`. Each one failed with its fix mutated out. Account for R2-N1..R2-N4 in prior_findings.\\n\\nRound 4 notes: round 3 (rrn-3461f6ff36909419) found N5 and N6.\\n- N5: a declared `dependsOn` path now owns its files even when the dependency is no longer discovered (`underDeclaredDependency`).\\n- N6: module metadata that does not decode is now an error. It means a full run under `--carry` and exit 2 under `--changed-from`.\\nThe regression tests are `TestCarryDeletedDependencySelectsItsDependents` and `TestCarryRejectsUndecodableMetadata`. Both failed with their fix mutated out. Account for R3-N5 and R3-N6 in prior_findings.\\n\\nPlease make this round an exhaustive sweep and report every remaining issue in it, each classified as blocker or follow-up, so the scope can converge. Cover at least:\\n- gitlinks and submodules;\\n- symlinks;\\n- paths that differ only by case;\\n- `moduleOverrides` modules that have no manifest;\\n- nested modules;\\n- a module whose matrix checks or stack change while the matrix digest does not;\\n- criticality and policy widening;\\n- chained carries over many bases;\\n- concurrent runs writing the canonical file.\\n- The lead's own sweep before this round found a gitlink case: a changed gitlink above a declared dependency selected nothing under it. A changed path now selects the modules and dependencies under it, tested by `TestChangedScopeGitlinkAboveADependencySelectsItsDependents`.\\n\\nRound 5 notes: round 4 (rrn-4b28f2ff95acf9c4) found N7–N10. The selection in `computeChangedScope` was rewritten instead of patched. Each changed file now independently selects:\\n- its most specific owner;\\n- every module beneath it;\\n- every module whose declared dependency contains it, lies beneath it or is the root `.`, when that dependency is not a discovered module, which the transitive widening covers;\\n- for a file no module owns, the root module and every module that is not self-contained.\\n\\n`planCarry` refuses when any module is reached through a symlink. `material_clean` now also requires the HEAD at the end of the run to equal the recorded head. The regression tests are `TestCarryDeletedNestedDependencySelectsItsDependents`, `TestCarryRootDependencyIsChangedByRootFiles`, `TestCarryRefusesModulesReachedThroughASymlink` and `TestValidateHeadMovingDuringTheRunIsNotClean`. Each failed with its fix mutated out. Account for R4-N7..R4-N10 in prior_findings, and again report every remaining issue in this round.\\n\\nRound 6 notes: round 5 (rrn-b07ee93779a65e40) found N11–N14.\\n- N11: every eligible dependency now counts (`declaredDependencyHits`).\\n- N12: a run whose HEAD moved, or that is otherwise not `material_clean`, records every material binding as unavailable.\\n- N13: `aliasedModule` also refuses modules that share a physical directory (`os.SameFile`).\\n- N14: the head is pinned before planning, and `planCarry`, the selection and the exclusions use that SHA.\\nThe regression tests are `TestChangedScopeEvaluatesEveryDeclaredDependency`, `TestValidateHeadMovingDuringTheRunBindsNoMaterial`, `TestCarryRefusesModulesSharingADirectory` and `TestCarryPlansAgainstThePinnedHead`. Each failed with its fix mutated out. Account for R5-N11..R5-N14 and the remaining partials R3-N9/R3-N10 in prior_findings, and report every remaining issue in this round.\\n\\nRound 7 notes: round 6 (rrn-88e0428bda9bc9c7) found N15 and N16.\\n- N15: a declared dependency now selects its consumer whenever a changed file intersects it, discovered or not, unless it is the file's own owner, which the transitive widening covers.\\n- N16: `planCarry` refuses when a declared dependency path is reached through a symlink.\\nThe regression tests are `TestChangedScopeDiscoveredAncestorDependencySelectsItsDependents`, which covers a parent and a discovered root dependency, and `TestCarryRefusesDependenciesReachedThroughASymlink`. Account for R6-N15 and R6-N16, and report every remaining issue in this round.\\n\\nRound 8 notes: round 7 (rrn-85704a129332a685) found N17–N19. Instead of chasing alias forms one path at a time, `planCarry` now applies global rules:\\n- `caseInsensitiveFilesystem` refuses on case-folding filesystems.\\n- `aliasingSymlink` refuses any tracked symlink whose path or target lies in a non-root module or intersects a declared dependency, or whose target leaves the repository. Symlinks between unowned paths, such as `.claude/skills` to `.agents/skills`, stay allowed, since a change on either side already selects the root and every non-self-contained module.\\n- `duplicateCheckID` and a base-id check refuse duplicate check ids.\\nThe tests are `TestCarryRefusesASymlinkInsideAModule`, `TestCarryRefusesASymlinkFromAModuleToAnUnownedPath`, `TestCarryAllowsSymlinksBetweenUnownedPaths`, `TestCarryDetectsACaseInsensitiveFilesystem` and `TestCarryRefusesDuplicateCheckIDs`. Account for R7-N17..R7-N19, and report every rema\n... 1655324 bytes omitted ...\n\n.pose/review-bundles/rvb-104f7a59000220d0.json:464:          \"rationale\": \"observe bounded structural deltas on the canonical review subject\",\n.pose/review-bundles/rvb-104f7a59000220d0.json:1029:      \"structural-causality\"\n.pose/review-bundles/rvb-c99b33799d3b9056.json:346:          \"description\": \"Explain how the selected design addresses the stated requirement and material cause, citing the relevant decision basis and structural observations where available.\",\n.pose/review-bundles/rvb-c99b33799d3b9056.json:455:          \"rationale\": \"observe bounded structural deltas on the canonical review subject\",\n.pose/review-bundles/rvb-c99b33799d3b9056.json:2124:      \"structural-causality\"\n.pose/review-bundles/rvb-44eb48e28d52f466.json:3111:      \"structural-causality\"\n.pose/review-bundles/rvb-552ff460f389edbb.json:338:          \"rationale\": \"observe bounded structural deltas on the canonical review subject\",\n.pose/review-bundles/rvb-552ff460f389edbb.json:974:      \"structural-causality\"\n.pose/review-bundles/rvb-84f1b7779fb959da.json:2996:            \"structural-materiality@1\"\n.pose/review-bundles/rvb-84f1b7779fb959da.json:3117:          \"description\": \"Explain how the selected design addresses the stated requirement and material cause, citing the relevant decision basis and structural observations where available.\",\n.pose/review-bundles/rvb-84f1b7779fb959da.json:3120:          \"requires_structural_mapping\": true,\n.pose/review-bundles/rvb-84f1b7779fb959da.json:3124:            \"structural-materiality@1\"\n.pose/review-bundles/rvb-84f1b7779fb959da.json:3203:            \"structural-materiality@1\"\n.pose/review-bundles/rvb-84f1b7779fb959da.json:3238:          \"rationale\": \"observe bounded structural deltas on the canonical review subject\",\n.pose/review-bundles/rvb-84f1b7779fb959da.json:3517:          \"ref\": \"structural-materiality@1\",\n.pose/review-bundles/rvb-84f1b7779fb959da.json:3520:          \"source\": \".pose/review-profiles/structural-materiality.json\",\n.pose/review-bundles/rvb-84f1b7779fb959da.json:5616:      \"structural-causality\"\n.pose/review-bundles/rvb-84f1b7779fb959d