{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_61","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n -i 'TODO|FIXME|stub|panic\\\\(' pose-mcp/internal/cli/assess.go pose-mcp/internal/cli/assess_sealed_test.go pose-mcp/internal/pose/assessment_sealed.go pose-mcp/internal/pose/assessment_sealed_test.go pose-mcp/internal/pose/discovery.go pose-mcp/internal/pose/integration.go pose-mcp/internal/pose/techdebt.go pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_plan.go pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief.go pose-mcp/internal/cli/help_catalog.go\"","aggregated_output":"pose-mcp/internal/cli/help_catalog.go:119:\t\tSummaryPtBR:     \"Executa a matriz determinística de validação em todos os módulos\",\npose-mcp/internal/cli/help_catalog.go:149:\t\tDescriptionPtBR: \"Realiza verificação estrutural completa em todos os arquivos do POSE, links quebrados em markdown, sintaxe de frontmatter, schemas JSON e grafos de specs.\",\npose-mcp/internal/cli/help_catalog.go:190:\t\tSummaryPtBR:     \"Lista, filtra e descobre especificações em todo o repositório\",\npose-mcp/internal/cli/help_catalog.go:328:\t\tDescriptionPtBR: \"pose review governa o sujeito (bundle, brief, atestação, verify); pose delegate governa as execuções. Termos: um agente é um perfil de CLI configurado em .pose/policy/delegation.json; um run é uma execução; uma tentativa é um run e suas continuações; uma thread são as rodadas de um escopo. review, adjudicate e smoke rodam o brief gerado do bundle selado num worktree descartável no commit selado, só com acesso de leitura, sob o ledger de tentativas e a contenção. Com delegated-review adotado e conclusions.issuer configurado, o motor registra automaticamente a conclusão completa e verificada; processo concluído sozinho nunca aprova. Sem --agent (ou com auto) o roteamento escolhe um agente do propósito: o vendor oposto ao da implementação que o bundle selou (routing.prefer), depois routing.on_unavailable (outro modelo do mesmo vendor, esperar um reset conhecido dentro de routing.max_wait, o mesmo modelo); --agent <nome> dispensa o roteamento e avisa quando o agente é do vendor da implementação. Todo run registra a decisão de roteamento e a independência alcançada. O processo filho não recebe nenhuma variável de sessão do agente pai. --dry-run mostra agente, propósito, acesso, diretório de trabalho e argv resolvidos e não reserva nada; --json imprime um documento versionado. Uma referência de run é um id de run, um id de tentativa, um --label ou um prefixo de sessão com seis caracteres ou mais. --detach inicia o run numa sessão própria e devolve a tentativa na hora; wait bloqueia até um run terminar e sai com 0 aprovado, 10 mudanças pedidas ou rejeitado, 20 falhou, 30 interrompido, 40 travado, 50 tempo esgotado. watch acompanha um run ao vivo, reproduzindo uma tentativa retomada como uma tarefa só, e escolhe um run com fzf ou um menu num terminal; on_terminal roda um comando uma vez depois que um run termina. handoff continua um run parado com outro agente na mesma tentativa; task entrega uma tarefa geral a outro agente, nunca como evidência; wait sai com 0 quando o agente teve sucesso. pose review dispatch, resume e status foram removidos. As mensagens seguem POSE_LOCALE.\",\npose-mcp/internal/cli/help_catalog.go:386:\t\t\t{\"draft-check\", \"pose review draft-check [<bundle-id|run-id>] --draft <file> [--json]\", \"Report every reason the conclusion step would refuse a review draft, without writing; inside a delegated review the bundle and round come from the run\", \"Relata todo motivo pelo qual a conclusão recusaria um rascunho de review, sem gravar; dentro de uma review delegada o bundle e a rodada vêm do run\"},\npose-mcp/internal/cli/help_catalog.go:577:\t\t\t{\"list\", \"pose contribute list [--json]\", \"List all staged contributions awaiting developer adjudication\", \"Lista todos os rascunhos locais aguardando avaliação do desenvolvedor\"},\npose-mcp/internal/cli/help_catalog.go:633:\t\tDescriptionPtBR: \"Agrega todos os follow-ups declarados nas specs na seção 7 (Final Report), sinalizando SLAs vencidos e propostas quase-duplicadas.\",\npose-mcp/internal/cli/help_catalog.go:636:\t\t\t{\"--all\", \"List all follow-ups across all specs regardless of disposition\", \"Lista todos os follow-ups em todas as specs independentemente da disposição\"},\npose-mcp/internal/cli/help_catalog.go:651:\t\tDescriptionPtBR: \"Recalcula e grava todos os índices estáticos incluindo spec-graph.json, roadmaps.json, releases.json e delivery-integrity.json, como uma geração confirmada por .pose/indexes/generation.json.\",\npose-mcp/internal/cli/help_catalog.go:725:\t\t\t{\"tech-debt\", \"pose assess tech-debt [--update-state] [--no-persist]\", \"Scan codebase for technical debt markers and uncovered stubs\", \"Escaneia a base de código por marcadores de débito e stubs\"},\npose-mcp/internal/cli/help_catalog.go:803:\t\tDescriptionPtBR: \"Verifica se todos os arquivos declarados na seção 3 (Technical Plan -> Artifacts) correspondem ao changeset real do Git atribuído via trailer (POSE-Spec: <slug>).\",\npose-mcp/internal/cli/help_catalog.go:884:\t\t\t{\"--outcomes\", \"Governance: with --waits/--rework, also compute the outcomes (reads the whole history)\", \"Governance: com --waits/--rework, calcula também os resultados (lê todo o histórico)\"},\npose-mcp/internal/cli/help_catalog.go:948:\t\tSummaryPtBR:     \"Verifica se todos os arquivos de log histórico estão rastreados no Git\",\npose-mcp/internal/cli/help_catalog.go:951:\t\tDescriptionPtBR: \"Garante que todos os arquivos históricos de tarefas sob .pose/reports/history/ estejam commitados e rastreados no controle de versão.\",\npose-mcp/internal/pose/techdebt.go:34:\tTODOs                int `json:\"todos\"`\npose-mcp/internal/pose/techdebt.go:35:\tFIXMEs               int `json:\"fixmes\"`\npose-mcp/internal/pose/techdebt.go:38:\tStubs                int `json:\"stubs\"`\npose-mcp/internal/pose/techdebt.go:70:\t// Portuguese \"todo\" and explanatory prose such as \"test stub\" are not debt\npose-mcp/internal/pose/techdebt.go:71:\t// declarations; executable stub constructs remain case-insensitive below.\npose-mcp/internal/pose/techdebt.go:72:\tdebtCommentMarkerRE = regexp.MustCompile(`\\b(TODO|FIXME|HACK|STUB)\\b`)\npose-mcp/internal/pose/techdebt.go:74:\tdebtStubRE          = regexp.MustCompile(`(?i)\\b(?:notimplementederror|notimplementedexception)\\b|\\b(?:unimplemented|todo)\\s*!\\s*\\(`)\npose-mcp/internal/pose/techdebt.go:173:\tif debtStubRE.MatchString(code) && !seen[\"STUB\"] {\npose-mcp/internal/pose/techdebt.go:174:\t\tmarkers = append(markers, \"STUB\")\npose-mcp/internal/pose/techdebt.go:329:// ignored, so a TODO after a 70 000-character line was lost without a word.\npose-mcp/internal/pose/techdebt.go:386:\t\tcase \"TODO\":\npose-mcp/internal/pose/techdebt.go:387:\t\t\tsummary.TODOs++\npose-mcp/internal/pose/techdebt.go:388:\t\tcase \"FIXME\":\npose-mcp/internal/pose/techdebt.go:389:\t\t\tsummary.FIXMEs++\npose-mcp/internal/pose/techdebt.go:394:\t\tcase \"STUB\":\npose-mcp/internal/pose/techdebt.go:395:\t\t\tsummary.Stubs++\npose-mcp/internal/pose/techdebt.go:459:- **TODOs**: %d | **FIXMEs**: %d | **HACKs**: %d | **Panics**: %d | **Stubs**: %d\npose-mcp/internal/pose/techdebt.go:469:\t\treport.Summary.TODOs, report.Summary.FIXMEs, report.Summary.Hacks, report.Summary.Panics,\npose-mcp/internal/pose/techdebt.go:470:\t\treport.Summary.Stubs, report.Summary.CoveredCount, report.Summary.UncoveredCount,\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_plan.go:184:\t\"assess-tech-debt\": {Rationale: \"inspect unresolved TODO, FIXME, panic and stub findings\", Phase: 20},\npose-mcp/internal/cli/assess_sealed_test.go:44:\twriteCloseoutCLIFile(t, root, \"svc/main.go\", \"package main\\n\\n// TODO: a marker\\nfunc main() {}\\n\")\npose-mcp/internal/cli/assess.go:741:\t\tfmt.Fprintf(stdout, \"  - %-30s LOC: %d (prod) / %d (test) | Debt TODOs: %d, FIXMEs: %d\\n\",\npose-mcp/internal/cli/assess.go:742:\t\t\tres.ComponentSlug, res.Metrics.LOCProduction, res.Metrics.LOCTests, res.TechnicalDebt.TODOs, res.TechnicalDebt.FIXMEs)\npose-mcp/internal/cli/assess.go:766:\tvar todos, fixmes, panics, stubs int\npose-mcp/internal/cli/assess.go:800:\t\ttodos += state.TechnicalDebt.TODOs\npose-mcp/internal/cli/assess.go:801:\t\tfixmes += state.TechnicalDebt.FIXMEs\npose-mcp/internal/cli/assess.go:803:\t\tstubs += state.TechnicalDebt.Stubs\npose-mcp/internal/cli/assess.go:832:\t\tfmt.Sprintf(\"- saude_de_codigo: TODOs=%d FIXMEs=%d panics=%d stubs=%d\", todos, fixmes, panics, stubs),\npose-mcp/internal/cli/assess.go:971:\tfmt.Fprintf(stdout, \"  - Total Debt Markers: %d (TODOs: %d, FIXMEs: %d, Panics: %d, Stubs: %d)\\n\",\npose-mcp/internal/cli/assess.go:972:\t\treport.Summary.TotalMarkers, report.Summary.TODOs, report.Summary.FIXMEs, report.Summary.Panics, report.Summary.Stubs)\npose-mcp/internal/pose/discovery.go:160:\tTODOs  int `json:\"todos\"`\npose-mcp/internal/pose/discovery.go:161:\tFIXMEs int `json:\"fixmes\"`\npose-mcp/internal/pose/discovery.go:163:\tStubs  int `json:\"stubs\"`\npose-mcp/internal/pose/discovery.go:511:\t\tstate.TechnicalDebt.TODOs += debt.TODOs\npose-mcp/internal/pose/discovery.go:512:\t\tstate.TechnicalDebt.FIXMEs += debt.FIXMEs\npose-mcp/internal/pose/discovery.go:514:\t\tstate.TechnicalDebt.Stubs += debt.Stubs\npose-mcp/internal/pose/discovery.go:529:\tscore -= float64(state.TechnicalDebt.TODOs) * 0.005\npose-mcp/internal/pose/discovery.go:530:\tscore -= float64(state.TechnicalDebt.FIXMEs) * 0.010\npose-mcp/internal/pose/discovery.go:532:\tscore -= float64(state.TechnicalDebt.Stubs) * 0.015\npose-mcp/internal/pose/discovery.go:617:\t\t\tcase \"TODO\":\npose-mcp/internal/pose/discovery.go:618:\t\t\t\tdebt.TODOs++\npose-mcp/internal/pose/discovery.go:619:\t\t\tcase \"FIXME\", \"HACK\":\npose-mcp/internal/pose/discovery.go:620:\t\t\t\tdebt.FIXMEs++\npose-mcp/internal/pose/discovery.go:623:\t\t\tcase \"STUB\":\npose-mcp/internal/pose/discovery.go:624:\t\t\t\tdebt.Stubs++\npose-mcp/internal/pose/discovery.go:680:> **Saúde de Código**: %d TODOs | %d FIXMEs | %d Panics | %d Stubs\npose-mcp/internal/pose/discovery.go:695:- **TODOs**: %d\npose-mcp/internal/pose/discovery.go:696:- **FIXMEs**: %d\npose-mcp/internal/pose/discovery.go:698:- **Stubs**: %d\npose-mcp/internal/pose/discovery.go:699:`, state.ComponentSlug, state.Path, state.Path, state.DiscoveredAt, state.BaselineCommit, state.Metrics.LOCProduction, state.Metrics.LOCTests, state.Metrics.TotalFiles, langs, state.TechnicalDebt.TODOs, state.TechnicalDebt.FIXMEs, state.TechnicalDebt.Panics, state.TechnicalDebt.Stubs, state.ComponentSlug, state.Path, s.projectLabel(), state.Status, state.CompletenessScore*100, state.TechnicalDebt.TODOs, state.TechnicalDebt.FIXMEs, state.TechnicalDebt.Panics, state.TechnicalDebt.Stubs)\npose-mcp/internal/pose/discovery.go:755:\tvar totalTODOs, totalFIXMEs, totalPanics, totalStubs int\npose-mcp/internal/pose/discovery.go:766:\t\ttotalTODOs += st.TechnicalDebt.TODOs\npose-mcp/internal/pose/discovery.go:767:\t\ttotalFIXMEs += st.TechnicalDebt.FIXMEs\npose-mcp/internal/pose/discovery.go:769:\t\ttotalStubs += st.TechnicalDebt.Stubs\npose-mcp/internal/pose/discovery.go:816:- **Dívidas Técnicas em Aberto**: %d TODOs | %d FIXMEs | %d Panics | %d Stubs\npose-mcp/internal/pose/discovery.go:824:| # | Componente Slug | Caminho do Módulo | Linguagens | LOC Produção | LOC Testes | Arquivos | TODOs | Completude | Status |\npose-mcp/internal/pose/discovery.go:826:`, project, now, commit, len(states), totalProd, totalTests, totalProd+totalTests, totalFiles, platformCompleteness*100, totalTODOs, totalFIXMEs, totalPanics, totalStubs, openSpecsCount, gapsCount)\npose-mcp/internal/pose/discovery.go:834:\t\t\ti+1, st.ComponentSlug, st.Path, langs, st.Metrics.LOCProduction, st.Metrics.LOCTests, st.Metrics.TotalFiles, st.TechnicalDebt.TODOs, st.CompletenessScore*100, st.Status)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_62","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"cat <<'POSE_DRAFT_EOF' | \\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\" review draft-check --draft -\ndecision: approved\n\nThe assessment writers, sealed-checkout guards, `--update-state` paths, planned assessment arguments and review brief instructions were reviewed against R1–R5. No subject defects were found. Focused Go tests and vet passed; full strict validation could not create temporary/build-cache files in this read-only sandbox. No repository changes or attestation were recorded.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"approved\",\n  \"findings\": [],\n  \"prior_findings\": [],\n  \"sweep\": \"Reviewed the 17-path sealed subject, R1-R5, D1-D2 and L1; traced all CLI assessment routes, every Store assessment writer, the sealed path predicate, --update-state gates, reviewToolArgs, review-brief/9 generation, help, English and Portuguese manuals and scaffold copies, template digest and regression tests. Verified that the only write-capable assessment routes either skip persistence or refuse in the sealed checkout, while normal persistence remains enabled outside it. Focused go test and go vet passed. The full strict validators were attempted but Go could not create build work directories or cache files in this read-only sandbox; the sealed bundle supplies passing build, unit, integration and e2e evidence. Surface-check reported one target, 236 results and zero findings. Recurrence-check found zero recurrent keys. The current brief lists no prior findings to account for; the round-one N1 mentioned in implementer notes is not included.\",\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assumption-integrity\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/sealed-checkout-child-evidence-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Verified that review dispatch sets POSE_SEALED_CHECKOUT to the worktree and that IsSealedCheckout resolves absolute paths and symlinks before comparing the CLI root. The Store writers use the same predicate. L1 is the disclosed residual assumption: a reviewer process that clears the environment marker can write, while dispatch’s post-run comparison still invalidates a changed checkout. I treat that as the spec’s explicit residual risk, not as an unmentioned guarantee.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-concurrency\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The change adds no goroutines, shared mutable state or asynchronous lifecycle. Persistence is decided per command invocation, and writer guards execute synchronously. No new cancellation surface is introduced; focused assessment and review-plan tests passed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-contracts\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/help-lists-every-command-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Reviewed the additive --no-persist CLI option, its help text, and the review plan’s command arguments. The three assessment commands continue to marshal the same result objects to JSON; persisted file formats are unchanged. The brief template advances to review-brief/9 for its new instruction.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-input-errors\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The new option is a boolean and introduces no unbounded input. Sealed write attempts through init, snapshot and request return an actionable refusal. Store writers return ErrSealedAssessmentWrite with --no-persist remediation. Regression coverage exercises sealed commands with --update-state and --no-persist.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-integration-impact\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/sealed-checkout-child-evidence-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Traced CLI assessment calls into guarded Store writers and the review-plan producer into the dispatched command arguments. No REST, event, MCP schema or cross-service contract changes. The live integration assessment reported three unobserved HTTP contracts unrelated to this change.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-observability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Non-persisting commands emit a stderr hint while keeping result JSON on stdout. Refused writes return a typed error with a usable remediation, and save/update-state failures retain command context.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"compatibility\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/help-lists-every-command-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Examined the CLI, review-plan arguments, help catalog, and review-brief template versioning. --no-persist is additive; absent it, assessment persistence remains enabled outside sealed checkouts. Existing assessment records and indexes keep their formats and meaning.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"correctness\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The focused `go -C pose-mcp test ./internal/cli ./internal/pose -run '\"'Assess|ReviewPlanRunsAssessments'\"'` and scoped vet passed. The regression test hashes the fixture tree around each writing assessment route, checks refusal routes and verifies normal persistence outside a sealed checkout. The full validator rerun was blocked before Go checks could execute by read-only temp/cache paths; sealed validation evidence passes.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"design-causality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-5297945ea4ddc675\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The stated failure cause is assessment commands persisting derived files into the reviewer’s sealed worktree. D1 addresses it at both layers: CLI skips writes and preserves the result output, while Store writers refuse as a last line. D2 makes review plans explicitly choose --no-persist. The design assessment observed no material structural deltas, so there are no structural facts requiring mappings.\",\n      \"mappings\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"documentation\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/help-lists-every-command-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Compared runtime flags and review-brief/9 instructions with the CLI help, POSE.md, pt-BR manual, and both scaffold copies. They describe the dispatching-engine invocation and the no-persist behavior consistently.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"operability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"A reviewer can tell that results were not persisted from the stderr hint. Direct write attempts explain that the checkout is sealed and identify --no-persist as the remediation; command-level failures identify the writer or update-state operation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"requirements\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"R1 is covered by no-persist output/no-write tests; R2 by unchanged-tree and refusal tests; R3 by reviewToolArgs tests; R4 by the before/after tree digest regression; and R5 by the review-brief/9 text and current-brief regression. The focused test command passed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"scope\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-5297945ea4ddc675\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The implementation covers the specified pose-mcp CLI, Store writers, planned assessment arguments and operational documentation. It does not change assessment scoring or data formats. The design assessment reported no material structural deltas, and surface-check found one delivery target with zero findings.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"security\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/adversarial-corpus-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The only new environmental authority is the dispatch-provided checkout path; matching canonicalizes absolute and symlink paths. Every assessment Store writer is guarded, while the CLI prevents capability-artifact writes. No new dependency, secret, external execution authority or user-controlled output path is introduced. The marker-clearing residual is disclosed as L1.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"solution-proportionality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-5297945ea4ddc675\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The layered policy is the smallest sufficient design for both required behaviors: a CLI-only check would leave other Store callers able to write, while a Store-only refusal would make planned review commands fail instead of returning results. Explicit plan flags also work when commands are copied into another checkout. No new schema or cache is added. The choice would need revisiting if dispatch stopped setting the marker or new writers bypassed the guard; post-run checkout comparison and the writer regression test address those cases.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"artifact-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:\"$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\" artifact-check --spec pose-assess-leaves-sealed-checkouts-alone --strict\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran through the dispatching engine and exited 0. It emitted 990 provenance warnings and resolved the indexed range through 7f3cf042, later than the supplied brief range ending at 3df50607, so I do not treat that output as scoped attribution proof.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-design\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-5297945ea4ddc675\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran the JSON design assessment; it observed the 17-file subject and no material deltas.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-discover\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:\"$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\" assess discover --no-persist --component pose-mcp\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran successfully, printed the not-persisted hint and returned the component result.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-integrate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:\"$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\" assess integrate --no-persist\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran successfully and printed the not-persisted hint. It reported three unobserved HTTP contracts outside this change’s subject.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-tech-debt\",\n      \"disposition\": \"failed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:\"$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\" assess tech-debt --no-persist\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The command exited 0 and did not persist, but reported an incomplete scan because two unrelated specs have unknown scope. A manual scan of the changed implementation found no new actionable debt marker.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"closeout-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:\"$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\" closeout-check spec:pose-assess-leaves-sealed-checkouts-alone\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Deferred because this completion gate requires a recorded review conclusion, and this task prohibits recording an attestation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"review-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:\"$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\" review-check spec:pose-assess-leaves-sealed-checkouts-alone\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Deferred because it requires a completed review attestation, which this task prohibits recording.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"suggest-review\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:\"$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\" suggest review --path pose-mcp\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran successfully and selected Backend Go, security and documentation-style rules; I read and applied those rules.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"surface-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"reachability:pose-mcp/go/spec-surface-reachability\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran successfully: one target, 236 results and zero findings.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"build:pose-mcp/go/build\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The strict validation command was attempted, but its Go build/test steps could not create work directories or cache files in the read-only sandbox. The sealed bundle’s build, e2e, integration and unit evidence passes, and the focused tests/vet passed independently.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The module strict validation command was attempted and hit the same read-only Go work/cache limitation. The sealed pose-mcp build, e2e, integration and unit evidence passes; focused assessment tests and vet passed independently.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\nPOSE_DRAFT_EOF'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
